data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/probe-0.log\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/probe-0.process.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/probe-0.prompt.txt\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/probe-0.response.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T164110-7313e7d0/probe-0.stdin.txt\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/controller-tests.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/controller-tests.log\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/controller-tests.process.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/manifest.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/previous-controller-tests.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/probe-0.log\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/probe-0.process.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/probe-0.prompt.txt\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/probe-0.response.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/probe-0.stdin.txt\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/controller-tests.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/controller-tests.log\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/controller-tests.process.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/manifest.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/previous-controller-tests.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/state.json\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"reasoning\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"**Planning JSON output**\\\\n\\\\nI need to work efficiently—it’s about 10 minutes I have. It seems like I should focus on just creating the final JSON. My commentary in JSON seems like a reasonable compromise. I have to inspect the targeted files, but there's no known Git record. I want to use commands without separating echoes because that can complicate things. Minor separators will do the trick. Batch processing should be the way to go!\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_5\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_5\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# AccDSL project instructions\\\\n\\\\n## Mission entry point\\\\n\\\\nBefore substantive work in this project, read:\\\\n\\\\n1. [Mission control](MISSION_CONTROL.md).\\\\n2. [Requirements and acceptance evidence](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\\\\n3. [Current checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md).\\\\n4. The gap records relevant to the task:\\\\n   [initial audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and\\\\n   [expanded mission audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\\\\n5. For the authorised master-program work, read the\\\\n   [master checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md), executable\\\\n   phase catalog and current `data/accounting-master/next-plan.md`. The older\\\\n   corpus checkpoint remains historical evidence; current phase execution is\\\\n   recorded by the master without rewriting frozen release hashes.\\\\n\\\\nThe mission preserves the user's goals across sessions. Current user directions\\\\nand higher-priority instructions still control. Local documents must not be\\\\nused to request fresh permission for work already authorised by the user.\\\\n\\\\n## Working rules\\\\n\\\\n- Identify the MC requirements addressed by each nontrivial plan or work unit.\\\\n  Audit the plan before implementation, experiments or long diagnostics.\\\\n- Preserve the full goals while staging execution. A small financing demo,\\\\n  clean PDF build or six populated research ledgers cannot close requirements\\\\n  for whole-company representation, research quality or implementation detail.\\\\n- Distinguish direct user requirements, policy requirements and derived\\\\n  engineering choices. Do not silently convert a convenient library, model\\\\n  assumption or stage boundary into an immutable product requirement.\\\\n- Keep source evidence, interpretations, assumptions, joint history families\\\\n  and scenario-specific results separate and traceable. Preserve unknowns;\\\\n  do not invent facts, probabilities, accounting compliance or completeness.\\\\n- Close gaps with the specified evidence, and update the requirements register\\\\n  and checkpoint after meaningful changes. Add newly discovered gaps rather\\\\n  than treating the current list as exhaustive.\\\\n- Follow the applicable policies under\\\\n  `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`. Preserve unrelated work and the\\\\n  original paper collection. The existing `.git` marker is not a usable\\\\n  repository; do not initialise or commit merely to create provenance.\\\\n- Keep operational mission/checklist material out of the reader-facing\\\\n  scholarly narrative unless it serves a real implementation-reference purpose.\\\\n- Apply MC35, the user's internal-preparation-before-paid-review requirement.\\\\n  Finish feasible source research, facts, calculations, software checks and\\\\n  document repairs before referring a specific question to a professional.\\\\n  Supply a proposed answer, exact sources, competing interpretation and checked\\\\n  consequences. Keep unfinished internal work on the internal queue; “human\\\\n  review pending” is an acceptance status, not a reason to stop that work.\\\\n  Ordinary reader feedback need not be purchased from an accounting firm.\\\\n  No professional engagement, outreach or fees are authorised by this policy.\\\\n  See `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md` and the current checkpoint.\\\\n\\\\nThe current manuscript is specification-incomplete. Read the checkpoint and\\\\nrequirements before resuming from an older note that says only final review\\\\nremains. This file authorises no autonomous background campaign or external\\\\npublication; it directs work undertaken under the user's active instructions.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'find data/accounting-master/deliverables/P00 data/accounting-master/deliverables/P01 -maxdepth 2 -type f -print'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'find data/accounting-master/deliverables/P00 data/accounting-master/deliverables/P01 -maxdepth 2 -type f -print'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"find: ‘data/accounting-master/deliverables/P00’: No such file or directory\\\\nfind: ‘data/accounting-master/deliverables/P01’: No such file or directory\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"failed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_7\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n -C 3 'MC02|MC04|MC10|MC20|MC23|MC24|G2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b|G12\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b|G15\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_7\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n -C 3 'MC02|MC04|MC10|MC20|MC23|MC24|G2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b|G12\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b|G15\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-53-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-54-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-55-| MC01 | Account for complete annual, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:56:| MC02 | Preserve numeric meaning: entities, perimeter, concept, dimensions, currency, units, scale, sign, basis and precision. U1, D. | Complete context/value types and compatibility rules, with valid/invalid examples and faithful rendering of the original disclosed amounts. | Specified in Chs. 3, 7 and Core 0 Context/Domain/Posting records, including display and rounding metadata. Schema, source scales and rounded-debt calculations have bounded checks; bounded debt context/type/source-binding checks and schema-valid rejection cases now pass. General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:57:| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:58:| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:61:| MC07 | Align differing company labels and overlapping dimensions without equating unlike measurements or double counting. U1, D. | Specify concept/mapping relationships, applicability and aggregation rules; demonstrate company extensions and product/geography totals over the same population. | Specified mapping composition, applicability and partition obligations in Ch. 3/Core 0. The product/channel overlap counterexample is checked; general company-extension/mapping validation awaits implementation. G2, G12. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-62-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-63-## M2 — Histories, interpretation and uncertainty\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-64-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-65-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-66-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:67:| MC08 | Preserve jointly consistent discrete alternatives and continuous unknowns across accounts, notes and dates. U2, D. | Define history-family and choice/constraint semantics; provide cases preserving linked alternatives and rejecting incompatible combinations without independent account-by-account selection. | Specified shared symbols, choices and joint formulas in Chs. 2, 6–8. Exact reference checks retain fixed/floating histories, reject incompatible debt and reject incompatible marginal extrema. General reconstruction implementation remains pending. G1, G2, G15. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-68-| MC09 | Construct historical families through a specified method, with honest scope and search completeness. U2, U3, D. | Define candidate templates, model-scope records, instantiation and constraint lowering, feasible/infeasible/unknown results, truncation and coverage evidence. | Specified finite template/slot construction and coverage rules in Ch. 6/Core 0. Northstar bridges are solved and checked within the declared scope; completeness concerns that model only. A compiler for arbitrary supported template registries remains pending. G1, G3. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:69:| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-70-| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:71:| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-72-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-73-## M3 — Economic events, journals and forecasts\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-74-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-75-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-76-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:77:| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-78-| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-79-| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-80-| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-81-| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:82:| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-83-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-84-## M4 — Standards, sectors and company variation\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-85-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-86-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-87-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-88-| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:89:| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-90-| MC21 | Represent banks' liabilities, assets, deposits, capital and regulatory/economic constraints. U1, U2. | Define core bank structural records now and operation-level later methods for funding, credit, liquidity and capital, including accounting/prudential reconciliation and an appropriate worked case. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 specifies bank origination, transfer, interest, allowance, cash funding and default; exact fixture balances and capital reconciliation pass. Prudential weights are illustrative; full allowance lifecycle, IFRS 9/CECL and jurisdictional capital rules remain open. G7, G8. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-91-| MC22 | Represent insurers' contract groups, claims, service/finance components, assets and reinsurance. U1, U2. | Define cohort/group state and movements, declared measurement approaches and interfaces, reinsurance links and a complete structural/roll-forward example; expand actuarial/accounting support. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` give a complete short-duration PAA gross/reinsurance roll-forward and chain-ladder point calculation. Selected AASB 17 paragraphs and Mack technical sections inspected. Separate treaty PAA eligibility and recognition timing are explicit in Version 1.2; journal counterexamples vary transferred risk and non-performance independently. General measurement, transition, variable fees and uncertainty/RA estimation remain open. G7, G8, G16. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-92-\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-94-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-95-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-96-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:97:| MC23 | Explain the DSL's role and tradeoffs against credible alternatives, including typed ordinary code, XBRL, ledgers, rule languages and probabilistic tools. U1, U3, P. | Tie each claimed benefit to the same concrete tasks and shared semantic requirements; state costs and a fair authoring comparison protocol. Keep empirical superiority unclaimed until evaluated. | Specified shared-IR comparison and identical authoring tasks in Chs. 5, 11/Core 0; limited syntax/literal equivalence checked. Participant study, full frontend equivalence and any superiority claim remain unevaluated. G2, G9. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:98:| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:99:| MC25 | Specify APIs, adapters, storage, versioning, identity and deterministic recovery. U3, P, D. | Define complete arguments/results, state ownership, migration semantics, evidence/model/run identity, event idempotency, random-stream allocation and replay requirements with examples. | Specified APIs, ownership, canonical identity, migration/replay and stream keying in Ch. 10/Core 0; concrete adapter exchanges included. Reference identity, replay/conflict, stream and bounded frozen-export integrity checks pass; transactional storage, migrations and non-Z3 adapters remain unimplemented. G2, G9, G18. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-100-| MC26 | Specify supported numerical/solver operations and their limits. U3, P, D. | Define formula fragments, reformulations, exact/approximate monetary treatment, rounding, strict-domain bounds, infeasibility/conflict evidence, timeout and resource behaviour. | Specified rational-linear/finite-choice scope, amount reformulation, quantisation distinctions and typed unknowns in Ch. 6/Core 0. Z3 checks 4.975 attained and 7.035 unattained and concrete histories. Nonlinear solvers and a production rounding/optimization layer remain pending. G3, G10. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:101:| MC27 | Specify analyst/LLM review and correction as a traceable local workflow. U1, U3, D. | Define proposal, acceptance, alternative, rejection and supersession actions, with evidence requirements, consistency checks and derived-result invalidation; show an actual conflict-resolution example. | Specified Propose/Accept/AcceptAlternative/Reject/Supersede actions, examples and dependency invalidation in Ch. 10/Core 0. The transitive invalidation oracle passes; a complete analyst UI/workflow and human adjudication remain pending. G2, G17. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-102-| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-103-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-104-## M6 — Literature, sources and reusable software\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-113-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-114-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-115-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:116:| MC32 | Deliver a detailed, readable LaTeX/PDF document that governs the intended implementation. U3, P. | Explain the whole problem, justify chosen methods, stage mathematical prerequisites, define supported behaviour and disclose open scope; connect derivations and sources to complete examples and interfaces. Preserve mathematical/source fidelity during revisions and inspect the rendered result. | Revised Version 1.2 candidate, 11 chapters plus two appendices, full cases and supporting normative files. Build, rendered inspection and baseline-preservation review are recorded in `review/author-review.md`. Human comprehension, domain review and independent implementability acceptance remain pending. G1, G2, G4, G5, G7, G10. |\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-117-\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-118-## M8 — Validation, completion and sustained direction\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-119-\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_8\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg --files -g '*borrowing*' -g '*core*' -g '*schema*' -g '*registry*' -g '*semantic*' -g 'test_accounting_p0*.py' -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*README*' -g '*grammar*' -g '*.acc' -g 'pyproject.toml' -g 'requirements*.txt'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_8\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg --files -g '*borrowing*' -g '*core*' -g '*schema*' -g '*registry*' -g '*semantic*' -g 'test_accounting_p0*.py' -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*README*' -g '*grammar*' -g '*.acc' -g 'pyproject.toml' -g 'requirements*.txt'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"scripts/__pycache__/build_demo_registry.cpython-311.pyc\\\\nscripts/__pycache__/core_semantics.cpython-311.pyc\\\\nscripts/build_core_contract.py\\\\nscripts/check_core_contract.py\\\\nscripts/core_semantics.py\\\\nscripts/check_semantic_preparation.py\\\\nscripts/build_demo_registry.py\\\\nscripts/accounting_master_response.schema.json\\\\ndocs/design/README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/duckdb_duckdb-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/openfisca_openfisca-core-LICENSE\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/Z3Prover_z3-README-CMake.md\\\\ndocs/design/fixtures/borrowings.json\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/Z3Prover_z3-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/openfisca_openfisca-core-contents.json\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/pymc-devs_pymc-README.rst\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/ledger_ledger-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/openfisca_openfisca-core-openfisca_core_variables_variable.py\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/openfisca_openfisca-core-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/openfisca_openfisca-core-meta.json\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/microsoft_table-transformer-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/pyro-ppl_pyro-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/docling-project_docling-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/stan-dev_stan-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/beancount_beancount-README.rst\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/Arelle_Arelle-README.md\\\\nAGENTS.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/hledgerorg_hledger-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-repair-2026-10-02/docs/design/README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/actusfrf_actus-techspecs-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/beancount_beancount-beancount_core_data.py\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/CatalaLang_catala-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/lballabio_QuantLib-README.md\\\\ndocs/design/research/software/ledger_ledger-README-snapshot.md\\\\ndocs/design/fixtures/core-ir-structure.json\\\\ndocs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\\\\ndocs/design/fixtures/core-demo-registry.json\\\\ndocs/design/fixtures/core-ir-demo.json\\\\ndocs/design/review/semantic-preparation-checks.json\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-repair-2026-10-02/AGENTS.md\\\\ndocs/design/spec/core-0.lark\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-20261002/P00/semantic-preparation-checks.json\\\\ndocs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/check_core_contract.py.outcome.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-20261002/P00/core-contract-checks.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-20261002/P00/check_semantic_preparation.py.log\\\\ndocs/papers/README.md\\\\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/check_semantic_preparation.py.log\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/check_core_contract.py.log\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/AGENTS.md\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/scripts/build_core_contract.py\\\\ndata/financial-report-benchmark/README.md\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/check_semantic_preparation.py.outcome.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/core-contract-checks.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/semantic-preparation-checks.json\\\\ndocs/design/review/core-contract-checks.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-repair-20261002/P00/semantic-preparation-checks.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-repair-20261002/P00/core-contract-checks.json\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-repair-20261002/P00/check_semantic_preparation.py.log\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-repair-20261002/P00/check_core_contract.py.log\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/scripts/check_core_contract.py\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-20261002/P00/check_core_contract.py.log\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/README.md\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/spec/core-0.lark\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/fixtures/borrowings.json\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/fixtures/core-ir-structure.json\\\\ndata/financial-report-benchmark/annotation-record.schema.json\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/fixtures/core-ir-demo.json\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_9\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"reasoning\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"**Narrowing historical focus**\\\\n\\\\nI need to concentrate on more specific local instructions rather than broad historical contexts. So, it’s important to read relevant contracts and codes to understand the mission checkpoints properly. I wonder how missing the details could impact the mission. I'll have to make sure I'm properly aligned with these instructions and clearly comprehend my focus. This approach will help me stay on track and avoid any misinterpretations.\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat scripts/core_semantics.py'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat scripts/core_semantics.py'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Bounded semantic validator for the authored debt IR; no general compiler.\\\\n\\\\nRejects unsupported populated sections and operations explicitly. External\\\\nexports are frozen data, never executable code or network-loaded dependencies.\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom datetime import date, datetime\\\\nfrom fractions import Fraction\\\\nimport hashlib\\\\nimport json\\\\nimport re\\\\n\\\\nimport jsonschema\\\\n\\\\nfrom build_demo_registry import build as expected_registry, canonical\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass Invalid(Exception):\\\\n    def __init__(self, code, location, detail):\\\\n        self.code, self.location, self.detail = code, location, detail\\\\n        super().__init__(f'{code} at {location}: {detail}')\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef require(condition, code, location, detail):\\\\n    if not condition:\\\\n        raise Invalid(code, location, detail)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef strict_json(text):\\\\n    def pairs(items):\\\\n        out = {}\\\\n        for key, value in items:\\\\n            require(key not in out, 'DuplicateJSONKey', key, 'Duplicate keys lose source information')\\\\n            out[key] = value\\\\n        return out\\\\n    def invalid_constant(value):\\\\n        raise Invalid('InvalidJSONNumber', value, 'Non-finite numbers are not JSON')\\\\n    return json.loads(text, object_pairs_hook=pairs, parse_constant=invalid_constant)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef rational(value, location):\\\\n    n, d = int(value['n']), int(value['d'])\\\\n    require(d > 0, 'InvalidRational', location, 'Positive denominator required')\\\\n    q = Fraction(n, d)\\\\n    require((str(q.numerator), str(q.denominator)) == (value['n'], value['d']),\\\\n            'NoncanonicalRational', location, 'Use reduced terms and zero 0/1')\\\\n    return q\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef iso_date(value, location):\\\\n    try:\\\\n        result = date.fromisoformat(value)\\\\n        require(result.isoformat() == value, 'InvalidDate', location, 'Use YYYY-MM-DD')\\\\n        return result\\\\n    except ValueError as exc:\\\\n        raise Invalid('InvalidDate', location, str(exc)) from exc\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef instant(value, location):\\\\n    try:\\\\n        t = datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace('Z', '+00:00'))\\\\n        require(t.tzinfo is not None, 'MissingTimezone', location, 'Timestamp requires timezone')\\\\n        return t\\\\n    except ValueError as exc:\\\\n        raise Invalid('InvalidTimestamp', location, str(exc)) from exc\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nSUPPORTED = {'models', 'contexts', 'sourceSpans', 'documents', 'observations',\\\\n             'entities', 'books', 'accounts', 'symbols', 'expressions', 'constraints',\\\\n             'assumptions', 'alternatives', 'contracts', 'states', 'packages',\\\\n             'scenarios', 'reviewDecisions', 'evidenceViews', 'modelScopes',\\\\n             'historyFamilies', 'reportMappings'}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass Validator:\\\\n    def __init__(self, document, registry, schema, root):\\\\n        try:\\\\n            jsonschema.Draft202012Validator(schema).validate(document)\\\\n        except jsonschema.ValidationError as exc:\\\\n            raise Invalid('StructuralError', '/'.join(map(str, exc.path)), exc.message) from exc\\\\n        self.doc, self.root, self.nodes, self.kinds = document, root, {}, {}\\\\n        self.external, self.values, self.inferred = {}, {}, {}\\\\n        for section, rows in document.items():\\\\n            if section == 'schema_version':\\\\n                continue\\\\n            require(not rows or section in SUPPORTED, 'UnsupportedSection', section,\\\\n                    'This preparation checker does not validate this populated section')\\\\n            for row in rows:\\\\n                identifier = row['id']\\\\n                require(identifier not in self.nodes, 'DuplicateID', identifier, 'IDs are globally unique')\\\\n                self.nodes[identifier], self.kinds[identifier] = row, section\\\\n        expected = {r['id']: r for r in expected_registry()['records']}\\\\n        require(isinstance(registry, dict) and registry.get('version') == '1' and\\\\n                registry.get('profile') == 'authored-debt-example' and\\\\n                isinstance(registry.get('records'), list), 'UnsupportedRegistry', 'registry',\\\\n                'Expected the versioned authored debt export set')\\\\n        for row in registry['records']:\\\\n            require(isinstance(row, dict) and set(row) == {'id', 'kind', 'artifact', 'sha256', 'pointer', 'value'},\\\\n                    'RegistryShape', 'registry', 'Export has missing or unknown fields')\\\\n            identifier = row['id']\\\\n            require(isinstance(identifier, str) and identifier in expected, 'UnsupportedRegistry', str(identifier),\\\\n                    'Export outside this fixed demonstration profile')\\\\n            template = expected[identifier]\\\\n            require(all(row[k] == template[k] for k in ['kind', 'artifact', 'pointer', 'value']),\\\\n                    'RegistryBinding', identifier, 'Export kind, location or built-in definition differs from this profile')\\\\n            require(identifier not in self.external and identifier not in self.nodes,\\\\n                    'DuplicateID', identifier, 'External and internal exports cannot collide')\\\\n            if row['artifact'] is None:\\\\n                value = row['value']\\\\n                digest = hashlib.sha256(canonical(value)).hexdigest()\\\\n            else:\\\\n                path = (root / row['artifact']).resolve()\\\\n                require(path.is_relative_to(root.resolve()) and path.is_file(),\\\\n                        'MissingArtifact', identifier, 'Expected a retained project file')\\\\n                digest = hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\\\n                value = strict_json(path.read_text())\\\\n                try:\\\\n                    for part in row['pointer'].split('/')[1:]:\\\\n                        part = part.replace('~1', '/').replace('~0', '~')\\\\n                        value = value[int(part)] if isinstance(value, list) else value[part]\\\\n                except (KeyError, ValueError, IndexError, TypeError) as exc:\\\\n                    raise Invalid('MissingExport', identifier, row['pointer']) from exc\\\\n            require(digest == row['sha256'], 'StaleArtifact', identifier, 'Frozen export content differs')\\\\n            self.external[identifier] = row['kind']\\\\n            self.values[identifier] = value\\\\n        require(set(self.external) == set(expected), 'MissingExport', 'registry', 'Incomplete demonstration export set')\\\\n\\\\n    def ref(self, identifier, kinds=None):\\\\n        kind = self.kinds.get(identifier, self.external.get(identifier))\\\\n        require(kind is not None, 'UnknownReference', identifier, 'No frozen export')\\\\n        require(kinds is None or kind in kinds, 'ReferenceKind', identifier, f'Expected {kinds}, got {kind}')\\\\n        return self.nodes.get(identifier, self.values.get(identifier))\\\\n\\\\n    def refs(self, identifiers, kinds=None):\\\\n        require(len(identifiers) == len(set(identifiers)), 'DuplicateReference', str(identifiers), 'Set-valued reference list')\\\\n        return [self.ref(i, kinds) for i in identifiers]\\\\n\\\\n    def time(self, t, where):\\\\n        start = iso_date(t['start'], where)\\\\n        self.ref(t['calendar'], {'Calendar'})\\\\n        if t['kind'] == 'instant':\\\\n            require(t['end_exclusive'] is None, 'InvalidPeriod', where, 'Instant has no end')\\\\n        else:\\\\n            require(t['end_exclusive'] is not None and iso_date(t['end_exclusive'], where) > start,\\\\n                    'InvalidPeriod', where, 'Interval must have a later exclusive end')\\\\n\\\\n    def domain(self, d, where):\\\\n        low = rational(d['lower'], where) if d['lower'] is not None else None\\\\n        high = rational(d['upper'], where) if d['upper'] is not None else None\\\\n        require(low is not None or not d['lower_closed'], 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Unbounded endpoint cannot be closed')\\\\n        require(high is not None or not d['upper_closed'], 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Unbounded endpoint cannot be closed')\\\\n        if d['kind'] == 'missing':\\\\n            require(low is high is None and not d['values'] and d['missing_reason'] is not None,\\\\n                    'InvalidDomain', where, 'Missingness cannot contain a value')\\\\n        else:\\\\n            require(d['missing_reason'] is None, 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Nonmissing domain has no missing reason')\\\\n            if d['kind'] == 'finite':\\\\n                require(low is high is None and bool(d['values']), 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Finite domain needs values only')\\\\n                self.refs(d['values'], {'expressions'})\\\\n            else:\\\\n                require(not d['values'], 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Numeric interval has no finite-value payload')\\\\n                require(low is None or high is None or low < high or\\\\n                        (low == high and d['lower_closed'] and d['upper_closed']),\\\\n                        'InvalidDomain', where, 'Empty/reversed interval')\\\\n                if d['kind'] == 'exact':\\\\n                    require(low is not None and low == high and d['lower_closed'] and d['upper_closed'],\\\\n                            'InvalidDomain', where, 'Exact domain requires equal closed finite bounds')\\\\n        return low, high\\\\n\\\\n    def merge_context(self, contexts, where):\\\\n        ids = [c for c in contexts if c is not None]\\\\n        if not ids:\\\\n            return None\\\\n        keys = ['entity', 'perimeter', 'basis', 'measurement', 'time', 'unit', 'currency', 'dimensions']\\\\n        first = self.ref(ids[0], {'contexts'})\\\\n        for identifier in ids[1:]:\\\\n            other = self.ref(identifier, {'contexts'})\\\\n            require(all(first[k] == other[k] for k in keys), 'ContextMismatch', where,\\\\n                    'Contexts require an explicit compatible mapping')\\\\n        return ids[0]\\\\n\\\\n    def expression(self, identifier, active=()):\\\\n        require(identifier not in active, 'ExpressionCycle', identifier, 'Cyclic expression dependency')\\\\n        if identifier in self.inferred:\\\\n            return self.inferred[identifier]\\\\n        e = self.ref(identifier, {'expressions'})\\\\n        op, target = e['op'], e['target']\\\\n        args = [self.expression(a, active + (identifier,)) for a in e['args']]\\\\n        types = [t for t, _ in args]\\\\n        context = self.merge_context([c for _, c in args], identifier)\\\\n        numeric = lambda t: t in {'Real', 'Int', 'YearFraction', 'Rate<annual_simple>'} or re.fullmatch(r'Money<[A-Z]{3}>', t) is not None\\\\n        require(not e['field_names'], 'UnsupportedExpression', identifier, 'Records/field selection not in this profile')\\\\n        if op == 'literal':\\\\n            require(not args and target is None and ((e['rational'] is None) != (e['text'] is None)),\\\\n                    'ExpressionPayload', identifier, 'One literal payload and no operands/target')\\\\n            result = e['type']\\\\n            if e['rational'] is not None:\\\\n                q = rational(e['rational'], identifier)\\\\n                require(numeric(result), 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Numeric literal has a numeric type')\\\\n                require(result != 'Int' or q.denominator == 1, 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Fractional integer')\\\\n            elif result == 'SourceRef':\\\\n                self.ref(e['text'], {'SourceRef'})\\\\n            elif result == 'Date':\\\\n                iso_date(e['text'], identifier)\\\\n            else:\\\\n                require(result == 'String' or (result == 'Bool' and e['text'] in {'true', 'false'}),\\\\n                        'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Invalid text literal type')\\\\n            context = e['context']\\\\n        else:\\\\n            require(e['rational'] is None and e['text'] is None, 'ExpressionPayload', identifier, 'Unused literal payload')\\\\n            if op == 'ref':\\\\n                require(not args, 'ArityMismatch', identifier, 'Reference takes no operands')\\\\n                r = self.ref(target, {'symbols', 'observations', 'expressions'})\\\\n                if self.kinds[target] == 'observations':\\\\n                    c = self.ref(r['context'], {'contexts'})\\\\n                    result, context = f'Observation<Money<{c[\\\\\\\"currency\\\\\\\"]}>>', r['context']\\\\n                elif self.kinds[target] == 'symbols':\\\\n                    result, context = r['type'], r['context']\\\\n                else:\\\\n                    result, context = self.expression(target, active + (identifier,))\\\\n            elif op == 'call':\\\\n                self.ref(target, {'Builtin'})\\\\n                require(len(args) == 1, 'ArityMismatch', identifier, 'Supported calls take one argument')\\\\n                if target == 'builtin:value@1':\\\\n                    require(types[0].startswith('Observation<') and types[0].endswith('>'),\\\\n                            'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'value requires an Observation')\\\\n                    result = types[0][12:-1]\\\\n                elif target == 'builtin:constant@1':\\\\n                    result = f'Driver<{types[0]}>'\\\\n                else:\\\\n                    raise Invalid('UnsupportedExpression', identifier, 'Builtin not implemented in this checker')\\\\n            else:\\\\n                require(target is None, 'ExpressionPayload', identifier, 'Operator cannot have target')\\\\n                arity = 1 if op in {'negate', 'not'} else 2\\\\n                require(len(args) == arity, 'ArityMismatch', identifier, 'Wrong operator argument count')\\\\n                if op in {'not', 'and', 'or'}:\\\\n                    require(all(t == 'Bool' for t in types), 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Boolean operands required')\\\\n                    result = 'Bool'\\\\n                elif op in {'eq', 'ne', 'lt', 'le', 'gt', 'ge', 'add', 'subtract'}:\\\\n                    require(types[0] == types[1] and (op in {'eq', 'ne'} or numeric(types[0])),\\\\n                            'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Compatible operand types required')\\\\n                    result = types[0] if op in {'add', 'subtract'} else 'Bool'\\\\n                elif op == 'negate':\\\\n                    require(numeric(types[0]), 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Numeric negation required')\\\\n                    result = types[0]\\\\n                else:\\\\n                    raise Invalid('UnsupportedExpression', identifier, op)\\\\n        if context is not None:\\\\n            c = self.ref(context, {'contexts'})\\\\n            m = re.fullmatch(r'Money<([A-Z]{3})>', result)\\\\n            require(not m or c['currency'] == m[1], 'ContextMismatch', identifier, 'Money/context currency mismatch')\\\\n        require((result, context) == (e['type'], e['context']), 'TypeMismatch', identifier,\\\\n                f'Declared {(e[\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\"], e[\\\\\\\"context\\\\\\\"])} but inferred {(result, context)}')\\\\n        self.inferred[identifier] = result, context\\\\n        return result, context\\\\n\\\\n    def bounds(self, identifier):\\\\n        e = self.ref(identifier, {'expressions'})\\\\n        if e['op'] == 'literal' and e['rational'] is not None:\\\\n            q = rational(e['rational'], identifier)\\\\n            return q, q\\\\n        if e['op'] == 'ref' and self.kinds.get(e['target']) in {'observations', 'symbols'}:\\\\n            return self.domain(self.nodes[e['target']]['domain'], identifier)\\\\n        if e['op'] == 'call' and e['target'] in {'builtin:value@1', 'builtin:constant@1'}:\\\\n            return self.bounds(e['args'][0])\\\\n        raise Invalid('UnprovedContractBound', identifier, 'Bound computation unsupported in this profile')\\\\n\\\\n    def assumption(self, expression, scope):\\\\n        require(any(a['expression'] == expression and a['scope'] == scope for a in self.doc['assumptions']),\\\\n                'MissingAssumption', scope + ':' + expression, 'Conditional input lacks assumption provenance')\\\\n\\\\n    def validate(self):\\\\n        d = self.doc\\\\n        reading = self.values['fixture:synthetic-note-7/exact-reading']\\\\n        package_data = self.values['fixture:demo-debt-package.json']\\\\n        horizon = self.values['DemoCalendar@1']['one_year']\\\\n        for key in ['models', 'contexts', 'documents', 'observations', 'entities', 'books', 'accounts',\\\\n                    'symbols', 'contracts', 'states', 'packages', 'scenarios', 'reviewDecisions',\\\\n                    'evidenceViews', 'modelScopes', 'historyFamilies', 'reportMappings']:\\\\n            require(bool(d[key]), 'IncompleteProfile', key, 'Required part of the authored debt example')\\\\n        for entity in d['entities']:\\\\n            require(re.fullmatch(r'[A-Z]{3}', entity['functional_currency']) is not None,\\\\n                    'InvalidCurrency', entity['id'], 'Three uppercase currency letters required')\\\\n        for c in d['contexts']:\\\\n            self.ref(c['entity'], {'entities'}); self.time(c['time'], c['id'])\\\\n            require(c['currency'] is not None and c['unit'] == c['currency'], 'ContextMismatch', c['id'], 'Monetary profile requires currency/unit agreement')\\\\n            require(len({x['axis'] for x in c['dimensions']}) == len(c['dimensions']), 'DuplicateDimension', c['id'], 'One member per axis')\\\\n            require(not c['dimensions'] and c['taxonomy_version'] is None, 'UnsupportedContext', c['id'],\\\\n                    'Taxonomy and dimensional mappings are outside this profile')\\\\n        for doc in d['documents']:\\\\n            instant(doc['available'], doc['id']); instant(doc['ingested'], doc['id'])\\\\n            require(doc['uri'] == 'fixture:demo-debt-package.json#registry/synthetic-note-7', 'UnsupportedSource', doc['id'], 'Only frozen synthetic source is handled')\\\\n            literal = self.values['fixture:synthetic-note-7/exact-reading']['literal']\\\\n            require(doc['sha256'] == hashlib.sha256(literal.encode()).hexdigest(), 'SourceDigestMismatch', doc['id'], 'Synthetic document hashes its literal bytes')\\\\n        for s in d['sourceSpans']:\\\\n            self.ref(s['document'], {'documents'})\\\\n            require(s['literal'] == self.values['fixture:synthetic-note-7/exact-reading']['literal'], 'SourceLiteralMismatch', s['id'], 'Source span differs from frozen reading')\\\\n            require(s['locator'] == 'fixture:registry/synthetic-note-7/literal' and s['extraction'].strip(),\\\\n                    'SourceLocatorMismatch', s['id'], 'Locator and extractor must identify the retained literal')\\\\n        for review in d['reviewDecisions']:\\\\n            self.refs(review['reading_ids'], {'Reading'}); self.refs(review['evidence'], {'sourceSpans'})\\\\n            self.ref(review['prior_view'], {'EvidenceView', 'evidenceViews'}); self.ref(review['new_view'], {'evidenceViews'})\\\\n            instant(review['date'], review['id'])\\\\n            require(review['reviewer'].strip() and review['reason'].strip(), 'MissingReviewReason', review['id'], 'Reviewer and rationale required')\\\\n            require(review['action'] == 'Accept' and not review['invalidated_descendants'],\\\\n                    'UnsupportedReview', review['id'], 'This profile checks initial acceptance, not revision transitions')\\\\n        for o in d['observations']:\\\\n            self.ref(o['context'], {'contexts'}); self.domain(o['domain'], o['id'])\\\\n            self.refs(o['source_spans'], {'sourceSpans'}); self.ref(o['reading'], {'Reading'})\\\\n            r = self.ref(o['review_decision'], {'reviewDecisions'})\\\\n            require(r['action'] == 'Accept' and o['reading'] in r['reading_ids'], 'ObservationNotAccepted', o['id'], 'This profile requires accepted, matching readings')\\\\n            require(not o['supersedes'], 'UnsupportedHistory', o['id'], 'Revision graph checked separately, not in this profile')\\\\n            require(bool(o['source_spans']) and set(o['source_spans']) <= set(r['evidence']),\\\\n                    'AdmissionEvidence', o['id'], 'Acceptance must retain the observation source')\\\\n            c = self.ref(o['context'], {'contexts'})\\\\n            require(all(c[k] == reading[k] for k in ['entity', 'perimeter', 'basis', 'concept', 'currency'])\\\\n                    and c['time']['kind'] == 'instant' and c['time']['start'] == reading['instant']\\\\n                    and c['measurement'] == 'principal', 'ReadingContextMismatch', o['id'],\\\\n                    'Admitted context differs from the frozen authored reading')\\\\n            require(o['domain']['kind'] == 'exact' and self.domain(o['domain'], o['id']) ==\\\\n                    (rational(reading['amount'], o['id']),) * 2, 'ReadingValueMismatch', o['id'],\\\\n                    'Admitted value differs from the frozen authored reading')\\\\n        for v in d['evidenceViews']:\\\\n            require(v['mode'] == 'ExplicitSelection' and not v['conflict_sets'] and not v['transforms'], 'UnsupportedView', v['id'], 'Only explicit nonconflicting fixture views')\\\\n            docs = self.refs(v['documents'], {'documents'}); self.refs(v['decisions'], {'reviewDecisions'})\\\\n            cutoff = instant(v['cutoff'], v['id'])\\\\n            system_cutoff = instant(v['system_as_of'], v['id']) if v['system_as_of'] is not None else None\\\\n            for review in self.refs(v['decisions'], {'reviewDecisions'}):\\\\n                require(review['new_view'] == v['id'], 'ViewMembership', review['id'], 'Decision must produce the selected view')\\\\n                require(system_cutoff is None or instant(review['date'], review['id']) <= system_cutoff,\\\\n                        'FutureReview', review['id'], 'Decision did not yet exist at the system cutoff')\\\\n            for doc in docs:\\\\n                require(instant(doc['available'], doc['id']) <= cutoff, 'FutureEvidence', doc['id'], 'Source unavailable at cutoff')\\\\n                if v['system_as_of'] is not None:\\\\n                    require(instant(doc['ingested'], doc['id']) <= instant(v['system_as_of'], v['id']), 'FutureIngestion', doc['id'], 'Source not yet in database')\\\\n            for o in self.refs(v['observations'], {'observations'}):\\\\n                require(o['review_decision'] in v['decisions'], 'ViewMembership', o['id'], 'Acceptance decision omitted from view')\\\\n                for span in self.refs(o['source_spans'], {'sourceSpans'}):\\\\n                    require(span['document'] in v['documents'], 'ViewMembership', span['id'], 'Observation source omitted from view')\\\\n        for book in d['books']:\\\\n            entity = self.ref(book['entity'], {'entities'}); package = self.ref(book['package'], {'packages'})\\\\n            require(book['currency'] == entity['functional_currency'], 'BookCurrency', book['id'], 'Declared functional currency differs')\\\\n            require(book['basis'] == package['id'], 'PackageBasis', book['id'], 'Demo book uses its dated package ID')\\\\n        for a in d['accounts']:\\\\n            self.ref(a['book'], {'books'})\\\\n            expected = {'Cash': ('Asset', 'cash'), 'Debt': ('Liability', 'debt'),\\\\n                        'InterestExpense': ('Expense', 'interest'), 'Retained': ('Equity', 'retained')}\\\\n            require(a['id'] in expected and (a['role'], a['report_concept']) == expected[a['id']],\\\\n                    'AccountMapping', a['id'], 'Account differs from the frozen statement-template role')\\\\n        for s in d['symbols']:\\\\n            self.domain(s['domain'], s['id']); self.ref(s['scope'], {'models', 'modelScopes'})\\\\n            self.refs(s['dependencies']); self.refs(s['provenance'], {'sourceSpans'})\\\\n            r = self.ref(s['admission'], {'reviewDecisions'})\\\\n            require(s['uncertainty_kind'] == 'HistoricalFact' and r['action'] == 'Accept', 'UnsupportedAdmission', s['id'], 'This profile handles an admitted factual unknown')\\\\n            require(s['id'] == 'alpha' and s['type'] == 'Real' and s['context'] is None and not s['dependencies'],\\\\n                    'UnsupportedSymbol', s['id'], 'Only the independent real fixed-rate fraction is supported')\\\\n            require(s['domain']['kind'] == 'interval' and self.domain(s['domain'], s['id']) == (0, 1)\\\\n                    and s['domain']['lower_closed'] and s['domain']['upper_closed'],\\\\n                    'AdmissionDomain', s['id'], 'Frozen admission specifies the full closed fraction interval')\\\\n            require(bool(s['provenance']) and set(s['provenance']) <= set(r['evidence']),\\\\n                    'AdmissionEvidence', s['id'], 'Unknown admission needs retained evidence')\\\\n        for e in d['expressions']:\\\\n            self.expression(e['id'])\\\\n        for a in d['assumptions']:\\\\n            self.expression(a['expression']); self.ref(a['scope'], {'alternatives', 'models', 'scenarios', 'contracts'})\\\\n            self.time(a['valid'], a['id']); instant(a['information_cutoff'], a['id']); self.refs(a['source_refs'])\\\\n            require(bool(a['rationale'].strip()), 'MissingAssumptionReason', a['id'], 'Rationale required')\\\\n            require(a['role'] != 'ReviewedDefault', 'UnprovedDefaultReview', a['id'], 'No reviewed-default evidence in this profile')\\\\n            require(a['valid']['kind'] == 'interval' and a['valid']['start'] <= horizon[0]\\\\n                    and a['valid']['end_exclusive'] >= horizon[1], 'AssumptionValidity', a['id'],\\\\n                    'Example assumptions must cover the full named scenario period')\\\\n            require(all(instant(a['information_cutoff'], a['id']) <= instant(v['cutoff'], v['id'])\\\\n                        for v in d['evidenceViews']), 'FutureAssumption', a['id'],\\\\n                    'Assumption information cutoff exceeds the example evidence view')\\\\n        for c in d['constraints']:\\\\n            require(self.expression(c['expression'])[0] == 'Bool', 'ConstraintType', c['id'], 'Constraint must be Boolean')\\\\n            self.ref(c['scope']); self.refs(c['source_refs'])\\\\n            if c['kind'] == 'assumption':\\\\n                self.assumption(c['expression'], c['scope'])\\\\n            else:\\\\n                raise Invalid('UnsupportedConstraint', c['id'], 'Only named assumption constraints in this profile')\\\\n        for a in d['alternatives']:\\\\n            self.ref(a['parent'], {'historyFamilies'}); self.ref(a['scope'], {'modelScopes'})\\\\n            self.refs(a['constraints'], {'constraints'}); self.refs(a['evidence'], {'sourceSpans'}); self.refs(a['opposing_evidence'], {'sourceSpans'})\\\\n            require(a['choice_group'] is None, 'UnsupportedChoice', a['id'], 'Named conditional views only')\\\\n            require(a['author'].strip() and a['reason'].strip(), 'MissingAlternativeReason', a['id'], 'Author and reason required')\\\\n            instant(a['created_at'], a['id'])\\\\n            require(bool(a['constraints']) and all(self.nodes[c]['scope'] == a['id'] for c in a['constraints']),\\\\n                    'AlternativeScope', a['id'], 'Alternative constraints must belong to that alternative')\\\\n            require(self.nodes[a['parent']]['scope'] == a['scope'], 'AlternativeScope', a['id'], 'Family and alternative scope differ')\\\\n        for p in d['packages']:\\\\n            path = self.root / 'docs/design/fixtures/demo-debt-package.json'\\\\n            require(p['id'] == 'DemoDebt@1' and p['version'] == '1', 'UnsupportedPackage', p['id'], 'Debt profile only')\\\\n            require(hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest() == p['digest'], 'PackageDigestMismatch', p['id'], 'Package lock differs from bytes')\\\\n            self.time(p['effective'], p['id']); self.refs(p['operations'], {'Operation'})\\\\n            self.refs(p['dependencies'], {'Library', 'Calendar'}); self.refs(p['authority'], {'SourceRef'})\\\\n            require(p['review_status'] == 'illustrative', 'UnprovedDomainReview', p['id'], 'No domain-review evidence supplied')\\\\n            require(p['basis'] == 'DemoDebt' and p['implementation'] is None and not p['extension_points'],\\\\n                    'UnsupportedPackage', p['id'], 'No executable package or overrides validated here')\\\\n            require(set(p['operations']) == {'DemoDebt@1/' + n for n in ['reset', 'accrue_and_pay', 'close', 'statements']},\\\\n                    'PackageOperations', p['id'], 'All demonstration operations required')\\\\n            require(p['effective']['kind'] == 'interval' and p['effective']['start'] <= horizon[0]\\\\n                    and p['effective']['end_exclusive'] >= horizon[1], 'PackageValidity', p['id'], 'Package must apply over the scenario period')\\\\n        for c in d['contracts']:\\\\n            self.ref(c['type'], {'ContractType'}); book = self.ref(c['book'], {'books'})\\\\n            require(c['package'] == book['package'], 'PackageBasis', c['id'], 'Contract and book package differ')\\\\n            self.refs(c['source_refs'], {'sourceSpans'})\\\\n            fields = {f['name']: f['expression'] for f in c['fields']}\\\\n            required = {'principal': f'Money<{book[\\\\\\\"currency\\\\\\\"]}>', 'fixed_fraction': 'Real', 'fixed_rate': 'Rate<annual_simple>', 'initial_floating_rate': 'Rate<annual_simple>'}\\\\n            require(len(fields) == len(c['fields']) and fields.keys() == required.keys(), 'ContractFields', c['id'], 'Wrong or repeated contract fields')\\\\n            for name, expected in required.items():\\\\n                require(self.expression(fields[name])[0] == expected, 'ContractType', c['id'] + '.' + name, expected)\\\\n                context = self.expression(fields[name])[1]\\\\n                if context is not None:\\\\n                    ctx = self.nodes[context]\\\\n                    require(ctx['entity'] == book['entity'] and ctx['basis'] == book['basis'],\\\\n                            'ContractContext', c['id'], 'Contract input belongs to another entity or basis')\\\\n                low, high = self.bounds(fields[name])\\\\n                require(low is not None and low >= 0 and (name != 'fixed_fraction' or (high is not None and high <= 1)), 'ContractDomain', name, 'Nonnegative amounts/rates and share in [0,1] required')\\\\n                if name in {'fixed_rate', 'initial_floating_rate'}:\\\\n                    self.assumption(fields[name], c['id'])\\\\n        for s in d['states']:\\\\n            self.ref(s['book'], {'books'}); iso_date(s['date'], s['id'])\\\\n            seen = set(); total = Fraction(0)\\\\n            for b in s['balances']:\\\\n                a = self.ref(b['account'], {'accounts'})\\\\n                require(a['book'] == s['book'], 'StateBook', s['id'], 'Balance belongs to another book')\\\\n                require(a['id'] not in seen, 'DuplicateBalance', s['id'], a['id']); seen.add(a['id'])\\\\n                total += rational(b['signed_amount'], s['id'])\\\\n            require(total == 0, 'UnbalancedState', s['id'], 'Signed opening balances must sum to zero')\\\\n            require(seen == {a['id'] for a in d['accounts'] if a['book'] == s['book']}, 'IncompleteState', s['id'], 'This fixture requires explicit zero balances too')\\\\n            self.refs(s['contracts'], {'contracts'}); self.refs(s['dependencies'])\\\\n            require(not s['measurements'], 'UnsupportedState', s['id'], 'Measurement state not validated in this profile')\\\\n            require(all(self.nodes[c]['book'] == s['book'] for c in s['contracts']),\\\\n                    'StateBook', s['id'], 'Active contract belongs to another book')\\\\n            opening = package_data['registry']['after-2025-close']\\\\n            require(s['book'] == opening['book'] and s['date'] == opening['date'] and\\\\n                    set(s['contracts']) == set(opening['contracts']) and\\\\n                    {b['account']: rational(b['signed_amount'], s['id']) for b in s['balances']} ==\\\\n                    {a: Fraction(v) for a, v in opening['signed_balances'].items()},\\\\n                    'OpeningStateMismatch', s['id'], 'Balanced state differs from the frozen authored opening')\\\\n        for s in d['scenarios']:\\\\n            require(s['kind'] == 'ExogenousStress' and s['probability_model'] is None and s['observed_event'] is None and s['structural_model'] is None and not s['replaced_equations'], 'UnsupportedScenario', s['id'], 'Exogenous debt stress only')\\\\n            require(len(s['drivers']) == 1 and s['drivers'][0]['name'] == 'market_rate', 'ScenarioDrivers', s['id'], 'Expected market_rate')\\\\n            require(self.expression(s['drivers'][0]['expression'])[0] == 'Driver<Rate<annual_simple>>', 'TypeMismatch', s['id'], 'Rate driver required')\\\\n            self.assumption(s['drivers'][0]['expression'], s['id'])\\\\n            low, _ = self.bounds(s['drivers'][0]['expression'])\\\\n            require(low is not None and low >= 0, 'ContractDomain', s['id'], 'DemoDebt rejects a negative reset rate')\\\\n        for scope in d['modelScopes']:\\\\n            self.refs(scope['templates'], {'ContractType'}); self.refs(scope['calendars'], {'Calendar'})\\\\n            require(not scope['choices'] and not scope['obligations'], 'UnsupportedScope', scope['id'], 'Additional structural choices/obligations need a fuller checker')\\\\n            require(len(scope['slot_limits']) == 1, 'SlotLimit', scope['id'], 'One concrete debt slot limit required')\\\\n            for slot in scope['slot_limits']:\\\\n                require(self.expression(slot['expression'])[0] == 'Int', 'SlotLimitType', scope['id'], 'Slot limit is an integer, not an implicit Real cast')\\\\n                low, high = self.bounds(slot['expression'])\\\\n                require(low == high and low is not None and low >= 0 and slot['name'] == 'debt_contracts' and len(d['contracts']) <= low, 'SlotLimit', scope['id'], 'Concrete nonnegative capacity required')\\\\n        for f in d['historyFamilies']:\\\\n            for key, kind in [('scope', 'modelScopes'), ('evidence_view', 'evidenceViews'), ('opening_state', 'states')]:\\\\n                self.ref(f[key], {kind})\\\\n            for key, kind in [('symbols', 'symbols'), ('constraints', 'constraints'), ('alternatives', 'alternatives')]:\\\\n                self.refs(f[key], {kind})\\\\n            self.refs(f['witnesses'], {'Witness'}); self.refs(f['solver_results'], {'ReferenceResult'})\\\\n            view = self.nodes[f['evidence_view']]\\\\n            require(all(o['id'] in view['observations'] for o in d['observations']) and\\\\n                    all(s['admission'] in view['decisions'] for s in d['symbols']),\\\\n                    'ViewMembership', f['id'], 'All evidence used by this bounded family must be selected')\\\\n            require(set(f['symbols']) == {s['id'] for s in d['symbols']} and\\\\n                    set(f['alternatives']) == {a['id'] for a in d['alternatives'] if a['parent'] == f['id']},\\\\n                    'FamilyMembership', f['id'], 'Family omits an authored symbol or conditional alternative')\\\\n            require(not f['choices'], 'UnsupportedChoice', f['id'], 'Finite structural cells not implemented here')\\\\n            require(f['coverage'] != 'ExactWithinScope' or f['unresolved_cells'] == 0, 'FalseCoverage', f['id'], 'Exact coverage cannot contain unknown cells')\\\\n            require(f['coverage'] != 'ExactWithinScope' or (f['completed_cells'] > 0 and f['solver_results']),\\\\n                    'FalseCoverage', f['id'], 'Exact label needs completed cells and result references; this is not proof verification')\\\\n            require(f['feasibility'] != 'Feasible' or bool(f['witnesses']), 'MissingWitness', f['id'], 'Feasible label requires a witness reference')\\\\n        for r in d['reportMappings']:\\\\n            b = self.ref(r['book'], {'books'})\\\\n            require(r['basis'] == b['basis'], 'PackageBasis', r['id'], 'Report and book bases differ')\\\\n            self.ref(r['closing_policy'], {'Operation'}); self.ref(r['cash_flow_policy'], {'CashFlowPolicy'})\\\\n            self.refs(r['required_operations'], {'Operation'})\\\\n            require(r['closing_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/close' and r['cash_flow_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/interest_operating'\\\\n                    and r['required_operations'] == ['DemoDebt@1/accrue_and_pay'], 'ReportPolicy', r['id'],\\\\n                    'Wrong policy binding for the frozen report template')\\\\n            require(len(r['rows']) == 1 and r['rows'][0]['name'] == 'package_mapping', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'One frozen template binding required')\\\\n            for row in r['rows']:\\\\n                require(self.expression(row['expression'])[0] == 'SourceRef', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'This profile binds a frozen report template')\\\\n                e = self.nodes[row['expression']]\\\\n                require(e['op'] == 'literal' and e['text'] == 'DemoDebt.statements.v1', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'Expected the statement mapping export')\\\\n        for m in d['models']:\\\\n            self.refs(m['declarations']); self.refs(m['package_lock'], {'packages'}); self.ref(m['scope'], {'modelScopes'})\\\\n            require(m['language_version'] == 'Core0.1', 'UnsupportedLanguage', m['id'], 'Core0.1 only')\\\\n            required = {r['id'] for section in ['entities', 'books', 'accounts', 'observations', 'symbols',\\\\n                        'contracts', 'alternatives', 'scenarios', 'reportMappings', 'states'] for r in d[section]}\\\\n            require(required <= set(m['declarations']) and set(m['package_lock']) == {p['id'] for p in d['packages']},\\\\n                    'ModelMembership', m['id'], 'Model omits an authored declaration or package lock')\\\\n        return {'status': 'passed', 'profile': 'authored-debt-example',\\\\n                'internal_records': len(self.nodes), 'external_exports': len(self.external),\\\\n                'coverage_claims_verified': False,\\\\n                'limits': 'Bounded static admission only; no general compiler, runtime, accounting certification or proof of historical coverage.'}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef validate(document, registry, schema, root):\\\\n    return Validator(document, registry, schema, root).validate()\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat scripts/check_core_contract.py'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_12\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat MISSION_CONTROL.md docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md data/accounting-master/next-plan.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat scripts/check_core_contract.py'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Bounded structural/semantic design oracles, with explicit coverage limits.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\\\nfrom fractions import Fraction as Q\\\\nimport hashlib\\\\nimport json\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nimport unicodedata\\\\nimport jsonschema\\\\nfrom lark import Lark, UnexpectedInput\\\\n\\\\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];D=ROOT/'docs/design';checks=[]\\\\ndef ck(name,ok,detail):\\\\n    checks.append(dict(name=name,passed=bool(ok),detail=detail))\\\\n    if not ok:raise AssertionError(name)\\\\ndef canonical(value):\\\\n    def normal(x):\\\\n        if isinstance(x,float):raise ValueError('FloatForbidden')\\\\n        if isinstance(x,str):return unicodedata.normalize('NFC',x)\\\\n        if isinstance(x,list):return [normal(i) for i in x]\\\\n        if isinstance(x,dict):return {k:normal(v) for k,v in sorted(x.items())}\\\\n        return x\\\\n    return json.dumps(normal(value),sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':'),ensure_ascii=False).encode()\\\\ndef digest(domain,value):return hashlib.sha256(domain.encode()+b'\\\\\\\\0'+canonical(value)).hexdigest()\\\\ndef uniform(seed,group,entity,contract,date,kind,index):\\\\n    key=['stream-v1',seed,group,entity,contract,date,kind,index]\\\\n    v=int.from_bytes(hashlib.sha256(canonical(key)).digest()[:8],'big')\\\\n    return Q(2*v+1,2**65)\\\\ndef main():\\\\n    source=(D/'fixtures/borrowing.acc').read_text();grammar=(D/'spec/core-0.lark').read_text()\\\\n    parser=Lark(grammar,parser='lalr',maybe_placeholders=False)\\\\n    a=parser.parse(source);b=parser.parse('// comment\\\\\\\\n'+source.replace(';',';\\\\\\\\n'))\\\\n    ck('grammar_format_invariance',a==b,'Same syntax tree after comments/whitespace')\\\\n    ck('declaration_closure',len(list(a.find_data('opening')))==1 and len(list(a.find_data('account')))==4,'Complete source has opening state and retained earnings account')\\\\n    try:parser.parse(source+'let bad = 1 + ;');raise AssertionError('Expected parse failure')\\\\n    except UnexpectedInput:ck('malformed_expression_rejected',True,'Incomplete binary expression rejected')\\\\n    package=json.loads((D/'fixtures/demo-debt-package.json').read_text())\\\\n    ck('opening_dependency_resolved',sum(Q(x) for x in package['registry']['after-2025-close']['signed_balances'].values())==0,'Cash 95, credit debt 100, debit retained loss 5')\\\\n    schema=json.loads((D/'spec/core-ir.schema.json').read_text());jsonschema.Draft202012Validator.check_schema(schema)\\\\n    fixture=json.loads((D/'fixtures/core-ir-structure.json').read_text());jsonschema.validate(fixture,schema)\\\\n    ck('closed_schema_fixture',True,'Structural validation only; full semantic compiler unimplemented')\\\\n    demo=json.loads((D/'fixtures/core-ir-demo.json').read_text());jsonschema.validate(demo,schema)\\\\n    ck('full_demo_ir_schema',True,'Author-entered expected lowering with source, context, review, state, contracts, alternatives, scenario and reporting package')\\\\n    expressions={e['id']:e for e in demo['expressions']};observations={o['id']:o for o in demo['observations']}\\\\n    def eval_expr(id,alpha):\\\\n        e=expressions[id]\\\\n        if e['op']=='literal':\\\\n            return Q(int(e['rational']['n']),int(e['rational']['d'])) if e['rational'] else e['text']\\\\n        if e['op']=='ref':return alpha if e['target']=='alpha' else observations[e['target']]\\\\n        if e['op']=='call':\\\\n            v=eval_expr(e['args'][0],alpha)\\\\n            if e['target']=='builtin:constant@1':return v\\\\n            if e['target']=='builtin:value@1':\\\\n                q=v['domain']['lower'];return Q(int(q['n']),int(q['d']))\\\\n        if e['op']=='eq':return eval_expr(e['args'][0],alpha)==eval_expr(e['args'][1],alpha)\\\\n        raise ValueError('UnsupportedReferenceExpression')\\\\n    fields={f['name']:f['expression'] for f in demo['contracts'][0]['fields']}\\\\n    for name,alpha,condition in [('allFixed',Q(1),'is.fixed'),('allFloating',Q(0),'is.floating')]:\\\\n        principal=eval_expr(fields['principal'],alpha);fixed=eval_expr(fields['fixed_rate'],alpha)\\\\n        floating=eval_expr(demo['scenarios'][0]['drivers'][0]['expression'],alpha)\\\\n        interest=principal*(alpha*fixed+(1-alpha)*floating)\\\\n        opening={x['account']:Q(int(x['signed_amount']['n']),int(x['signed_amount']['d'])) for x in demo['states'][0]['balances']}\\\\n        expected=package['expected'][name]\\\\n        ck('demo_ir_to_result_'+name,eval_expr(condition,alpha) and interest==Q(expected['interest']) and opening['Cash']-interest==Q(expected['cash']) and -opening['Retained']-interest==Q(expected['equity']),\\\\n           'Reference evaluator consumes authored IR; general source-to-IR compiler still pending')\\\\n    bad=deepcopy(fixture);bad['expressions'][0]['hidden_assumption']=True\\\\n    try:jsonschema.validate(bad,schema);raise AssertionError('Expected unknown field error')\\\\n    except jsonschema.ValidationError:ck('unknown_ir_field_rejected',True,'Closed record detects undeclared data')\\\\n    # A literal parsed from the real source agrees with a typed-library value.\\\\n    obs=list(a.find_data('observation'))[0];number=list(obs.find_data('number'))[0]\\\\n    parsed=Q(str(number.children[0]));typed=Q(100)\\\\n    ck('literal_frontend_equivalence',parsed==typed and fixture['expressions'][0]['rational']==dict(n=str(typed.numerator),d=str(typed.denominator)),'Limited literal lowering, not whole-program compiler conformance')\\\\n    x={'model':'M','amount':{'n':'5','d':'1'},'label':'caf\\\\\\\\u00e9'}\\\\n    y={'label':'cafe\\\\\\\\u0301','amount':{'d':'1','n':'5'},'model':'M'}\\\\n    ck('canonical_key_unicode',digest('model-v1',x)==digest('model-v1',y),'Dictionary order and Unicode composition do not change semantic digest')\\\\n    changed=deepcopy(x);changed['amount']['n']='7'\\\\n    ck('changed_model_identity',digest('model-v1',x)!=digest('model-v1',changed),'Rate/value change creates a different model')\\\\n    ck('identity_domains_separate',digest('evidence-v1',x)!=digest('model-v1',x),'Evidence and model hashes are not interchangeable')\\\\n    try:canonical({'amount':0.1});raise AssertionError('Expected float rejection')\\\\n    except ValueError:ck('canonical_float_rejected',True,'No accidental binary float identity')\\\\n    branches=['fixed','floating'];draws={b:uniform('seed1','shared','Acme','debt1','2026-01-01','rate',0) for b in branches}\\\\n    reversed_draws={b:uniform('seed1','shared','Acme','debt1','2026-01-01','rate',0) for b in reversed(branches)}\\\\n    ck('stable_branch_streams',draws==reversed_draws and draws['fixed']==draws['floating'],'Ordering absent; common coupling explicit')\\\\n    ck('measurement_outer_stream_separation',uniform('seed1','shared','Acme','loan1','2026-01-01','inner-default',0)!=uniform('seed1','shared','Acme','loan1','2026-01-01','outer-default',0),'No reuse of realised outer default in allowance draw')\\\\n    ck('uniform_open_interval',all(0<u<1 for u in draws.values()),'Reference primitive produces neither endpoint')\\\\n    # Dependency closure after a review correction.\\\\n    graph={'reading':['mapping'],'mapping':['constraint'],'constraint':['family'],'family':['run'],'run':['report'],'unrelated':[]}\\\\n    pending=['reading'];affected=set()\\\\n    while pending:\\\\n        k=pending.pop()\\\\n        for child in graph.get(k,[]):\\\\n            if child not in affected:affected.add(child);pending.append(child)\\\\n    ck('review_invalidation',affected=={'mapping','constraint','family','run','report'},'Transitive descendants stale; unrelated state reusable')\\\\n    # Information capability uses role/date rather than exposing the entire path.\\\\n    records=[dict(id='current-pd',date='2026-01-01',kind='forecast'),dict(id='future-default',date='2026-06-01',kind='realised')]\\\\n    visible=[r['id'] for r in records if r['date']<='2026-01-01']\\\\n    ck('no_future_realisation',visible==['current-pd'],'Measurement can use current PD, not future realised default')\\\\n    partitions={'geography':{'domestic':Q(180),'overseas':Q(80)},'channel':{'wholesale':Q(200),'retail':Q(60)}}\\\\n    ck('overlapping_axes',all(sum(v.values())==260 for v in partitions.values()) and sum(sum(v.values()) for v in partitions.values())==520,'Adding both axes double-counts the same population; require one partition')\\\\n    # Genuine joint counterexample: extrema of cash/equity cannot be selected independently.\\\\n    import z3\\\\n    alpha=z3.Real('alpha_joint');s=z3.Solver();s.add(alpha>=0,alpha<=1,z3.RealVal('93.6')+z3.RealVal('1.6')*alpha==z3.RealVal('93.6'),z3.RealVal('146.6')+z3.RealVal('1.6')*alpha==z3.RealVal('148.2'))\\\\n    ck('incompatible_marginal_extrema',s.check()==z3.unsat,'Lowest cash and highest equity do not describe one history')\\\\n    apple=json.loads((D/'cases/apple/manifest.json').read_text())\\\\n    ck('real_source_note_inventory',len([n for n in apple['notes'] if n['source']=='annual'])==13 and len([n for n in apple['notes'] if n['source']=='interim'])==10,'Note headings reconciled to annual/interim indices')\\\\n    for row in apple['statements']:\\\\n        ck('apple_balance_'+row['date'],Q(row['assets'])==Q(row['liabilities'])+Q(row['equity']),row['source'])\\\\n    d=apple['debt_measurements'];ck('apple_debt_measurements',Q(d['principal'])+Q(d['discount_cost_adjustment'])+Q(d['hedge_carrying_adjustment'])==Q(d['carrying']),'Note 9 principal differs from carrying and fair value')\\\\n    scenario=apple['marginal_stress'];i=Q(scenario['exposure_assumption'])*Q(scenario['rate_increment'])*Q(scenario['year_fraction']);last=apple['statements'][-1];expected=scenario['expected']\\\\n    ck('apple_marginal_forecast',i==Q(expected['interest']) and Q(last['cash'])-i==Q(expected['cash']) and Q(last['assets'])-i==Q(expected['assets']) and Q(last['equity'])-i==Q(expected['equity']),'Conditional extra interest 72.875 million, not estimated actual sensitivity')\\\\n    ck('external_reference_limit_visible',any(x['status'].startswith('not_acquired') for x in apple['cross_reference_obligations']),'Proxy/reference closure is not called complete')\\\\n    L=Q(5)/Q('1.1')+Q(105)/Q('1.21');L1=L*Q('1.1')-5;L2=L1*Q('1.1')-5\\\\n    ck('compound_bond',L==Q(11050,121) and L1==Q(1050,11) and L2==100 and (100-L)+L==100,'Separate issue components and amortisation before redemption/conversion')\\\\n    f1=(Q(150)+180)/(100+120);f2=Q(180)/150;reserve=180*f2-180+140*f1*f2-140\\\\n    ck('chain_ladder_point',f1==Q('1.5') and f2==Q('1.2') and reserve==148,'Point projection only; terminal variance not identified by one paired observation')\\\\n    decisions=json.loads((D/'research/forward-screening-decisions.json').read_text())['records'];ids={r['id'] for r in decisions}\\\\n    forward=json.loads((D/'research/forward-snowball.json').read_text())['records']\\\\n    ck('screening_traceability',all(c['id'] in ids and c.get('decision_source') for r in forward for c in r.get('candidates',[])),'Every retrieved candidate has an individual decision; metadata screening distinct from full-text support')\\\\n    out=D/'review/core-contract-checks.json';out.write_text(json.dumps(dict(status='passed',checks=checks,count=len(checks),scope='Reference grammar, selected schema/literal semantics, identities, information/dependency/financial counterexamples; no full compiler or adapter integration',command='python3 scripts/check_core_contract.py',sha256={str(p.relative_to(ROOT)):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in [D/'spec/core-0.lark',D/'spec/core-ir.schema.json',D/'spec/core-contract.md']}),indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\n')\\\\n    print(json.dumps(dict(status='passed',checks=len(checks),report=str(out.relative_to(ROOT)))))\\\\n\\\\nif __name__=='__main__':main()\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_12\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat MISSION_CONTROL.md docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md data/accounting-master/next-plan.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# AccDSL mission control\\\\n\\\\nEstablished 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong) at the user's request.\\\\nStatus: active mission; Version 1.2 is a repaired design candidate with checked\\\\nreference cases. Full product, domain and human acceptance remain pending.\\\\n\\\\n## Purpose\\\\n\\\\nDesign a system that represents a company's historical financial disclosures,\\\\npreserves economically different histories and interpretations compatible with\\\\nthe evidence, and carries those alternatives into scenario-dependent future\\\\njournals and financial statements. Preserve their separate conditional outcome\\\\ndistributions or feasible sets, including uncertainty that cannot be assigned\\\\ndefensible probabilities.\\\\n\\\\nThe immediate deliverable is a detailed, readable LaTeX product and method\\\\ndesign, with compiled PDF, supporting literature and software investigation,\\\\nprecise implementation contracts and acceptance examples. The eventual product\\\\nis the working representation and simulation engine. A document build, a small\\\\nfinancing example and an implemented prototype are different achievements.\\\\n\\\\n## Authority and origin\\\\n\\\\nThis mission records the user's existing directions; it does not replace new\\\\nuser instructions or higher-priority instructions. The three original requests\\\\nare preserved in saved session `01a0f8e0-0c0b-7332-8f7e-d6b93ce32761`, at JSONL\\\\nrecords 10, 115 and 145. They establish whole-company history, heterogeneous\\\\naccounting, preservation of alternative journals/outcomes, a broad literature\\\\nand software survey, and an implementation-governing LaTeX document. The current\\\\nrequest establishes this durable mission and a requirements-based gap audit.\\\\n\\\\nThe user's subsequent direction establishes MC35: complete feasible internal\\\\npreparation before paying for professional review. The user supplied a planning\\\\nrate of US$500–1,200/hour. This work order is binding; no estimated savings or\\\\nprofessional engagement is inferred from it.\\\\n\\\\nThe [requirements register](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md)\\\\ndistinguishes direct user requirements from policy obligations and engineering\\\\nrequirements derived from those goals. Python, storage engines, parser design,\\\\nsolver libraries and a particular first-company example remain replaceable\\\\nimplementation proposals. Designing a DSL is part of the work; claiming it is\\\\nbetter than all alternatives is not a predetermined conclusion.\\\\n\\\\n## Main goals\\\\n\\\\n| Goal | Required outcome |\\\\n| --- | --- |\\\\n| M1 — Represent the historical record | Preserve annual, quarterly and semi-annual statements, notes, policies and relevant referenced disclosures, with their source, context, temporal meaning and unresolved content. |\\\\n| M2 — Preserve alternative explanations | Represent joint families of admissible histories, journal movements, contract states and interpretations; distinguish absent facts, accounting choices, estimates and future randomness. |\\\\n| M3 — Simulate financial evolution | Apply explicit economic scenarios and behaviour to economic state, generate admissible journal entries, and produce coherent future statements and conditional results. |\\\\n| M4 — Handle accounting and sector diversity | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE, industry and company differences, group boundaries, banks, insurers, liabilities, capital, bonds and equity. |\\\\n| M5 — Specify implementable methods and language | Define reconstruction, accounting, inference and execution procedures, types, IR, DSL, interfaces, failure behaviour and persistence precisely enough for compatible implementations. |\\\\n| M6 — Ground choices in research and reusable tools | Inspect primary literature beyond the existing collection and official software, archive relevant sources, compare credible alternatives and document justified inclusion/exclusion and reuse decisions. |\\\\n| M7 — Deliver the governing design | Produce one rigorous, understandable LaTeX/PDF argument with complete worked cases, explicit scope, source support, method details and an implementation sequence. |\\\\n| M8 — Establish evidence and maintain direction | Define conformance and release evidence, preserve reproducibility, keep engineering/accounting/scientific conclusions separate, and maintain requirements and open decisions as work proceeds. |\\\\n\\\\n## Requirements that must survive every implementation choice\\\\n\\\\n1. Source preservation is broader than numerical extraction. Account for all\\\\n   source material within the declared disclosure package, including notes and\\\\n   cross-references. Content that cannot yet be formalised stays visible with\\\\n   a reason; it is not silently excluded from a completeness claim.\\\\n2. Preserve reported assertions, derived consequences and modelling assumptions\\\\n   separately. A missing value is not zero; a reported number is not automatic\\\\n   proof of the underlying economic state. Source conflicts remain inspectable.\\\\n3. Carry entity, group perimeter, concept, dimensions, units, currency, basis,\\\\n   precision and time through every calculation. Label mapping does not itself\\\\n   convert between accounting standards. Avoid double counting overlapping\\\\n   classifications.\\\\n4. Preserve original and revised information. Economic time, reporting periods,\\\\n   availability/publication and system ingestion/version time answer different\\\\n   questions. Historical forecasts cannot use later evidence inadvertently.\\\\n5. Keep alternatives jointly consistent across statements, notes, dates,\\\\n   contracts and accounts. Include economic state beyond journals: identical\\\\n   historical postings can conceal different future exposures.\\\\n6. Every reconstructed family has an explicit model scope and completeness\\\\n   status. A selected witness, bounded search or convenient aggregate cannot be\\\\n   presented as all real histories. Scope exclusions remain mission limitations.\\\\n7. Preserve conditional results by explanation and scenario. A set or interval\\\\n   does not become a probability distribution without a declared measure. No\\\\n   weights from representation counts, arbitrary equality or LLM confidence.\\\\n   Keep dependence between statement amounts and through time.\\\\n8. Generate events from explicit contract and behavioural assumptions, then\\\\n   apply recognition/measurement and posting rules. Balanced journals are\\\\n   necessary but do not prove accounting treatment or economic correctness.\\\\n9. Treat unsupported calculations, unresolved branches, numerical failure and\\\\n   economically meaningful default as distinct outcomes. Do not silently drop\\\\n   failed branches, manufacture financing or report sampled extrema as exact\\\\n   bounds.\\\\n10. Compare a DSL with credible alternatives on the same tasks, especially the\\\\n    typed-library/shared-IR baseline. Reuse software where its inspected\\\\n    capabilities fit, with explicit adapter contracts and limits.\\\\n11. Support imported technical claims with inspected primary sections and local\\\\n    copies. Preserve relevant papers under `docs/papers` using\\\\n    `Title First-author-surname (year).pdf`; preserve the original collection.\\\\n    Technical reading, actual literature screening and source corrections must\\\\n    be recorded, not inferred from metadata or generated status labels.\\\\n12. Make assumptions, derivations, scope and limits understandable in the\\\\n    manuscript itself. Full company cases and precise expected outputs must\\\\n    connect the concepts to implementation. Page count and polished prose are\\\\n    not substitutes for these requirements.\\\\n\\\\n## What counts as completion\\\\n\\\\nThe [requirement register](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md)\\\\ndefines evidence needed for MC01–MC35. Each requirement must have an identified\\\\ndocument location, stated behaviour/method, a suitable worked case or other\\\\ncheck, and an honest assessment. A mention is `partial`; promised future work\\\\nis `open`; a precise design is `specified`; checked evidence can support\\\\n`checked` within its stated scope. `Not checked` is never silently converted\\\\nto `passed`. These are design statuses, not implemented-product statuses.\\\\n\\\\nA proposed implementation-governing design requires:\\\\n\\\\n- complete scope and methods for the declared initial executable profile;\\\\n- a concrete structural design and method/support obligations for every\\\\n  explicitly requested domain, including later bank and insurance modules;\\\\n- source-to-record-to-history-to-journal-to-statement worked cases, with\\\\n  uncertainty, revisions and failure cases;\\\\n- exact interfaces and conformance fixtures for the supported language/model;\\\\n- inspected support for imported claims and explicit disposition of genuine\\\\n  source gaps;\\\\n- checked mathematics, references and rendered presentation, with review\\\\n  records identifying what was and was not checked.\\\\n\\\\nA source gap blocks its unsupported claim. A missing later engine does not\\\\nblock the initial core, but a method that is still unspecified remains open\\\\nin the full design. Do not close the wider mission merely by making a tiny\\\\nmodel's scope exclude every difficult case. Scope reductions require actual\\\\nuser direction; routine choices within the scope do not require repeated\\\\npermission.\\\\n\\\\nHuman comprehension, independent domain review, executable conformance and\\\\nscientific forecast validation retain their own pending or completed states.\\\\nMissing feedback does not block provisional drafting and repair. Do not\\\\ninvent acceptance or claim a compliant engine from author self-review.\\\\n\\\\n## Internal preparation before paid review\\\\n\\\\nFinish feasible internal source retrieval and inspection, fact collection,\\\\ncalculations, software tests, competing-interpretation analysis and document\\\\nrepairs before referring a particular question to a professional. “Review\\\\npending” must not transfer those tasks to an accountant or stop authorised work.\\\\nSeparate ordinary reader feedback from accounting-firm review. Keep acceptance\\\\nprovisional where human evidence is still missing.\\\\n\\\\nUse the [G1–G18 work allocation](docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md)\\\\nto preserve the internal queue. A possible later question needs a proposed\\\\nanswer, strongest counterargument, precise authority, complete facts and\\\\nchecked consequences. The [unsent brief](docs/design/review/future-professional-review-brief.md)\\\\nprovides question-specific deliverables and a user-chosen fee/time cap for any\\\\nfuture engagement. No packet is presently declared ready for paid review.\\\\nMissing current authority, software or actual contract facts are preparation\\\\ntasks, not generic requests for professional approval.\\\\n\\\\n## How work is controlled\\\\n\\\\nBefore a nontrivial work unit, identify its MC requirements, current gaps,\\\\nassumptions and smallest useful validation. Perform the skeptical plan audit\\\\nrequired by the project policies. Use the existing research-plan/evidence\\\\nworkflow for actual experiments; document-only edits do not need invented\\\\nresearch metrics or a performance campaign.\\\\n\\\\nAfter a substantive change, update the affected requirement assessments and\\\\nthe [checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md). A gap\\\\ncloses only against its stated evidence. Maintain continuity between the\\\\noriginal [G1–G10 audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and the\\\\n[expanded audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md). New findings\\\\ncan be added; neither list is asserted to be permanently exhaustive. Review\\\\ninteractions between requirements, not only the rows separately.\\\\n\\\\nUse separate judgements for the document, engineering implementation,\\\\naccounting validity and scientific interpretation. Follow the applicable\\\\npolicies in `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`, including scientific\\\\ncoding, literature audit and natural reader-facing prose. Operational mission\\\\nrecords belong here, not as repeated administrative scaffolding in the paper.\\\\n\\\\nThe user's corpus-first priority has reached source acceptance: panel v2 has\\\\n192 annual/interim reports across nine issuers, three evidenced accounting\\\\nfamilies and eight complete years per issuer (2018–2025). Henkel and Munich Re\\\\nreplace the two inaccessible interim series under the reviewed selection repair;\\\\nv1 evidence remains preserved. The [corpus result](docs/plans/accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md)\\\\nand independent integrity manifest record the checks and limitations. Resume\\\\nfrom that source set, not the former tiny real-company baseline. This closes\\\\nthe source-collection work unit, not accounting annotations, complete package\\\\nsemantics, historical availability, implementation or model validation.\\\\n\\\\nAfter the source-corpus work, extend the checked authored-debt registry and\\\\nsemantic validator to the supported Core 0 language and shared-IR compilation,\\\\nthen the bounded\\\\nNorthstar reconstruction/execution path. Use the new cases to validate selected\\\\nadapters. Acquire missing accounting authority and expand the real corpus as\\\\nbank/insurer and broader standards methods advance. These stages preserve the\\\\nfull mission; their unimplemented status does not erase the design delivered.\\\\n\\\\n## Current assessment and open decisions\\\\n\\\\nThe [reviewed repair plan](docs/plans/accounting-gap-repair-2026-10-02.md) has\\\\nbeen executed as a bounded document/specification campaign. The revised\\\\n[design](docs/design/accounting-product-design.pdf) has 11 chapters and two\\\\nappendices, a complete synthetic company, a named Apple disclosure case,\\\\nrounded reconstruction, finite probability examples, corporate/sector cases,\\\\nCore 0 contracts and acceptance protocols. The [result map](docs/design/review/gap-repair-results-2026-10-02.md)\\\\nrecords G1–G18 repairs and remaining obligations. All MC01–MC34 assessments\\\\nhave been updated without changing their requirement or acceptance wording.\\\\n\\\\nThe [internal preparation results](docs/design/review/internal-preparation-results.md)\\\\nrecord Version 1.2 corrections, a bounded semantic checker, adversarial inputs,\\\\nthree accounting dossiers, and MC35's standing cost constraint. The original\\\\n34 technical requirements remain intact; MC35 adds the user's work-order rule.\\\\n\\\\nReference arithmetic, solver, grammar/schema, bounded static and review checks support their\\\\nstated examples only. The full compiler/runtime and non-Z3 adapters are not\\\\nimplemented. The real filing has complete acquired-file inventory but partial\\\\nsemantics and incomplete external incorporation closure. Full ASC authority,\\\\nofficial-current ASBE verification, richer bank/insurance methods, independent\\\\naccounting/implementability review and human comprehension remain open.\\\\n\\\\nDecisions now recorded include Northstar/Apple, rational-linear reconstruction,\\\\nseparate evidence clocks and review actions, deterministic operating assumptions,\\\\noptional finite weights, schema/identity/storage boundaries, corpus strata and\\\\nprovisional workload limits. Future measured capacity, production library locks,\\\\nempirical forecast calibration and corpus adjudication need their own evidence.\\\\nThe [checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md) preserves\\\\ncommands, review records and the next justified steps. No scope reduction or\\\\nwhole-mission completion is implied by this candidate.\\\\n\\\\nNo external deployment, global agent-policy installation, production-security\\\\nprogramme, full-economy equilibrium model or forecast-superiority claim is\\\\nimplied by this mission. Such work needs its own substantive justification.\\\\n# Accounting master checkpoint\\\\n\\\\nEstablished: 2 October 2026 under the user's create/review/execute instruction.\\\\nThe executable catalog covers G1–G18 while retaining MC01–MC35 unchanged.\\\\n\\\\n## Resume entry point\\\\n\\\\nRun this exact command, without shell wrappers or environment prefixes:\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py run\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nRead current execution state rather than this installation-time note:\\\\n\\\\n- ../../data/accounting-master/state.json\\\\n- ../../data/accounting-master/next-plan.md\\\\n- ../../data/accounting-master/events.jsonl\\\\n- ../../data/accounting-master/runs/\\\\n- accounting-master-program.md\\\\n- ../design/review/accounting-master-review.md\\\\n\\\\nThe status command uses the same prefix and never starts workers. A stop command\\\\nrequests bounded child termination and preserves partial work. Normal run resumes\\\\nafter a previous stop. --retry-blocked is reserved for deliberately retrying a\\\\nknown external block after changed access or environment; ordinary resume does\\\\nnot repeatedly probe it.\\\\n\\\\n## Evidence and scope\\\\n\\\\nThe accepted financial-report corpus remains frozen and source-complete for its\\\\ndeclared panel. Master outputs go under data/accounting-master; original release\\\\nhashes are not rewritten to conceal changes. Existing Git remains unusable and\\\\nhas not been initialised. Prior editable source bytes are retained before phase\\\\nworkers change them. New source research must preserve provenance and limitations.\\\\n\\\\nPlanning, implementation and read-only review run sequentially, with no nested\\\\nagents. The upfront grant is scoped to this program, its filesystem sandboxes,\\\\nlegitimate public-source research and project-local work. It does not authorise\\\\nprofessional fees, paid data/accounts, deployment, outreach or global packages.\\\\n\\\\nA bounded accepted phase does not close its wider accounting/design gap. The\\\\nrefreshed plan retains residuals and next actions; independent work continues\\\\nwhile external/human acceptance is pending. P00/P01 preflights passed after a\\\\nbaseline import-path repair. Full execution and reviewer verdicts are recorded\\\\nby the runner, not assumed here.\\\\n# Accounting master — refreshed next plan\\\\n\\\\nUpdated: 2026-10-02T18:12:07.392068+00:00\\\\n\\\\nNext eligible phase: P02.\\\\nMission complete: **no**. Scoped phase acceptance does not close the original gaps.\\\\n\\\\n| Phase | State | Residual work |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| P00 — Verify the accepted baseline | accepted_internal | All G1–G18 retain work; bounded reference checks do not establish accounting or forecast validity. |\\\\n| P01 — Prepare source-context and availability work records | accepted_internal | Publication/version evidence, semantic annotation, incorporated packages and benchmark labels remain open. |\\\\n| P02 — Complete the bounded Apple case preparation | needs_repair |  |\\\\n| P03 — Implement source lowering and shared IR | running |  |\\\\n| P04 — Implement reconstruction and numerical operations | pending |  |\\\\n| P05 — Execute the bounded company path | pending |  |\\\\n| P06 — Enforce context, chronology and resolution | pending |  |\\\\n| P07 — Implement review, persistence and recovery | pending |  |\\\\n| P08 — Resolve authority and corporate-method obligations | pending |  |\\\\n| P09 — Extend bank methods | pending |  |\\\\n| P10 — Extend insurance methods | pending |  |\\\\n| P11 — Exercise adapters and matched frontends | pending |  |\\\\n| P12 — Prepare and exercise a bounded benchmark | pending |  |\\\\n| P13 — Develop calibrated forecasting methods and evidence | pending |  |\\\\n| P14 — Integrate the design and independent-review preparation | pending |  |\\\\n\\\\n## Latest outcome\\\\n\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"P02\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"needs_repair\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"issues\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    \\\\\\\"MasterError: Command failed (timeout); inspect data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P02/plan-0.log\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"residuals\\\\\\\": []\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n## Next action\\\\n\\\\nReview the next eligible slice against these actual outcomes; all gap closures require separate requirement evidence.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_13\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc docs/design/spec/core-0.lark'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_13\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc docs/design/spec/core-0.lark'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"module BorrowingExample version \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\";\\\\nuse DemoDebt version \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\";\\\\nsource note7 = external(\\\\\\\"synthetic-note-7\\\\\\\");\\\\nentity Acme functional USD;\\\\nbook Local entity Acme basis DemoDebt version \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\";\\\\naccount Cash : Asset book Local;\\\\naccount Debt : Liability book Local;\\\\naccount InterestExpense : Expense book Local;\\\\naccount Retained : Equity book Local;\\\\nopening after2025 for Local from external(\\\\\\\"after-2025-close\\\\\\\");\\\\nobservation debt : Money<USD> instant @2025-12-31 = 100 USD from note7;\\\\nsymbol alpha : Real in [0, 1] because \\\\\\\"Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed\\\\\\\";\\\\ncontract loans : DebtMix book Local {\\\\n  principal = value(debt);\\\\n  fixed_fraction = alpha;\\\\n  fixed_rate = 0.05 per year;\\\\n  initial_floating_rate = 0.05 per year;\\\\n}\\\\nalternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }\\\\nalternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }\\\\nscenario rateShock { set market_rate = constant(0.07 per year); }\\\\nreport statements for Local { mapping = external(\\\\\\\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\\\\\\\"); }\\\\n// Normative Core 0 syntax, Lark EBNF. UTF-8 input; ASCII identifiers.\\\\n// Longest token wins; keywords cannot be declaration identifiers.\\\\nstart: \\\\\\\"module\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\" declaration*\\\\n?declaration: use | source | entity | book | account | observation | symbol\\\\n            | choice | binding | constraint | alternative | contract | event\\\\n            | rule | scenario | report | opening\\\\nuse: \\\\\\\"use\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nsource: \\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nentity: \\\\\\\"entity\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"functional\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nbook: \\\\\\\"book\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"entity\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"basis\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\naccount: \\\\\\\"account\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"book\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nobservation: \\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type time_spec \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\"from\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\ntime_spec: \\\\\\\"instant\\\\\\\" DATE | \\\\\\\"period\\\\\\\" DATE \\\\\\\"to\\\\\\\" DATE\\\\nsymbol: \\\\\\\"symbol\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type \\\\\\\"in\\\\\\\" domain \\\\\\\"because\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\ndomain: \\\\\\\"[\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" expr (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" expr)* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nchoice: \\\\\\\"choice\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"in\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" NAME (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" NAME)* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"because\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nbinding: \\\\\\\"let\\\\\\\" NAME [\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type] \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nconstraint: \\\\\\\"constraint\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nalternative: \\\\\\\"alternative\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" assumption* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nassumption: \\\\\\\"assume\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\ncontract: \\\\\\\"contract\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"book\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" field* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nfield: NAME \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nevent: \\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"(\\\\\\\" [parameters] \\\\\\\")\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"book\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nparameters: NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type)*\\\\nrule: \\\\\\\"rule\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"for\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"as\\\\\\\" NAME [\\\\\\\"overrides\\\\\\\" NAME (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" NAME)*] \\\\\\\"when\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" rule_statement* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\n?rule_statement: binding | require | post\\\\nrequire: \\\\\\\"require\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\npost: \\\\\\\"post\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" posting+ \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nposting: SIDE NAME expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nscenario: \\\\\\\"scenario\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" setting* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nsetting: \\\\\\\"set\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nreport: \\\\\\\"report\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"for\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" field* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nopening: \\\\\\\"opening\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"for\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"from\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\ntype: NAME [\\\\\\\"<\\\\\\\" type (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" type)* \\\\\\\">\\\\\\\"]\\\\n?expr: disjunction\\\\n?disjunction: conjunction (OR conjunction)*\\\\n?conjunction: comparison (AND comparison)*\\\\n?comparison: sum [COMPARE sum]\\\\n?sum: product (ADD product)*\\\\n?product: unary (MUL unary)*\\\\n?unary: UNARY unary | postfix\\\\n?postfix: atom (\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\" NAME)*\\\\n?atom: number | STRING | DATE | BOOL | call | NAME | \\\\\\\"(\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\")\\\\\\\" | array | record\\\\ncall: NAME \\\\\\\"(