37982110db15fa7a355f7\\\\\\\",\\\\ndata/accounting-master/state.json:79:        \\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/checks.json\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"af0cb563dcaa33f3a024051d403069b805f2460130898c89d41b80581a21724e\\\\\\\"\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:1:# Product-design gap audit\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:7:## Question, baseline and skeptical audit\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:26:document's own typed-library baseline. Check all chapters and companion records\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:33:## Findings\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:47:### G1. Reconstruction defines the answer more precisely than the algorithm\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:67:candidate-generation procedure, constraint lowering, scope exclusions,\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:73:### G2. The normative language and IR contracts remain incomplete\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G3. Ordinary disclosure uncertainty can leave the promised solver fragment\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:111:complete lowering or approximation policy is not.\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:124:### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:145:### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:164:### G6. Forward economic and probability models remain interfaces\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:192:### G7. Standards, banks and insurance are largely deferred requirements\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:218:### G8. Literature breadth exceeds the depth of the follow-up screening\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:246:### G9. Tool selection is a shortlist, without demonstrated adapter contracts\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:265:### G10. Acceptance and completion are not yet determinate\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:289:## Prioritised repair sequence\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:306:## Review evidence and limits\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:320:that any proposed library is unsuitable.\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:1:# Review against the AccDSL mission\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:9:## Answer and review scope\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:24:## Goals and current coverage\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:37:## Additional explicit findings\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:39:### G11. Whole-report coverage and narrative formalisation need a procedure\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:41:Requirements: MC01, MC03. Refines G2 and G5.\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:60:### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:62:Requirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:79:### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:81:Requirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:119:### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:121:Requirements: MC04, MC08, MC10, MC12, MC24. Refines G1, G2 and G6.\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:138:### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:147:avoids claiming a general equivalence-deciding compiler, but does not specify\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:156:### G17. Local evidence review needs a state machine and invalidation rules\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:158:Requirements: MC04, MC27. Refines G2, G5 and G10.\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:174:### G18. Reproducibility needs identity and replay definitions, not only fields\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:176:Requirements: MC25, MC34. Refines G2, G9 and G10.\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:193:## Completion consequences\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:213:## Evidence and limits of this pass\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:1:# Active checkpoint\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:8:## Accepted source corpus and next execution\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:38:Core 0 semantic/compiler implementation using the preserved source set and\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:46:## Current deliverable\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:83:## Evidence preserved\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:99:manifest and tracks the external grammar input. The library contains 32\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:105:compiler. The new `core_semantics.py` validates the authored monetary debt\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:117:## Remaining work and next justified steps\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:119:1. Extend the checked debt-profile registry/reference/type validation and implement source-to-IR lowering\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:120:   against the positive/negative cases. Schema parsing is not complete compiler\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:146:## Recovery history\\\\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/global-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md\\\\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/scholarly-literature-audit-policy.md\\\\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/humanizer-ai-writing-patterns.md\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_15\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"reasoning\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"**Evaluating output truncation**\\\\n\\\\nI’m considering how output truncation needs to be handled, focusing on ensuring that all key evidence is kept while avoiding any broad statements. It seems like it’s crucial to define clear boundaries for what information is included. I wonder how to balance conciseness with comprehensive coverage of important evidence. I'll aim for precision while making sure important details aren't lost in the process, which can definitely be a tricky balance!\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_16\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"cat docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc docs/design/spec/core-0.lark; wc -l scripts/core_semantics.py docs/design/spec/core-contract.md scripts/check_semantic_preparation.py scripts/build_demo_registry.py docs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json; sed -n '1,200p' scripts/core_semantics.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_16\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"cat docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc docs/design/spec/core-0.lark; wc -l scripts/core_semantics.py docs/design/spec/core-contract.md scripts/check_semantic_preparation.py scripts/build_demo_registry.py docs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json; sed -n '1,200p' scripts/core_semantics.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"module BorrowingExample version \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\";\\\\nuse DemoDebt version \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\";\\\\nsource note7 = external(\\\\\\\"synthetic-note-7\\\\\\\");\\\\nentity Acme functional USD;\\\\nbook Local entity Acme basis DemoDebt version \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\";\\\\naccount Cash : Asset book Local;\\\\naccount Debt : Liability book Local;\\\\naccount InterestExpense : Expense book Local;\\\\naccount Retained : Equity book Local;\\\\nopening after2025 for Local from external(\\\\\\\"after-2025-close\\\\\\\");\\\\nobservation debt : Money<USD> instant @2025-12-31 = 100 USD from note7;\\\\nsymbol alpha : Real in [0, 1] because \\\\\\\"Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed\\\\\\\";\\\\ncontract loans : DebtMix book Local {\\\\n  principal = value(debt);\\\\n  fixed_fraction = alpha;\\\\n  fixed_rate = 0.05 per year;\\\\n  initial_floating_rate = 0.05 per year;\\\\n}\\\\nalternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }\\\\nalternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }\\\\nscenario rateShock { set market_rate = constant(0.07 per year); }\\\\nreport statements for Local { mapping = external(\\\\\\\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\\\\\\\"); }\\\\n// Normative Core 0 syntax, Lark EBNF. UTF-8 input; ASCII identifiers.\\\\n// Longest token wins; keywords cannot be declaration identifiers.\\\\nstart: \\\\\\\"module\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\" declaration*\\\\n?declaration: use | source | entity | book | account | observation | symbol\\\\n            | choice | binding | constraint | alternative | contract | event\\\\n            | rule | scenario | report | opening\\\\nuse: \\\\\\\"use\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nsource: \\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nentity: \\\\\\\"entity\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"functional\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nbook: \\\\\\\"book\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"entity\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"basis\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\naccount: \\\\\\\"account\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"book\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nobservation: \\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type time_spec \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\"from\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\ntime_spec: \\\\\\\"instant\\\\\\\" DATE | \\\\\\\"period\\\\\\\" DATE \\\\\\\"to\\\\\\\" DATE\\\\nsymbol: \\\\\\\"symbol\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type \\\\\\\"in\\\\\\\" domain \\\\\\\"because\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\ndomain: \\\\\\\"[\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" expr (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" expr)* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nchoice: \\\\\\\"choice\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"in\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" NAME (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" NAME)* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"because\\\\\\\" STRING \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nbinding: \\\\\\\"let\\\\\\\" NAME [\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type] \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nconstraint: \\\\\\\"constraint\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nalternative: \\\\\\\"alternative\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" assumption* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nassumption: \\\\\\\"assume\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\ncontract: \\\\\\\"contract\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"book\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" field* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nfield: NAME \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nevent: \\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"(\\\\\\\" [parameters] \\\\\\\")\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"book\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nparameters: NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" type)*\\\\nrule: \\\\\\\"rule\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"for\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"as\\\\\\\" NAME [\\\\\\\"overrides\\\\\\\" NAME (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" NAME)*] \\\\\\\"when\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" rule_statement* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\n?rule_statement: binding | require | post\\\\nrequire: \\\\\\\"require\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\npost: \\\\\\\"post\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" posting+ \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nposting: SIDE NAME expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nscenario: \\\\\\\"scenario\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" setting* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nsetting: \\\\\\\"set\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\nreport: \\\\\\\"report\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"for\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" field* \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nopening: \\\\\\\"opening\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"for\\\\\\\" NAME \\\\\\\"from\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\";\\\\\\\"\\\\ntype: NAME [\\\\\\\"<\\\\\\\" type (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" type)* \\\\\\\">\\\\\\\"]\\\\n?expr: disjunction\\\\n?disjunction: conjunction (OR conjunction)*\\\\n?conjunction: comparison (AND comparison)*\\\\n?comparison: sum [COMPARE sum]\\\\n?sum: product (ADD product)*\\\\n?product: unary (MUL unary)*\\\\n?unary: UNARY unary | postfix\\\\n?postfix: atom (\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\" NAME)*\\\\n?atom: number | STRING | DATE | BOOL | call | NAME | \\\\\\\"(\\\\\\\" expr \\\\\\\")\\\\\\\" | array | record\\\\ncall: NAME \\\\\\\"(\\\\\\\" [expr (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" expr)*] \\\\\\\")\\\\\\\"\\\\nnumber: NUMBER [NAME | \\\\\\\"per\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"year\\\\\\\"]\\\\narray: \\\\\\\"[\\\\\\\" [expr (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" expr)*] \\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\"\\\\nrecord: \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\" [record_field (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\" record_field)*] \\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"\\\\nrecord_field: NAME \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\" expr\\\\nSIDE: \\\\\\\"debit\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"credit\\\\\\\"\\\\nOR: \\\\\\\"or\\\\\\\"\\\\nAND: \\\\\\\"and\\\\\\\"\\\\nUNARY: \\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"not\\\\\\\"\\\\nCOMPARE: \\\\\\\"==\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"!=\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"<=\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\">=\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"<\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\">\\\\\\\"\\\\nADD: \\\\\\\"+\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\"\\\\nMUL: \\\\\\\"*\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"\\\\nBOOL.2: \\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"false\\\\\\\"\\\\nDATE: /@[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}/\\\\nNAME: /[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*/\\\\nNUMBER: /(?:0|[1-9][0-9]*)(?:\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+)?/\\\\nSTRING: /\\\\\\\"(?:[^\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\x00-\\\\\\\\x1f]|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\(?:[\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\/bfnrt]|u[0-9a-fA-F]{4}))*\\\\\\\"/\\\\n%import common.WS\\\\n%ignore WS\\\\n%ignore /\\\\\\\\/\\\\\\\\/[^\\\\\\\\n]*/\\\\n   501 scripts/core_semantics.py\\\\n   407 docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\\\\n   211 scripts/check_semantic_preparation.py\\\\n    56 scripts/build_demo_registry.py\\\\n  2879 docs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json\\\\n  4054 total\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Bounded semantic validator for the authored debt IR; no general compiler.\\\\n\\\\nRejects unsupported populated sections and operations explicitly. External\\\\nexports are frozen data, never executable code or network-loaded dependencies.\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom datetime import date, datetime\\\\nfrom fractions import Fraction\\\\nimport hashlib\\\\nimport json\\\\nimport re\\\\n\\\\nimport jsonschema\\\\n\\\\nfrom build_demo_registry import build as expected_registry, canonical\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass Invalid(Exception):\\\\n    def __init__(self, code, location, detail):\\\\n        self.code, self.location, self.detail = code, location, detail\\\\n        super().__init__(f'{code} at {location}: {detail}')\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef require(condition, code, location, detail):\\\\n    if not condition:\\\\n        raise Invalid(code, location, detail)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef strict_json(text):\\\\n    def pairs(items):\\\\n        out = {}\\\\n        for key, value in items:\\\\n            require(key not in out, 'DuplicateJSONKey', key, 'Duplicate keys lose source information')\\\\n            out[key] = value\\\\n        return out\\\\n    def invalid_constant(value):\\\\n        raise Invalid('InvalidJSONNumber', value, 'Non-finite numbers are not JSON')\\\\n    return json.loads(text, object_pairs_hook=pairs, parse_constant=invalid_constant)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef rational(value, location):\\\\n    n, d = int(value['n']), int(value['d'])\\\\n    require(d > 0, 'InvalidRational', location, 'Positive denominator required')\\\\n    q = Fraction(n, d)\\\\n    require((str(q.numerator), str(q.denominator)) == (value['n'], value['d']),\\\\n            'NoncanonicalRational', location, 'Use reduced terms and zero 0/1')\\\\n    return q\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef iso_date(value, location):\\\\n    try:\\\\n        result = date.fromisoformat(value)\\\\n        require(result.isoformat() == value, 'InvalidDate', location, 'Use YYYY-MM-DD')\\\\n        return result\\\\n    except ValueError as exc:\\\\n        raise Invalid('InvalidDate', location, str(exc)) from exc\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef instant(value, location):\\\\n    try:\\\\n        t = datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace('Z', '+00:00'))\\\\n        require(t.tzinfo is not None, 'MissingTimezone', location, 'Timestamp requires timezone')\\\\n        return t\\\\n    except ValueError as exc:\\\\n        raise Invalid('InvalidTimestamp', location, str(exc)) from exc\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nSUPPORTED = {'models', 'contexts', 'sourceSpans', 'documents', 'observations',\\\\n             'entities', 'books', 'accounts', 'symbols', 'expressions', 'constraints',\\\\n             'assumptions', 'alternatives', 'contracts', 'states', 'packages',\\\\n             'scenarios', 'reviewDecisions', 'evidenceViews', 'modelScopes',\\\\n             'historyFamilies', 'reportMappings'}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass Validator:\\\\n    def __init__(self, document, registry, schema, root):\\\\n        try:\\\\n            jsonschema.Draft202012Validator(schema).validate(document)\\\\n        except jsonschema.ValidationError as exc:\\\\n            raise Invalid('StructuralError', '/'.join(map(str, exc.path)), exc.message) from exc\\\\n        self.doc, self.root, self.nodes, self.kinds = document, root, {}, {}\\\\n        self.external, self.values, self.inferred = {}, {}, {}\\\\n        for section, rows in document.items():\\\\n            if section == 'schema_version':\\\\n                continue\\\\n            require(not rows or section in SUPPORTED, 'UnsupportedSection', section,\\\\n                    'This preparation checker does not validate this populated section')\\\\n            for row in rows:\\\\n                identifier = row['id']\\\\n                require(identifier not in self.nodes, 'DuplicateID', identifier, 'IDs are globally unique')\\\\n                self.nodes[identifier], self.kinds[identifier] = row, section\\\\n        expected = {r['id']: r for r in expected_registry()['records']}\\\\n        require(isinstance(registry, dict) and registry.get('version') == '1' and\\\\n                registry.get('profile') == 'authored-debt-example' and\\\\n                isinstance(registry.get('records'), list), 'UnsupportedRegistry', 'registry',\\\\n                'Expected the versioned authored debt export set')\\\\n        for row in registry['records']:\\\\n            require(isinstance(row, dict) and set(row) == {'id', 'kind', 'artifact', 'sha256', 'pointer', 'value'},\\\\n                    'RegistryShape', 'registry', 'Export has missing or unknown fields')\\\\n            identifier = row['id']\\\\n            require(isinstance(identifier, str) and identifier in expected, 'UnsupportedRegistry', str(identifier),\\\\n                    'Export outside this fixed demonstration profile')\\\\n            template = expected[identifier]\\\\n            require(all(row[k] == template[k] for k in ['kind', 'artifact', 'pointer', 'value']),\\\\n                    'RegistryBinding', identifier, 'Export kind, location or built-in definition differs from this profile')\\\\n            require(identifier not in self.external and identifier not in self.nodes,\\\\n                    'DuplicateID', identifier, 'External and internal exports cannot collide')\\\\n            if row['artifact'] is None:\\\\n                value = row['value']\\\\n                digest = hashlib.sha256(canonical(value)).hexdigest()\\\\n            else:\\\\n                path = (root / row['artifact']).resolve()\\\\n                require(path.is_relative_to(root.resolve()) and path.is_file(),\\\\n                        'MissingArtifact', identifier, 'Expected a retained project file')\\\\n                digest = hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\\\n                value = strict_json(path.read_text())\\\\n                try:\\\\n                    for part in row['pointer'].split('/')[1:]:\\\\n                        part = part.replace('~1', '/').replace('~0', '~')\\\\n                        value = value[int(part)] if isinstance(value, list) else value[part]\\\\n                except (KeyError, ValueError, IndexError, TypeError) as exc:\\\\n                    raise Invalid('MissingExport', identifier, row['pointer']) from exc\\\\n            require(digest == row['sha256'], 'StaleArtifact', identifier, 'Frozen export content differs')\\\\n            self.external[identifier] = row['kind']\\\\n            self.values[identifier] = value\\\\n        require(set(self.external) == set(expected), 'MissingExport', 'registry', 'Incomplete demonstration export set')\\\\n\\\\n    def ref(self, identifier, kinds=None):\\\\n        kind = self.kinds.get(identifier, self.external.get(identifier))\\\\n        require(kind is not None, 'UnknownReference', identifier, 'No frozen export')\\\\n        require(kinds is None or kind in kinds, 'ReferenceKind', identifier, f'Expected {kinds}, got {kind}')\\\\n        return self.nodes.get(identifier, self.values.get(identifier))\\\\n\\\\n    def refs(self, identifiers, kinds=None):\\\\n        require(len(identifiers) == len(set(identifiers)), 'DuplicateReference', str(identifiers), 'Set-valued reference list')\\\\n        return [self.ref(i, kinds) for i in identifiers]\\\\n\\\\n    def time(self, t, where):\\\\n        start = iso_date(t['start'], where)\\\\n        self.ref(t['calendar'], {'Calendar'})\\\\n        if t['kind'] == 'instant':\\\\n            require(t['end_exclusive'] is None, 'InvalidPeriod', where, 'Instant has no end')\\\\n        else:\\\\n            require(t['end_exclusive'] is not None and iso_date(t['end_exclusive'], where) > start,\\\\n                    'InvalidPeriod', where, 'Interval must have a later exclusive end')\\\\n\\\\n    def domain(self, d, where):\\\\n        low = rational(d['lower'], where) if d['lower'] is not None else None\\\\n        high = rational(d['upper'], where) if d['upper'] is not None else None\\\\n        require(low is not None or not d['lower_closed'], 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Unbounded endpoint cannot be closed')\\\\n        require(high is not None or not d['upper_closed'], 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Unbounded endpoint cannot be closed')\\\\n        if d['kind'] == 'missing':\\\\n            require(low is high is None and not d['values'] and d['missing_reason'] is not None,\\\\n                    'InvalidDomain', where, 'Missingness cannot contain a value')\\\\n        else:\\\\n            require(d['missing_reason'] is None, 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Nonmissing domain has no missing reason')\\\\n            if d['kind'] == 'finite':\\\\n                require(low is high is None and bool(d['values']), 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Finite domain needs values only')\\\\n                self.refs(d['values'], {'expressions'})\\\\n            else:\\\\n                require(not d['values'], 'InvalidDomain', where, 'Numeric interval has no finite-value payload')\\\\n                require(low is None or high is None or low < high or\\\\n                        (low == high and d['lower_closed'] and d['upper_closed']),\\\\n                        'InvalidDomain', where, 'Empty/reversed interval')\\\\n                if d['kind'] == 'exact':\\\\n                    require(low is not None and low == high and d['lower_closed'] and d['upper_closed'],\\\\n                            'InvalidDomain', where, 'Exact domain requires equal closed finite bounds')\\\\n        return low, high\\\\n\\\\n    def merge_context(self, contexts, where):\\\\n        ids = [c for c in contexts if c is not None]\\\\n        if not ids:\\\\n            return None\\\\n        keys = ['entity', 'perimeter', 'basis', 'measurement', 'time', 'unit', 'currency', 'dimensions']\\\\n        first = self.ref(ids[0], {'contexts'})\\\\n        for identifier in ids[1:]:\\\\n            other = self.ref(identifier, {'contexts'})\\\\n            require(all(first[k] == other[k] for k in keys), 'ContextMismatch', where,\\\\n                    'Contexts require an explicit compatible mapping')\\\\n        return ids[0]\\\\n\\\\n    def expression(self, identifier, active=()):\\\\n        require(identifier not in active, 'ExpressionCycle', identifier, 'Cyclic expression dependency')\\\\n        if identifier in self.inferred:\\\\n            return self.inferred[identifier]\\\\n        e = self.ref(identifier, {'expressions'})\\\\n        op, target = e['op'], e['target']\\\\n        args = [self.expression(a, active + (identifier,)) for a in e['args']]\\\\n        types = [t for t, _ in args]\\\\n        context = self.merge_context([c for _, c in args], identifier)\\\\n        numeric = lambda t: t in {'Real', 'Int', 'YearFraction', 'Rate<annual_simple>'} or re.fullmatch(r'Money<[A-Z]{3}>', t) is not None\\\\n        require(not e['field_names'], 'UnsupportedExpression', identifier, 'Records/field selection not in this profile')\\\\n        if op == 'literal':\\\\n            require(not args and target is None and ((e['rational'] is None) != (e['text'] is None)),\\\\n                    'ExpressionPayload', identifier, 'One literal payload and no operands/target')\\\\n            result = e['type']\\\\n            if e['rational'] is not None:\\\\n                q = rational(e['rational'], identifier)\\\\n                require(numeric(result), 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Numeric literal has a numeric type')\\\\n                require(result != 'Int' or q.denominator == 1, 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Fractional integer')\\\\n            elif result == 'SourceRef':\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_17\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '190,360p' scripts/core_semantics.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_17\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '190,360p' scripts/core_semantics.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"        numeric = lambda t: t in {'Real', 'Int', 'YearFraction', 'Rate<annual_simple>'} or re.fullmatch(r'Money<[A-Z]{3}>', t) is not None\\\\n        require(not e['field_names'], 'UnsupportedExpression', identifier, 'Records/field selection not in this profile')\\\\n        if op == 'literal':\\\\n            require(not args and target is None and ((e['rational'] is None) != (e['text'] is None)),\\\\n                    'ExpressionPayload', identifier, 'One literal payload and no operands/target')\\\\n            result = e['type']\\\\n            if e['rational'] is not None:\\\\n                q = rational(e['rational'], identifier)\\\\n                require(numeric(result), 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Numeric literal has a numeric type')\\\\n                require(result != 'Int' or q.denominator == 1, 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Fractional integer')\\\\n            elif result == 'SourceRef':\\\\n                self.ref(e['text'], {'SourceRef'})\\\\n            elif result == 'Date':\\\\n                iso_date(e['text'], identifier)\\\\n            else:\\\\n                require(result == 'String' or (result == 'Bool' and e['text'] in {'true', 'false'}),\\\\n                        'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Invalid text literal type')\\\\n            context = e['context']\\\\n        else:\\\\n            require(e['rational'] is None and e['text'] is None, 'ExpressionPayload', identifier, 'Unused literal payload')\\\\n            if op == 'ref':\\\\n                require(not args, 'ArityMismatch', identifier, 'Reference takes no operands')\\\\n                r = self.ref(target, {'symbols', 'observations', 'expressions'})\\\\n                if self.kinds[target] == 'observations':\\\\n                    c = self.ref(r['context'], {'contexts'})\\\\n                    result, context = f'Observation<Money<{c[\\\\\\\"currency\\\\\\\"]}>>', r['context']\\\\n                elif self.kinds[target] == 'symbols':\\\\n                    result, context = r['type'], r['context']\\\\n                else:\\\\n                    result, context = self.expression(target, active + (identifier,))\\\\n            elif op == 'call':\\\\n                self.ref(target, {'Builtin'})\\\\n                require(len(args) == 1, 'ArityMismatch', identifier, 'Supported calls take one argument')\\\\n                if target == 'builtin:value@1':\\\\n                    require(types[0].startswith('Observation<') and types[0].endswith('>'),\\\\n                            'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'value requires an Observation')\\\\n                    result = types[0][12:-1]\\\\n                elif target == 'builtin:constant@1':\\\\n                    result = f'Driver<{types[0]}>'\\\\n                else:\\\\n                    raise Invalid('UnsupportedExpression', identifier, 'Builtin not implemented in this checker')\\\\n            else:\\\\n                require(target is None, 'ExpressionPayload', identifier, 'Operator cannot have target')\\\\n                arity = 1 if op in {'negate', 'not'} else 2\\\\n                require(len(args) == arity, 'ArityMismatch', identifier, 'Wrong operator argument count')\\\\n                if op in {'not', 'and', 'or'}:\\\\n                    require(all(t == 'Bool' for t in types), 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Boolean operands required')\\\\n                    result = 'Bool'\\\\n                elif op in {'eq', 'ne', 'lt', 'le', 'gt', 'ge', 'add', 'subtract'}:\\\\n                    require(types[0] == types[1] and (op in {'eq', 'ne'} or numeric(types[0])),\\\\n                            'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Compatible operand types required')\\\\n                    result = types[0] if op in {'add', 'subtract'} else 'Bool'\\\\n                elif op == 'negate':\\\\n                    require(numeric(types[0]), 'TypeMismatch', identifier, 'Numeric negation required')\\\\n                    result = types[0]\\\\n                else:\\\\n                    raise Invalid('UnsupportedExpression', identifier, op)\\\\n        if context is not None:\\\\n            c = self.ref(context, {'contexts'})\\\\n            m = re.fullmatch(r'Money<([A-Z]{3})>', result)\\\\n            require(not m or c['currency'] == m[1], 'ContextMismatch', identifier, 'Money/context currency mismatch')\\\\n        require((result, context) == (e['type'], e['context']), 'TypeMismatch', identifier,\\\\n                f'Declared {(e[\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\"], e[\\\\\\\"context\\\\\\\"])} but inferred {(result, context)}')\\\\n        self.inferred[identifier] = result, context\\\\n        return result, context\\\\n\\\\n    def bounds(self, identifier):\\\\n        e = self.ref(identifier, {'expressions'})\\\\n        if e['op'] == 'literal' and e['rational'] is not None:\\\\n            q = rational(e['rational'], identifier)\\\\n            return q, q\\\\n        if e['op'] == 'ref' and self.kinds.get(e['target']) in {'observations', 'symbols'}:\\\\n            return self.domain(self.nodes[e['target']]['domain'], identifier)\\\\n        if e['op'] == 'call' and e['target'] in {'builtin:value@1', 'builtin:constant@1'}:\\\\n            return self.bounds(e['args'][0])\\\\n        raise Invalid('UnprovedContractBound', identifier, 'Bound computation unsupported in this profile')\\\\n\\\\n    def assumption(self, expression, scope):\\\\n        require(any(a['expression'] == expression and a['scope'] == scope for a in self.doc['assumptions']),\\\\n                'MissingAssumption', scope + ':' + expression, 'Conditional input lacks assumption provenance')\\\\n\\\\n    def validate(self):\\\\n        d = self.doc\\\\n        reading = self.values['fixture:synthetic-note-7/exact-reading']\\\\n        package_data = self.values['fixture:demo-debt-package.json']\\\\n        horizon = self.values['DemoCalendar@1']['one_year']\\\\n        for key in ['models', 'contexts', 'documents', 'observations', 'entities', 'books', 'accounts',\\\\n                    'symbols', 'contracts', 'states', 'packages', 'scenarios', 'reviewDecisions',\\\\n                    'evidenceViews', 'modelScopes', 'historyFamilies', 'reportMappings']:\\\\n            require(bool(d[key]), 'IncompleteProfile', key, 'Required part of the authored debt example')\\\\n        for entity in d['entities']:\\\\n            require(re.fullmatch(r'[A-Z]{3}', entity['functional_currency']) is not None,\\\\n                    'InvalidCurrency', entity['id'], 'Three uppercase currency letters required')\\\\n        for c in d['contexts']:\\\\n            self.ref(c['entity'], {'entities'}); self.time(c['time'], c['id'])\\\\n            require(c['currency'] is not None and c['unit'] == c['currency'], 'ContextMismatch', c['id'], 'Monetary profile requires currency/unit agreement')\\\\n            require(len({x['axis'] for x in c['dimensions']}) == len(c['dimensions']), 'DuplicateDimension', c['id'], 'One member per axis')\\\\n            require(not c['dimensions'] and c['taxonomy_version'] is None, 'UnsupportedContext', c['id'],\\\\n                    'Taxonomy and dimensional mappings are outside this profile')\\\\n        for doc in d['documents']:\\\\n            instant(doc['available'], doc['id']); instant(doc['ingested'], doc['id'])\\\\n            require(doc['uri'] == 'fixture:demo-debt-package.json#registry/synthetic-note-7', 'UnsupportedSource', doc['id'], 'Only frozen synthetic source is handled')\\\\n            literal = self.values['fixture:synthetic-note-7/exact-reading']['literal']\\\\n            require(doc['sha256'] == hashlib.sha256(literal.encode()).hexdigest(), 'SourceDigestMismatch', doc['id'], 'Synthetic document hashes its literal bytes')\\\\n        for s in d['sourceSpans']:\\\\n            self.ref(s['document'], {'documents'})\\\\n            require(s['literal'] == self.values['fixture:synthetic-note-7/exact-reading']['literal'], 'SourceLiteralMismatch', s['id'], 'Source span differs from frozen reading')\\\\n            require(s['locator'] == 'fixture:registry/synthetic-note-7/literal' and s['extraction'].strip(),\\\\n                    'SourceLocatorMismatch', s['id'], 'Locator and extractor must identify the retained literal')\\\\n        for review in d['reviewDecisions']:\\\\n            self.refs(review['reading_ids'], {'Reading'}); self.refs(review['evidence'], {'sourceSpans'})\\\\n            self.ref(review['prior_view'], {'EvidenceView', 'evidenceViews'}); self.ref(review['new_view'], {'evidenceViews'})\\\\n            instant(review['date'], review['id'])\\\\n            require(review['reviewer'].strip() and review['reason'].strip(), 'MissingReviewReason', review['id'], 'Reviewer and rationale required')\\\\n            require(review['action'] == 'Accept' and not review['invalidated_descendants'],\\\\n                    'UnsupportedReview', review['id'], 'This profile checks initial acceptance, not revision transitions')\\\\n        for o in d['observations']:\\\\n            self.ref(o['context'], {'contexts'}); self.domain(o['domain'], o['id'])\\\\n            self.refs(o['source_spans'], {'sourceSpans'}); self.ref(o['reading'], {'Reading'})\\\\n            r = self.ref(o['review_decision'], {'reviewDecisions'})\\\\n            require(r['action'] == 'Accept' and o['reading'] in r['reading_ids'], 'ObservationNotAccepted', o['id'], 'This profile requires accepted, matching readings')\\\\n            require(not o['supersedes'], 'UnsupportedHistory', o['id'], 'Revision graph checked separately, not in this profile')\\\\n            require(bool(o['source_spans']) and set(o['source_spans']) <= set(r['evidence']),\\\\n                    'AdmissionEvidence', o['id'], 'Acceptance must retain the observation source')\\\\n            c = self.ref(o['context'], {'contexts'})\\\\n            require(all(c[k] == reading[k] for k in ['entity', 'perimeter', 'basis', 'concept', 'currency'])\\\\n                    and c['time']['kind'] == 'instant' and c['time']['start'] == reading['instant']\\\\n                    and c['measurement'] == 'principal', 'ReadingContextMismatch', o['id'],\\\\n                    'Admitted context differs from the frozen authored reading')\\\\n            require(o['domain']['kind'] == 'exact' and self.domain(o['domain'], o['id']) ==\\\\n                    (rational(reading['amount'], o['id']),) * 2, 'ReadingValueMismatch', o['id'],\\\\n                    'Admitted value differs from the frozen authored reading')\\\\n        for v in d['evidenceViews']:\\\\n            require(v['mode'] == 'ExplicitSelection' and not v['conflict_sets'] and not v['transforms'], 'UnsupportedView', v['id'], 'Only explicit nonconflicting fixture views')\\\\n            docs = self.refs(v['documents'], {'documents'}); self.refs(v['decisions'], {'reviewDecisions'})\\\\n            cutoff = instant(v['cutoff'], v['id'])\\\\n            system_cutoff = instant(v['system_as_of'], v['id']) if v['system_as_of'] is not None else None\\\\n            for review in self.refs(v['decisions'], {'reviewDecisions'}):\\\\n                require(review['new_view'] == v['id'], 'ViewMembership', review['id'], 'Decision must produce the selected view')\\\\n                require(system_cutoff is None or instant(review['date'], review['id']) <= system_cutoff,\\\\n                        'FutureReview', review['id'], 'Decision did not yet exist at the system cutoff')\\\\n            for doc in docs:\\\\n                require(instant(doc['available'], doc['id']) <= cutoff, 'FutureEvidence', doc['id'], 'Source unavailable at cutoff')\\\\n                if v['system_as_of'] is not None:\\\\n                    require(instant(doc['ingested'], doc['id']) <= instant(v['system_as_of'], v['id']), 'FutureIngestion', doc['id'], 'Source not yet in database')\\\\n            for o in self.refs(v['observations'], {'observations'}):\\\\n                require(o['review_decision'] in v['decisions'], 'ViewMembership', o['id'], 'Acceptance decision omitted from view')\\\\n                for span in self.refs(o['source_spans'], {'sourceSpans'}):\\\\n                    require(span['document'] in v['documents'], 'ViewMembership', span['id'], 'Observation source omitted from view')\\\\n        for book in d['books']:\\\\n            entity = self.ref(book['entity'], {'entities'}); package = self.ref(book['package'], {'packages'})\\\\n            require(book['currency'] == entity['functional_currency'], 'BookCurrency', book['id'], 'Declared functional currency differs')\\\\n            require(book['basis'] == package['id'], 'PackageBasis', book['id'], 'Demo book uses its dated package ID')\\\\n        for a in d['accounts']:\\\\n            self.ref(a['book'], {'books'})\\\\n            expected = {'Cash': ('Asset', 'cash'), 'Debt': ('Liability', 'debt'),\\\\n                        'InterestExpense': ('Expense', 'interest'), 'Retained': ('Equity', 'retained')}\\\\n            require(a['id'] in expected and (a['role'], a['report_concept']) == expected[a['id']],\\\\n                    'AccountMapping', a['id'], 'Account differs from the frozen statement-template role')\\\\n        for s in d['symbols']:\\\\n            self.domain(s['domain'], s['id']); self.ref(s['scope'], {'models', 'modelScopes'})\\\\n            self.refs(s['dependencies']); self.refs(s['provenance'], {'sourceSpans'})\\\\n            r = self.ref(s['admission'], {'reviewDecisions'})\\\\n            require(s['uncertainty_kind'] == 'HistoricalFact' and r['action'] == 'Accept', 'UnsupportedAdmission', s['id'], 'This profile handles an admitted factual unknown')\\\\n            require(s['id'] == 'alpha' and s['type'] == 'Real' and s['context'] is None and not s['dependencies'],\\\\n                    'UnsupportedSymbol', s['id'], 'Only the independent real fixed-rate fraction is supported')\\\\n            require(s['domain']['kind'] == 'interval' and self.domain(s['domain'], s['id']) == (0, 1)\\\\n                    and s['domain']['lower_closed'] and s['domain']['upper_closed'],\\\\n                    'AdmissionDomain', s['id'], 'Frozen admission specifies the full closed fraction interval')\\\\n            require(bool(s['provenance']) and set(s['provenance']) <= set(r['evidence']),\\\\n                    'AdmissionEvidence', s['id'], 'Unknown admission needs retained evidence')\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_18\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_18\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# AccDSL Core 0 contract, revision 2\\\\n\\\\nNormative companions: `core-0.lark`, `core-ir.schema.json` and\\\\n`../fixtures/demo-debt-package.json`. The authored expected lowering is\\\\n`../fixtures/core-ir-demo.json`; it is not compiler-generated. The LaTeX chapters teach the semantics;\\\\nthese files settle serialisation and the complete demonstration dependency set.\\\\nNo general compiler or product runtime is asserted to exist.\\\\n\\\\nThe supplemental `core-demo-registry.json` freezes the authored debt example's\\\\n17 exports by kind, location and digest. `scripts/core_semantics.py` implements\\\\nbounded static admission for that profile, including references, source-reading\\\\nbindings, types, dates, evidence selection, assumptions, opening state and\\\\npackage/report bindings. `scripts/check_semantic_preparation.py` exercises\\\\npositive variations and schema-valid corruptions. This checker is intentionally\\\\nlimited to the authored monetary debt model and its known registry; other\\\\npopulated IR sections and unsupported operations are rejected. It is not a\\\\ngeneral package loader, source-to-IR compiler, execution engine or coverage\\\\nproof verifier. Its output explicitly leaves coverage claims unverified.\\\\n\\\\n## Lexical and static meaning\\\\n\\\\nInput is UTF-8 with LF or CRLF accepted. Identifiers are ASCII, case-sensitive;\\\\nall literal words in the grammar and `true/false/or/and/not/per/year` are\\\\nreserved. Strings use JSON escaping, reject unpaired surrogates and are NFC\\\\nnormalised for semantic identity; original bytes remain evidence. No exponent,\\\\nthousands separator, percent literal, implicit multiplication or host-language\\\\nescape is supported. Negative numbers use unary minus; decimals become reduced\\\\nrationals directly. Dates must be valid Gregorian dates (the token shape alone\\\\ndoes not validate them). Currency/name suffixes are resolved before typing.\\\\n\\\\nOperators follow grammar precedence, arithmetic associates left, comparisons\\\\ncannot chain, `and/or` are logical connectives over a joint formula. No\\\\nthree-valued source missingness is coerced to Boolean. `not` may recursively\\\\napply to a Boolean/formula; arithmetic sign applies to a numeric expression.\\\\nNo declaration identifier may repeat in a namespace. Imports expose qualified\\\\nexports; short names must resolve uniquely. Fields must exist on the declared\\\\nrecord, argument counts/types must match, no implicit money or calendar cast.\\\\nRecords reject duplicate keys and unknown fields. Arrays are homogeneous unless\\\\ntheir declared type is an explicit tuple. Cyclic let/reference definitions are\\\\nrejected before solver dispatch; event dependencies are checked separately.\\\\n\\\\nThe schema fixes all IR node fields, forbids extra fields and distinguishes\\\\nnullable optional links from empty collections. Every reference resolves in\\\\nthe frozen package/evidence closure. Schema validation precedes semantic\\\\nvalidation: reference kind, acyclic graphs, type compatibility, context\\\\ncompatibility, numeric canonical form, units, rules and capability admission.\\\\nAn enum value permitted by JSON Schema is not evidence that its requested\\\\noperation is implemented. Schemas and semantic rules are jointly normative.\\\\n\\\\nExpression arities are fixed: `literal` and `ref` have no arguments; `negate`,\\\\n`not` and `field` have one; arithmetic, comparison, `and` and `or` have two.\\\\nA `call` matches its registered signature. `array` has its declared element\\\\ntype and any permitted length; `record` has one argument per distinct\\\\n`field_names` entry, in that order. A literal has exactly one rational or text\\\\npayload consistent with its type; a reference has a target ID; a field has its\\\\nfield name in `text`; a call has a qualified function ID in `target`. Unused\\\\npayload fields are null and unused `field_names` is empty. Arithmetic and\\\\nordering require compatible numeric types/contexts; equality requires matching\\\\ntypes; logical operators require Boolean values or Boolean formulas. Field\\\\nselection and record construction use the registered record type. No schema\\\\nsuccess bypasses these semantic checks.\\\\n\\\\nExternal identifiers such as `builtin:Core0@1`, `DemoCalendar@1`, package\\\\noperations and `fixture:` reading/view/witness IDs resolve through a frozen\\\\nregistry with declared kinds, versions and content digests. The demonstration\\\\npackage describes these exports and its calendar periods. They are not all\\\\nembedded as top-level IR nodes. The frozen demonstration registry and bounded\\\\nsemantic checker validate these specific bindings; general registry resolution\\\\nand compiler validation remain implementation obligations. A missing export is an error,\\\\nnot authority to invent a value or load mutable network content.\\\\n\\\\nSourceSpan locators use `pdf:<1-based-page>:<x0>,<y0>,<x1>,<y1>` with PDF\\\\npoints from the top-left of the rotated visible page, or `html:<element-id>`\\\\nwith a retained node ordinal fallback in the frozen parse. A text-extract\\\\ncharacter range is a derived locator and retains the extractor version; it\\\\ndoes not pretend to be an original page bounding box. Monetary Context has\\\\nnon-null currency and a compatible unit. Posting amount is nonnegative in the\\\\nbook's functional currency; optional original_quantity/original_unit retain\\\\nforeign money or commodities and require a valuation when converted.\\\\nJournal assumptions and accrual_period preserve the measurement's conditions\\\\nseparately from its cash posting date. The schema's nullable fields are always\\\\npresent; null is permitted only under these stated semantic conditions.\\\\n\\\\nA decimal `100 USD` lowers to `literal` with rational `{n:\\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",d:\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"}`,\\\\ntype `Money<USD>` and no hidden scale multiplier. `alpha` lowers to a `ref` to\\\\nthe same symbol ID on every use. `0.05 per year` has type `Rate<annual_simple>`.\\\\nSource references and origin offsets are kept in the evidence binding, outside\\\\nthe semantic expression digest. A program with source observations cannot run\\\\nuntil its evidence registry and accepted review decisions are supplied.\\\\n\\\\nSource symbol-domain intervals are closed; strict bounds use explicit\\\\nconstraints. Choice members resolve within their choice namespace. The\\\\nsurface syntax has no unbounded loops, recursion, dynamic code evaluation or\\\\nhost calls; finite schedules/collections come from typed packages. Report\\\\nfields bind supported mapping expressions and cannot override recognition.\\\\nEvery assumption constraint or conditional model input has an Assumption\\\\nrecord carrying its expression, scope, rationale, origin, evidence, validity\\\\nperiod, information cutoff and role (Baseline, Hypothesis, Convenience or\\\\nReviewedDefault). An authored baseline is not automatically a reviewed\\\\ndefault. Conditional example endpoints are hypotheses, not inferred facts.\\\\nThe debt example also records its assumed initial 5% component rates and 7%\\\\nstress driver as assumptions. The integer contract-slot limit has its own\\\\n`Int` literal; it does not reuse the `Real` literal in the fraction comparison.\\\\n\\\\n## Exact values, contexts and built-ins\\\\n\\\\nRationals use base-10 signed numerator strings and positive denominator strings,\\\\nlowest terms; zero is `0/1`. Money adds only within one currency and compatible\\\\ncontext. Real times money is money; rate times money must also supply a\\\\nYearFraction through `simpleInterest`. Rate alone is not a dimensionless Real.\\\\nNo rate basis is implicitly coerced. The demonstration's accrual rule uses\\\\n`simpleInterest(principal,rate,fraction)` explicitly. Integer counts stay integer.\\\\nDivision by a symbolic value\\\\nrequires nonzero proof and is outside the rational-linear solver fragment.\\\\n\\\\nContext equality compares entity, perimeter version, measurement basis,\\\\ncurrency/unit, instant/period/calendar and dimensions. A sum may discard a\\\\ndimension only through a valid partition mapping. Reference fields and source\\\\nspans may differ without changing financial comparability. Observation\\\\nprecision is a domain, not a tolerance argument. Unknown rounding convention\\\\nis an unresolved reading, not an assumed half-unit interval.\\\\n\\\\nDomain `display` preserves the disclosed spelling, unit/scale and sign when\\\\navailable; `rounding_rule` identifies the declared convention or is null for\\\\nan unrounded mathematical symbol. The SourceSpan retains the original text.\\\\nAn exact numeric domain has equal closed bounds; an interval has ordered bounds\\\\nand explicit endpoint inclusion (a null endpoint is unbounded and open).\\\\nFinite-domain `values` are distinct typed expression IDs and use null bounds.\\\\nA missing domain has null bounds, no values, and a non-null `missing_reason`;\\\\nother domain kinds have null `missing_reason`. Empty or contradictory admitted\\\\ndomains return an explicit consistency error. Display text alone never supplies\\\\nan unknown rounding convention.\\\\n\\\\nThe complete built-in set is:\\\\n\\\\n| Name | Signature and effect |\\\\n| --- | --- |\\\\n| external | String -> SourceRef; resolves a frozen registry key; never fetches network content during evaluation |\\\\n| value | Observation<T> -> contextual T or shared constrained Symbol<T>; missing raises MissingEvidence |\\\\n| constant | T -> dated exogenous Driver<T>, all dates in the explicit scenario horizon |\\\\n| simpleInterest | Money<C>, Rate<annual_simple>, YearFraction -> Money<C>, exact product; symbolic classification happens after expansion |\\\\n| yearFraction | start, end, CalendarRef, ConventionRef -> YearFraction; supported conventions `one_year` and `half_year_fixture` require exact named periods; others require a registered calculator |\\\\n| currencyScale | CurrencyRef -> Int from the frozen currency registry, USD=2 in demonstration |\\\\n| roundMoney | Money<C>, Int, String -> Money<C>; only half_even supported in DemoDebt; rounding at posting boundary, rational ties exact |\\\\n| sumOver | PartitionRef, array of contextual T -> contextual T with that dimension removed; disjoint/exhaustive population proof required |\\\\n| convert | Money<C1>, Measurement<Rate<C2/C1>> -> Money<C2>; valuation date and purpose must match, source amount retained |\\\\n| balance | StateRef, AccountRef -> signed Money<C>; read-only committed state at information date |\\\\n\\\\nAll other functions must have a package-registered pure signature and versioned\\\\nimplementation digest; their capability is explicit. Rules may bind values,\\\\ncheck requirements and propose postings. They cannot sample, mutate state or\\\\naccess I/O. Contract and behaviour plugins produce proposed events/state\\\\nchanges through the typed interfaces below. Zero-posting contract changes need\\\\nan explicit non-recognition operation.\\\\n\\\\n## Reconstruction model and finite coverage\\\\n\\\\nA ModelScope lists templates, slots per entity/period, books, account roles,\\\\ntiming/calendar resolution, allowed choices, bounds, and forbidden/unsupported\\\\noperations. A slot is a possible aggregate event, with an active flag and\\\\nnonnegative amount; inactive implies zero. A template declares both its posting\\\\nincidence vector and economic-state change. Sales and collections are different\\\\nslots; issue and reset are different slots. Debt states retain F/V, rates,\\\\nreset calendar, maturity and hedge links even when historical incidence agrees.\\\\n\\\\nInstantiate every declared slot once, then share variables by economic IDs and\\\\nobservation IDs. Compile roll-forwards and report mappings into constraints;\\\\nadd each accepted evidence domain once. Match source observations by exact\\\\ncontext/mapping, never by label similarity. Attach source/assumption IDs to\\\\nconstraints. Branch on finite choices only, with mutually exclusive guards;\\\\ncontinuous families remain formulas. Count completed, infeasible and unresolved\\\\nchoice cells. `ExactWithinScope` requires every cell decided and each matching\\\\nsource obligation resolved or explicitly outside simulation scope. A satisfied\\\\nwitness alone does not establish coverage. Real-world completeness is never\\\\ninferred from this finite result.\\\\n\\\\nSupported solver fragment: rational linear equalities/inequalities, strict\\\\nbounds, finite enums and Boolean combinations lowered to finite disjunctions.\\\\nMoney quantisation either occurs after continuous analysis or uses integer\\\\nminor-unit variables with a separately declared bounded integer solver. Integer\\\\nand nonlinear constraints may not be silently submitted as continuous LPs.\\\\nUnknown-by-unknown products, symbolic discount rates/exponents, arbitrary\\\\nfunctions and unbounded integer search return UnsupportedFragment/Unknown.\\\\nFixed proportions times known totals are linear; variable F,V with F+V=D is\\\\nlinear even when D is rounded. A fixed constraint F/D >= a with known a and\\\\nproved D>0 becomes F>=aD; an unknown a restores bilinearity.\\\\n\\\\nFeasibility results are sat+exact witness, unsat+constraint/source core or\\\\nunknown+reason+undecided formula. Bounds include lower/upper rational value,\\\\nattainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\\\\ninequalities require infimum/supremum semantics. An unbounded result is neither\\\\nunknown nor a finite extreme. Resource budgets are explicit request fields;\\\\ntimeout preserves undecided cells rather than deleting them.\\\\n\\\\n## Temporal selection and local review\\\\n\\\\nAn EvidenceView first filters by availability cutoff and (if requested)\\\\ningestion cutoff. Day-only availability maps to the next local midnight using\\\\nthe named timezone; finer availability requires evidence. Selective explicit\\\\nsupersession removes only the targeted assertions in the same context. A\\\\nsuperseding assertion must be eligible itself. Transitive successors follow\\\\nthe acyclic supersession graph. Competing maximal assertions form a conflict\\\\nset, never a last-row-wins result. Original view chooses initial assertions in\\\\neach chain from a declared filing, not arbitrary earliest ingestion. A filing\\\\nwith no prior version supplies its original itself. Harmonisation derives new\\\\nobservations, preserves originals and records all transformation rules.\\\\n\\\\nIntervals are [start,end_exclusive) in a calendar; balance instants refer to\\\\nthe end-of-day boundary. Cumulative subtraction requires same start, nested\\\\nend, units/basis/perimeter and revision group, or an explicit compatibility\\\\nassertion supported by review. A restatement of one flow does not restate every\\\\nnote. Prospective estimate changes affect events from their effective date;\\\\nretrospective corrections generate a new view and an explicit opening bridge.\\\\n\\\\nReview states are Proposed, Accepted, AcceptedAlternative, Rejected and\\\\nSuperseded. Accept requires verified locator/literal, context, rationale,\\\\nreviewer/date, applicability checks and a reconciliation result. Acceptance\\\\nof an extraction is separate from acceptance of an accounting interpretation.\\\\nSeveral accepted alternatives need a choice group. Reject never deletes source\\\\nbytes. Correction creates a new reading linked to the old one; replacing an\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_19\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '360,520p' scripts/core_semantics.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_19\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '360,520p' scripts/core_semantics.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"                    'AdmissionEvidence', s['id'], 'Unknown admission needs retained evidence')\\\\n        for e in d['expressions']:\\\\n            self.expression(e['id'])\\\\n        for a in d['assumptions']:\\\\n            self.expression(a['expression']); self.ref(a['scope'], {'alternatives', 'models', 'scenarios', 'contracts'})\\\\n            self.time(a['valid'], a['id']); instant(a['information_cutoff'], a['id']); self.refs(a['source_refs'])\\\\n            require(bool(a['rationale'].strip()), 'MissingAssumptionReason', a['id'], 'Rationale required')\\\\n            require(a['role'] != 'ReviewedDefault', 'UnprovedDefaultReview', a['id'], 'No reviewed-default evidence in this profile')\\\\n            require(a['valid']['kind'] == 'interval' and a['valid']['start'] <= horizon[0]\\\\n                    and a['valid']['end_exclusive'] >= horizon[1], 'AssumptionValidity', a['id'],\\\\n                    'Example assumptions must cover the full named scenario period')\\\\n            require(all(instant(a['information_cutoff'], a['id']) <= instant(v['cutoff'], v['id'])\\\\n                        for v in d['evidenceViews']), 'FutureAssumption', a['id'],\\\\n                    'Assumption information cutoff exceeds the example evidence view')\\\\n        for c in d['constraints']:\\\\n            require(self.expression(c['expression'])[0] == 'Bool', 'ConstraintType', c['id'], 'Constraint must be Boolean')\\\\n            self.ref(c['scope']); self.refs(c['source_refs'])\\\\n            if c['kind'] == 'assumption':\\\\n                self.assumption(c['expression'], c['scope'])\\\\n            else:\\\\n                raise Invalid('UnsupportedConstraint', c['id'], 'Only named assumption constraints in this profile')\\\\n        for a in d['alternatives']:\\\\n            self.ref(a['parent'], {'historyFamilies'}); self.ref(a['scope'], {'modelScopes'})\\\\n            self.refs(a['constraints'], {'constraints'}); self.refs(a['evidence'], {'sourceSpans'}); self.refs(a['opposing_evidence'], {'sourceSpans'})\\\\n            require(a['choice_group'] is None, 'UnsupportedChoice', a['id'], 'Named conditional views only')\\\\n            require(a['author'].strip() and a['reason'].strip(), 'MissingAlternativeReason', a['id'], 'Author and reason required')\\\\n            instant(a['created_at'], a['id'])\\\\n            require(bool(a['constraints']) and all(self.nodes[c]['scope'] == a['id'] for c in a['constraints']),\\\\n                    'AlternativeScope', a['id'], 'Alternative constraints must belong to that alternative')\\\\n            require(self.nodes[a['parent']]['scope'] == a['scope'], 'AlternativeScope', a['id'], 'Family and alternative scope differ')\\\\n        for p in d['packages']:\\\\n            path = self.root / 'docs/design/fixtures/demo-debt-package.json'\\\\n            require(p['id'] == 'DemoDebt@1' and p['version'] == '1', 'UnsupportedPackage', p['id'], 'Debt profile only')\\\\n            require(hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest() == p['digest'], 'PackageDigestMismatch', p['id'], 'Package lock differs from bytes')\\\\n            self.time(p['effective'], p['id']); self.refs(p['operations'], {'Operation'})\\\\n            self.refs(p['dependencies'], {'Library', 'Calendar'}); self.refs(p['authority'], {'SourceRef'})\\\\n            require(p['review_status'] == 'illustrative', 'UnprovedDomainReview', p['id'], 'No domain-review evidence supplied')\\\\n            require(p['basis'] == 'DemoDebt' and p['implementation'] is None and not p['extension_points'],\\\\n                    'UnsupportedPackage', p['id'], 'No executable package or overrides validated here')\\\\n            require(set(p['operations']) == {'DemoDebt@1/' + n for n in ['reset', 'accrue_and_pay', 'close', 'statements']},\\\\n                    'PackageOperations', p['id'], 'All demonstration operations required')\\\\n            require(p['effective']['kind'] == 'interval' and p['effective']['start'] <= horizon[0]\\\\n                    and p['effective']['end_exclusive'] >= horizon[1], 'PackageValidity', p['id'], 'Package must apply over the scenario period')\\\\n        for c in d['contracts']:\\\\n            self.ref(c['type'], {'ContractType'}); book = self.ref(c['book'], {'books'})\\\\n            require(c['package'] == book['package'], 'PackageBasis', c['id'], 'Contract and book package differ')\\\\n            self.refs(c['source_refs'], {'sourceSpans'})\\\\n            fields = {f['name']: f['expression'] for f in c['fields']}\\\\n            required = {'principal': f'Money<{book[\\\\\\\"currency\\\\\\\"]}>', 'fixed_fraction': 'Real', 'fixed_rate': 'Rate<annual_simple>', 'initial_floating_rate': 'Rate<annual_simple>'}\\\\n            require(len(fields) == len(c['fields']) and fields.keys() == required.keys(), 'ContractFields', c['id'], 'Wrong or repeated contract fields')\\\\n            for name, expected in required.items():\\\\n                require(self.expression(fields[name])[0] == expected, 'ContractType', c['id'] + '.' + name, expected)\\\\n                context = self.expression(fields[name])[1]\\\\n                if context is not None:\\\\n                    ctx = self.nodes[context]\\\\n                    require(ctx['entity'] == book['entity'] and ctx['basis'] == book['basis'],\\\\n                            'ContractContext', c['id'], 'Contract input belongs to another entity or basis')\\\\n                low, high = self.bounds(fields[name])\\\\n                require(low is not None and low >= 0 and (name != 'fixed_fraction' or (high is not None and high <= 1)), 'ContractDomain', name, 'Nonnegative amounts/rates and share in [0,1] required')\\\\n                if name in {'fixed_rate', 'initial_floating_rate'}:\\\\n                    self.assumption(fields[name], c['id'])\\\\n        for s in d['states']:\\\\n            self.ref(s['book'], {'books'}); iso_date(s['date'], s['id'])\\\\n            seen = set(); total = Fraction(0)\\\\n            for b in s['balances']:\\\\n                a = self.ref(b['account'], {'accounts'})\\\\n                require(a['book'] == s['book'], 'StateBook', s['id'], 'Balance belongs to another book')\\\\n                require(a['id'] not in seen, 'DuplicateBalance', s['id'], a['id']); seen.add(a['id'])\\\\n                total += rational(b['signed_amount'], s['id'])\\\\n            require(total == 0, 'UnbalancedState', s['id'], 'Signed opening balances must sum to zero')\\\\n            require(seen == {a['id'] for a in d['accounts'] if a['book'] == s['book']}, 'IncompleteState', s['id'], 'This fixture requires explicit zero balances too')\\\\n            self.refs(s['contracts'], {'contracts'}); self.refs(s['dependencies'])\\\\n            require(not s['measurements'], 'UnsupportedState', s['id'], 'Measurement state not validated in this profile')\\\\n            require(all(self.nodes[c]['book'] == s['book'] for c in s['contracts']),\\\\n                    'StateBook', s['id'], 'Active contract belongs to another book')\\\\n            opening = package_data['registry']['after-2025-close']\\\\n            require(s['book'] == opening['book'] and s['date'] == opening['date'] and\\\\n                    set(s['contracts']) == set(opening['contracts']) and\\\\n                    {b['account']: rational(b['signed_amount'], s['id']) for b in s['balances']} ==\\\\n                    {a: Fraction(v) for a, v in opening['signed_balances'].items()},\\\\n                    'OpeningStateMismatch', s['id'], 'Balanced state differs from the frozen authored opening')\\\\n        for s in d['scenarios']:\\\\n            require(s['kind'] == 'ExogenousStress' and s['probability_model'] is None and s['observed_event'] is None and s['structural_model'] is None and not s['replaced_equations'], 'UnsupportedScenario', s['id'], 'Exogenous debt stress only')\\\\n            require(len(s['drivers']) == 1 and s['drivers'][0]['name'] == 'market_rate', 'ScenarioDrivers', s['id'], 'Expected market_rate')\\\\n            require(self.expression(s['drivers'][0]['expression'])[0] == 'Driver<Rate<annual_simple>>', 'TypeMismatch', s['id'], 'Rate driver required')\\\\n            self.assumption(s['drivers'][0]['expression'], s['id'])\\\\n            low, _ = self.bounds(s['drivers'][0]['expression'])\\\\n            require(low is not None and low >= 0, 'ContractDomain', s['id'], 'DemoDebt rejects a negative reset rate')\\\\n        for scope in d['modelScopes']:\\\\n            self.refs(scope['templates'], {'ContractType'}); self.refs(scope['calendars'], {'Calendar'})\\\\n            require(not scope['choices'] and not scope['obligations'], 'UnsupportedScope', scope['id'], 'Additional structural choices/obligations need a fuller checker')\\\\n            require(len(scope['slot_limits']) == 1, 'SlotLimit', scope['id'], 'One concrete debt slot limit required')\\\\n            for slot in scope['slot_limits']:\\\\n                require(self.expression(slot['expression'])[0] == 'Int', 'SlotLimitType', scope['id'], 'Slot limit is an integer, not an implicit Real cast')\\\\n                low, high = self.bounds(slot['expression'])\\\\n                require(low == high and low is not None and low >= 0 and slot['name'] == 'debt_contracts' and len(d['contracts']) <= low, 'SlotLimit', scope['id'], 'Concrete nonnegative capacity required')\\\\n        for f in d['historyFamilies']:\\\\n            for key, kind in [('scope', 'modelScopes'), ('evidence_view', 'evidenceViews'), ('opening_state', 'states')]:\\\\n                self.ref(f[key], {kind})\\\\n            for key, kind in [('symbols', 'symbols'), ('constraints', 'constraints'), ('alternatives', 'alternatives')]:\\\\n                self.refs(f[key], {kind})\\\\n            self.refs(f['witnesses'], {'Witness'}); self.refs(f['solver_results'], {'ReferenceResult'})\\\\n            view = self.nodes[f['evidence_view']]\\\\n            require(all(o['id'] in view['observations'] for o in d['observations']) and\\\\n                    all(s['admission'] in view['decisions'] for s in d['symbols']),\\\\n                    'ViewMembership', f['id'], 'All evidence used by this bounded family must be selected')\\\\n            require(set(f['symbols']) == {s['id'] for s in d['symbols']} and\\\\n                    set(f['alternatives']) == {a['id'] for a in d['alternatives'] if a['parent'] == f['id']},\\\\n                    'FamilyMembership', f['id'], 'Family omits an authored symbol or conditional alternative')\\\\n            require(not f['choices'], 'UnsupportedChoice', f['id'], 'Finite structural cells not implemented here')\\\\n            require(f['coverage'] != 'ExactWithinScope' or f['unresolved_cells'] == 0, 'FalseCoverage', f['id'], 'Exact coverage cannot contain unknown cells')\\\\n            require(f['coverage'] != 'ExactWithinScope' or (f['completed_cells'] > 0 and f['solver_results']),\\\\n                    'FalseCoverage', f['id'], 'Exact label needs completed cells and result references; this is not proof verification')\\\\n            require(f['feasibility'] != 'Feasible' or bool(f['witnesses']), 'MissingWitness', f['id'], 'Feasible label requires a witness reference')\\\\n        for r in d['reportMappings']:\\\\n            b = self.ref(r['book'], {'books'})\\\\n            require(r['basis'] == b['basis'], 'PackageBasis', r['id'], 'Report and book bases differ')\\\\n            self.ref(r['closing_policy'], {'Operation'}); self.ref(r['cash_flow_policy'], {'CashFlowPolicy'})\\\\n            self.refs(r['required_operations'], {'Operation'})\\\\n            require(r['closing_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/close' and r['cash_flow_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/interest_operating'\\\\n                    and r['required_operations'] == ['DemoDebt@1/accrue_and_pay'], 'ReportPolicy', r['id'],\\\\n                    'Wrong policy binding for the frozen report template')\\\\n            require(len(r['rows']) == 1 and r['rows'][0]['name'] == 'package_mapping', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'One frozen template binding required')\\\\n            for row in r['rows']:\\\\n                require(self.expression(row['expression'])[0] == 'SourceRef', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'This profile binds a frozen report template')\\\\n                e = self.nodes[row['expression']]\\\\n                require(e['op'] == 'literal' and e['text'] == 'DemoDebt.statements.v1', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'Expected the statement mapping export')\\\\n        for m in d['models']:\\\\n            self.refs(m['declarations']); self.refs(m['package_lock'], {'packages'}); self.ref(m['scope'], {'modelScopes'})\\\\n            require(m['language_version'] == 'Core0.1', 'UnsupportedLanguage', m['id'], 'Core0.1 only')\\\\n            required = {r['id'] for section in ['entities', 'books', 'accounts', 'observations', 'symbols',\\\\n                        'contracts', 'alternatives', 'scenarios', 'reportMappings', 'states'] for r in d[section]}\\\\n            require(required <= set(m['declarations']) and set(m['package_lock']) == {p['id'] for p in d['packages']},\\\\n                    'ModelMembership', m['id'], 'Model omits an authored declaration or package lock')\\\\n        return {'status': 'passed', 'profile': 'authored-debt-example',\\\\n                'internal_records': len(self.nodes), 'external_exports': len(self.external),\\\\n                'coverage_claims_verified': False,\\\\n                'limits': 'Bounded static admission only; no general compiler, runtime, accounting certification or proof of historical coverage.'}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef validate(document, registry, schema, root):\\\\n    return Validator(document, registry, schema, root).validate()\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_20\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"cat scripts/build_demo_registry.py; sed -n '1,145p' scripts/check_semantic_preparation.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_20\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"cat scripts/build_demo_registry.py; sed -n '1,145p' scripts/check_semantic_preparation.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Freeze the external exports needed by the authored debt IR example.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nimport hashlib\\\\nimport json\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\n\\\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\\\nFIX = ROOT / 'docs/design/fixtures'\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef canonical(value):\\\\n    return json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'),\\\\n                      ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef build():\\\\n    records = []\\\\n\\\\n    def inline(identifier, kind, value):\\\\n        records.append(dict(id=identifier, kind=kind, value=value,\\\\n                            sha256=hashlib.sha256(canonical(value)).hexdigest(),\\\\n                            artifact=None, pointer=None))\\\\n\\\\n    def bound(identifier, kind, filename, pointer):\\\\n        p = FIX / filename\\\\n        records.append(dict(id=identifier, kind=kind, artifact=str(p.relative_to(ROOT)),\\\\n                            sha256=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\\\\n                            pointer=pointer, value=None))\\\\n\\\\n    inline('builtin:Core0@1', 'Library', {'version': '0.1', 'pure': True})\\\\n    inline('builtin:value@1', 'Builtin', {'arguments': ['Observation<T>'], 'result': 'T'})\\\\n    inline('builtin:constant@1', 'Builtin', {'arguments': ['T'], 'result': 'Driver<T>'})\\\\n    inline('DemoCalendar@1', 'Calendar', {'calendar': 'Gregorian',\\\\n           'one_year': ['2026-01-01', '2027-01-01'], 'instant': 'end_of_day'})\\\\n    inline('fixture:empty-view', 'EvidenceView', {'documents': [], 'observations': [], 'decisions': []})\\\\n    for value in [0, 1]:\\\\n        inline(f'fixture:alpha={value}', 'Witness', {'alpha': {'n': str(value), 'd': '1'}})\\\\n    package = 'demo-debt-package.json'\\\\n    bound('fixture:demo-debt-package.json', 'SourceRef', package, '')\\\\n    bound('fixture:synthetic-note-7/exact-reading', 'Reading', package, '/registry/synthetic-note-7')\\\\n    bound('DemoDebt@1/DebtMix', 'ContractType', package, '/DebtMix')\\\\n    for index, name in enumerate(['reset', 'accrue_and_pay', 'close']):\\\\n        bound('DemoDebt@1/' + name, 'Operation', package, f'/DebtMix/operations/{index}')\\\\n    bound('DemoDebt@1/statements', 'Operation', package, '/registry/DemoDebt.statements.v1')\\\\n    bound('DemoDebt@1/interest_operating', 'CashFlowPolicy', package,\\\\n          '/registry/DemoDebt.statements.v1/cash_flow')\\\\n    bound('DemoDebt.statements.v1', 'SourceRef', package, '/registry/DemoDebt.statements.v1')\\\\n    bound('fixture:borrowings.json#exact', 'ReferenceResult', 'borrowings.json', '/exact')\\\\n    return {'version': '1', 'profile': 'authored-debt-example', 'records': records,\\\\n            'limits': 'Frozen example exports; not a general package loader or executed third-party integration.'}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nif __name__ == '__main__':\\\\n    p = FIX / 'core-demo-registry.json'\\\\n    p.write_text(json.dumps(build(), indent=2) + '\\\\\\\\n')\\\\n    print(p.relative_to(ROOT))\\\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Challenge the bounded debt validator using schema-valid semantic defects.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\\\nimport hashlib\\\\nimport json\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nimport time\\\\n\\\\nimport jsonschema\\\\n\\\\nfrom core_semantics import Invalid, strict_json, validate\\\\n\\\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\\\nD = ROOT / 'docs/design'\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef main():\\\\n    started = time.monotonic()\\\\n    inputs = [D/'fixtures/core-ir-demo.json', D/'fixtures/core-demo-registry.json',\\\\n              D/'spec/core-ir.schema.json']\\\\n    document, registry, schema = [strict_json(p.read_text()) for p in inputs]\\\\n    jsonschema.Draft202012Validator.check_schema(schema)\\\\n    structural = jsonschema.Draft202012Validator(schema)\\\\n    checks = []\\\\n\\\\n    def node(d, section, identifier):\\\\n        return next(r for r in d[section] if r['id'] == identifier)\\\\n\\\\n    def field(section, identifier, key, value):\\\\n        return lambda d, r: node(d, section, identifier).__setitem__(key, value)\\\\n\\\\n    def negative(name, expected, change):\\\\n        d, r = deepcopy(document), deepcopy(registry)\\\\n        change(d, r)\\\\n        structural.validate(d)  # A structural failure must not masquerade as a semantic test.\\\\n        try:\\\\n            validate(d, r, schema, ROOT)\\\\n        except Invalid as exc:\\\\n            if exc.code != expected:\\\\n                raise AssertionError(f'{name}: expected {expected}, got {exc}') from exc\\\\n            checks.append(dict(name=name, kind='schema_valid_negative', expected=expected,\\\\n                               observed=exc.code, location=exc.location, passed=True))\\\\n        else:\\\\n            raise AssertionError(f'{name}: invalid input was accepted')\\\\n\\\\n    def positive(name, change=lambda d, r: None):\\\\n        d, r = deepcopy(document), deepcopy(registry)\\\\n        change(d, r)\\\\n        result = validate(d, r, schema, ROOT)\\\\n        assert result['status'] == 'passed' and not result['coverage_claims_verified']\\\\n        checks.append(dict(name=name, kind='positive', passed=True, result=result))\\\\n\\\\n    positive('authored_fixture')\\\\n\\\\n    def reorder(d, r):\\\\n        for values in d.values():\\\\n            if isinstance(values, list):\\\\n                values.reverse()\\\\n        r['records'].reverse()\\\\n\\\\n    positive('record_and_export_order_independent', reorder)\\\\n    positive('system_cutoff_at_exact_availability',\\\\n             field('evidenceViews', 'synthetic-2025-exact', 'system_as_of', '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'))\\\\n    positive('equivalent_offset_timestamp',\\\\n             field('documents', 'synthetic-note-document', 'available', '2025-12-31T19:00:00-05:00'))\\\\n\\\\n    def other_stress(d, r):\\\\n        node(d, 'expressions', 'rate.stress')['rational'] = dict(n='9', d='100')\\\\n        node(d, 'assumptions', 'admission.rateShock')['rationale'] = 'Illustrative 9% constant annual simple stress'\\\\n\\\\n    positive('another_documented_nonnegative_stress', other_stress)\\\\n\\\\n    negative('original_real_slot_limit', 'SlotLimitType',\\\\n             lambda d, r: d['modelScopes'][0]['slot_limits'][0].__setitem__('expression', 'one'))\\\\n    negative('unknown_reference', 'UnknownReference', field('expressions', 'alpha.ref', 'target', 'absent'))\\\\n    negative('wrong_reference_kind', 'ReferenceKind', field('expressions', 'alpha.ref', 'target', 'Local'))\\\\n    negative('duplicate_identifier', 'DuplicateID', lambda d, r: d['accounts'].append(deepcopy(d['accounts'][0])))\\\\n    negative('expression_self_cycle', 'ExpressionCycle', field('expressions', 'alpha.ref', 'target', 'alpha.ref'))\\\\n    negative('comparison_missing_operand', 'ArityMismatch', field('expressions', 'is.fixed', 'args', ['alpha.ref']))\\\\n    negative('unused_literal_payload', 'ExpressionPayload', field('expressions', 'is.fixed', 'text', 'extra'))\\\\n    negative('implicit_money_cast', 'ContractType', field('expressions', 'rate.fixed', 'type', 'Money<USD>'))\\\\n    negative('declared_currency_disagrees_with_context', 'TypeMismatch', field('expressions', 'debt.value', 'type', 'Money<EUR>'))\\\\n    negative('fractional_slot_count', 'TypeMismatch', field('expressions', 'slot.one', 'rational', dict(n='1', d='2')))\\\\n    negative('unreduced_rational', 'NoncanonicalRational', field('expressions', 'rate.fixed', 'rational', dict(n='2', d='40')))\\\\n    negative('negative_zero', 'NoncanonicalRational', field('expressions', 'zero', 'rational', dict(n='-0', d='1')))\\\\n    negative('impossible_gregorian_date', 'InvalidDate',\\\\n             lambda d, r: d['contexts'][0]['time'].__setitem__('start', '2025-02-30'))\\\\n    negative('empty_period', 'InvalidPeriod',\\\\n             lambda d, r: d['assumptions'][0]['valid'].__setitem__('end_exclusive', '2026-01-01'))\\\\n    negative('timezone_missing', 'MissingTimezone', field('documents', 'synthetic-note-document', 'available', '2026-01-01T00:00:00'))\\\\n    negative('reversed_domain', 'InvalidDomain', lambda d, r: d['symbols'][0]['domain'].__setitem__('lower', dict(n='2', d='1')))\\\\n    negative('empty_open_interval', 'InvalidDomain',\\\\n             lambda d, r: d['symbols'][0]['domain'].update(upper=dict(n='0', d='1'), lower_closed=False))\\\\n    negative('invented_admitted_value', 'ReadingValueMismatch',\\\\n             lambda d, r: d['observations'][0]['domain'].update(lower=dict(n='101', d='1'), upper=dict(n='101', d='1')))\\\\n    negative('invented_source_context', 'ReadingContextMismatch', field('contexts', 'debt-context', 'perimeter', 'OtherGroup'))\\\\n    negative('changed_source_literal', 'SourceLiteralMismatch', field('sourceSpans', 'synthetic-note-7', 'literal', 'Debt 101'))\\\\n    negative('changed_source_digest', 'SourceDigestMismatch', field('documents', 'synthetic-note-document', 'sha256', '0' * 64))\\\\n    negative('source_locator_mismatch', 'SourceLocatorMismatch', field('sourceSpans', 'synthetic-note-7', 'locator', 'fixture:wrong'))\\\\n    negative('source_evidence_absent', 'AdmissionEvidence', field('reviewDecisions', 'demo-review-1', 'evidence', []))\\\\n    negative('duplicate_dimension', 'DuplicateDimension', field('contexts', 'debt-context', 'dimensions', [dict(axis='region', member='A')] * 2))\\\\n    negative('money_unit_mismatch', 'ContextMismatch', field('contexts', 'debt-context', 'unit', 'EUR'))\\\\n    negative('wrong_book_currency', 'BookCurrency', field('books', 'Local', 'currency', 'EUR'))\\\\n    negative('assumption_reason_absent', 'MissingAssumptionReason', field('assumptions', 'admission.allFixed', 'rationale', ' '))\\\\n    negative('unearned_default_status', 'UnprovedDefaultReview', field('assumptions', 'admission.allFixed', 'role', 'ReviewedDefault'))\\\\n    negative('assumption_expires_before_horizon', 'AssumptionValidity',\\\\n             lambda d, r: d['assumptions'][0]['valid'].__setitem__('end_exclusive', '2026-07-01'))\\\\n    negative('future_assumption_information', 'FutureAssumption', field('assumptions', 'admission.allFixed', 'information_cutoff', '2026-01-02T00:00:00Z'))\\\\n    negative('conditional_provenance_absent', 'MissingAssumption',\\\\n             lambda d, r: d.__setitem__('assumptions', [a for a in d['assumptions'] if a['id'] != 'admission.allFixed']))\\\\n    negative('stress_provenance_absent', 'MissingAssumption',\\\\n             lambda d, r: d.__setitem__('assumptions', [a for a in d['assumptions'] if a['id'] != 'admission.rateShock']))\\\\n    negative('contract_rate_provenance_absent', 'MissingAssumption',\\\\n             lambda d, r: d.__setitem__('assumptions', [a for a in d['assumptions'] if a['id'] != 'admission.loans']))\\\\n    negative('future_public_evidence', 'FutureEvidence', field('documents', 'synthetic-note-document', 'available', '2026-01-02T00:00:00Z'))\\\\n\\\\n    def future_system(d, r):\\\\n        d['evidenceViews'][0]['system_as_of'] = '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'\\\\n        d['documents'][0]['ingested'] = '2026-01-02T00:00:00Z'\\\\n\\\\n    negative('future_ingestion', 'FutureIngestion', future_system)\\\\n\\\\n    def future_review(d, r):\\\\n        d['evidenceViews'][0]['system_as_of'] = '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'\\\\n        d['reviewDecisions'][0]['date'] = '2026-01-02T00:00:00Z'\\\\n\\\\n    negative('future_system_review', 'FutureReview', future_review)\\\\n    negative('view_omits_source', 'ViewMembership', field('evidenceViews', 'synthetic-2025-exact', 'documents', []))\\\\n    negative('view_omits_acceptance', 'ViewMembership', field('evidenceViews', 'synthetic-2025-exact', 'decisions', []))\\\\n    negative('view_omits_used_observation', 'ViewMembership', field('evidenceViews', 'synthetic-2025-exact', 'observations', []))\\\\n    negative('reviewer_reason_absent', 'MissingReviewReason', field('reviewDecisions', 'demo-review-1', 'reason', ''))\\\\n    negative('alternative_author_absent', 'MissingAlternativeReason', field('alternatives', 'allFixed', 'author', ''))\\\\n    negative('alternative_uses_other_condition', 'AlternativeScope', field('alternatives', 'allFixed', 'constraints', ['condition.floating']))\\\\n    negative('unbalanced_opening', 'UnbalancedState', lambda d, r: d['states'][0]['balances'][0].__setitem__('signed_amount', dict(n='96', d='1')))\\\\n    negative('duplicate_balance', 'DuplicateBalance', lambda d, r: d['states'][0]['balances'].append(deepcopy(d['states'][0]['balances'][0])))\\\\n    negative('omitted_explicit_zero', 'IncompleteState', lambda d, r: d['states'][0]['balances'].pop())\\\\n\\\\n    def cross_book(d, r):\\\\n        book = deepcopy(d['books'][0]); book['id'] = 'OtherBook'; d['books'].append(book)\\\\n        d['accounts'][0]['book'] = 'OtherBook'\\\\n\\\\n    negative('cross_book_balance', 'StateBook', cross_book)\\\\n\\\\n    def balanced_but_wrong_opening(d, r):\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_21\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"assumptions\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"checks\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"scripts/core_semantics.py\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"scripts/check_core_contract.py\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"issues\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"next_actions\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"residuals\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"steps\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The existing validator binds many identifiers and evidence values to the authored debt fixture, and the frontend check compares only one literal. P03 needs a separate, versioned lowering path with explicit source and review inputs, plus tests that change whole programs and reject unsupported semantics.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"verdict\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PLAN\\\\\\\"}\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_22\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,122p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '235,407p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_22\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,122p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '235,407p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# AccDSL Core 0 contract, revision 2\\\\n\\\\nNormative companions: `core-0.lark`, `core-ir.schema.json` and\\\\n`../fixtures/demo-debt-package.json`. The authored expected lowering is\\\\n`../fixtures/core-ir-demo.json`; it is not compiler-generated. The LaTeX chapters teach the semantics;\\\\nthese files settle serialisation and the complete demonstration dependency set.\\\\nNo general compiler or product runtime is asserted to exist.\\\\n\\\\nThe supplemental `core-demo-registry.json` freezes the authored debt example's\\\\n17 exports by kind, location and digest. `scripts/core_semantics.py` implements\\\\nbounded static admission for that profile, including references, source-reading\\\\nbindings, types, dates, evidence selection, assumptions, opening state and\\\\npackage/report bindings. `scripts/check_semantic_preparation.py` exercises\\\\npositive variations and schema-valid corruptions. This checker is intentionally\\\\nlimited to the authored monetary debt model and its known registry; other\\\\npopulated IR sections and unsupported operations are rejected. It is not a\\\\ngeneral package loader, source-to-IR compiler, execution engine or coverage\\\\nproof verifier. Its output explicitly leaves coverage claims unverified.\\\\n\\\\n## Lexical and static meaning\\\\n\\\\nInput is UTF-8 with LF or CRLF accepted. Identifiers are ASCII, case-sensitive;\\\\nall literal words in the grammar and `true/false/or/and/not/per/year` are\\\\nreserved. Strings use JSON escaping, reject unpaired surrogates and are NFC\\\\nnormalised for semantic identity; original bytes remain evidence. No exponent,\\\\nthousands separator, percent literal, implicit multiplication or host-language\\\\nescape is supported. Negative numbers use unary minus; decimals become reduced\\\\nrationals directly. Dates must be valid Gregorian dates (the token shape alone\\\\ndoes not validate them). Currency/name suffixes are resolved before typing.\\\\n\\\\nOperators follow grammar precedence, arithmetic associates left, comparisons\\\\ncannot chain, `and/or` are logical connectives over a joint formula. No\\\\nthree-valued source missingness is coerced to Boolean. `not` may recursively\\\\napply to a Boolean/formula; arithmetic sign applies to a numeric expression.\\\\nNo declaration identifier may repeat in a namespace. Imports expose qualified\\\\nexports; short names must resolve uniquely. Fields must exist on the declared\\\\nrecord, argument counts/types must match, no implicit money or calendar cast.\\\\nRecords reject duplicate keys and unknown fields. Arrays are homogeneous unless\\\\ntheir declared type is an explicit tuple. Cyclic let/reference definitions are\\\\nrejected before solver dispatch; event dependencies are checked separately.\\\\n\\\\nThe schema fixes all IR node fields, forbids extra fields and distinguishes\\\\nnullable optional links from empty collections. Every reference resolves in\\\\nthe frozen package/evidence closure. Schema validation precedes semantic\\\\nvalidation: reference kind, acyclic graphs, type compatibility, context\\\\ncompatibility, numeric canonical form, units, rules and capability admission.\\\\nAn enum value permitted by JSON Schema is not evidence that its requested\\\\noperation is implemented. Schemas and semantic rules are jointly normative.\\\\n\\\\nExpression arities are fixed: `literal` and `ref` have no arguments; `negate`,\\\\n`not` and `field` have one; arithmetic, comparison, `and` and `or` have two.\\\\nA `call` matches its registered signature. `array` has its declared element\\\\ntype and any permitted length; `record` has one argument per distinct\\\\n`field_names` entry, in that order. A literal has exactly one rational or text\\\\npayload consistent with its type; a reference has a target ID; a field has its\\\\nfield name in `text`; a call has a qualified function ID in `target`. Unused\\\\npayload fields are null and unused `field_names` is empty. Arithmetic and\\\\nordering require compatible numeric types/contexts; equality requires matching\\\\ntypes; logical operators require Boolean values or Boolean formulas. Field\\\\nselection and record construction use the registered record type. No schema\\\\nsuccess bypasses these semantic checks.\\\\n\\\\nExternal identifiers such as `builtin:Core0@1`, `DemoCalendar@1`, package\\\\noperations and `fixture:` reading/view/witness IDs resolve through a frozen\\\\nregistry with declared kinds, versions and content digests. The demonstration\\\\npackage describes these exports and its calendar periods. They are not all\\\\nembedded as top-level IR nodes. The frozen demonstration registry and bounded\\\\nsemantic checker validate these specific bindings; general registry resolution\\\\nand compiler validation remain implementation obligations. A missing export is an error,\\\\nnot authority to invent a value or load mutable network content.\\\\n\\\\nSourceSpan locators use `pdf:<1-based-page>:<x0>,<y0>,<x1>,<y1>` with PDF\\\\npoints from the top-left of the rotated visible page, or `html:<element-id>`\\\\nwith a retained node ordinal fallback in the frozen parse. A text-extract\\\\ncharacter range is a derived locator and retains the extractor version; it\\\\ndoes not pretend to be an original page bounding box. Monetary Context has\\\\nnon-null currency and a compatible unit. Posting amount is nonnegative in the\\\\nbook's functional currency; optional original_quantity/original_unit retain\\\\nforeign money or commodities and require a valuation when converted.\\\\nJournal assumptions and accrual_period preserve the measurement's conditions\\\\nseparately from its cash posting date. The schema's nullable fields are always\\\\npresent; null is permitted only under these stated semantic conditions.\\\\n\\\\nA decimal `100 USD` lowers to `literal` with rational `{n:\\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",d:\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"}`,\\\\ntype `Money<USD>` and no hidden scale multiplier. `alpha` lowers to a `ref` to\\\\nthe same symbol ID on every use. `0.05 per year` has type `Rate<annual_simple>`.\\\\nSource references and origin offsets are kept in the evidence binding, outside\\\\nthe semantic expression digest. A program with source observations cannot run\\\\nuntil its evidence registry and accepted review decisions are supplied.\\\\n\\\\nSource symbol-domain intervals are closed; strict bounds use explicit\\\\nconstraints. Choice members resolve within their choice namespace. The\\\\nsurface syntax has no unbounded loops, recursion, dynamic code evaluation or\\\\nhost calls; finite schedules/collections come from typed packages. Report\\\\nfields bind supported mapping expressions and cannot override recognition.\\\\nEvery assumption constraint or conditional model input has an Assumption\\\\nrecord carrying its expression, scope, rationale, origin, evidence, validity\\\\nperiod, information cutoff and role (Baseline, Hypothesis, Convenience or\\\\nReviewedDefault). An authored baseline is not automatically a reviewed\\\\ndefault. Conditional example endpoints are hypotheses, not inferred facts.\\\\nThe debt example also records its assumed initial 5% component rates and 7%\\\\nstress driver as assumptions. The integer contract-slot limit has its own\\\\n`Int` literal; it does not reuse the `Real` literal in the fraction comparison.\\\\n\\\\n## Exact values, contexts and built-ins\\\\n\\\\nRationals use base-10 signed numerator strings and positive denominator strings,\\\\nlowest terms; zero is `0/1`. Money adds only within one currency and compatible\\\\ncontext. Real times money is money; rate times money must also supply a\\\\nYearFraction through `simpleInterest`. Rate alone is not a dimensionless Real.\\\\nNo rate basis is implicitly coerced. The demonstration's accrual rule uses\\\\n`simpleInterest(principal,rate,fraction)` explicitly. Integer counts stay integer.\\\\nDivision by a symbolic value\\\\nrequires nonzero proof and is outside the rational-linear solver fragment.\\\\n\\\\nContext equality compares entity, perimeter version, measurement basis,\\\\ncurrency/unit, instant/period/calendar and dimensions. A sum may discard a\\\\ndimension only through a valid partition mapping. Reference fields and source\\\\nspans may differ without changing financial comparability. Observation\\\\nprecision is a domain, not a tolerance argument. Unknown rounding convention\\\\nis an unresolved reading, not an assumed half-unit interval.\\\\n\\\\ncorrections replace evidence views; likelihoods update probability models;\\\\nhypothetical stresses alone do none of those.\\\\n\\\\nExogenousStress supplies named driver paths without updating historical weights.\\\\nObservationalConditioning supplies observed events, a joint model and positive\\\\nevent probability/likelihood; finite enumeration computes normalised joint\\\\nweights exactly. Zero probability yields UndefinedConditioning, not equal\\\\nweights. Continuous density conditioning requires an explicit conditional\\\\nmodel/regular conditional distribution adapter. StructuralIntervention replaces\\\\nspecified equations in a named acyclic structural model, retaining exogenous\\\\nnoise; absence of that model yields UnsupportedScenario. Risk-neutral pricing\\\\nand real-world simulation measures have different IDs and cannot be mixed\\\\nwithout an explicit justified transformation.\\\\n\\\\nInformationView(date, observer, role, evidence_view, committed_prefix,\\\\nannounced_scenario_inputs, forecast_model) exposes past/current facts and\\\\npermitted forecasts. Future realised innovations and future event outcomes\\\\nare unavailable. A scenario may announce an entire stress path to management\\\\nonly when its visibility is `announced`; otherwise management sees current and\\\\npast driver values. Valuation uses an inner expectation conditional on this\\\\nview, with an independent stream domain from outer realised defaults.\\\\n\\\\nRunResult preserves rows by hypothesis/continuous condition, scenario, path and\\\\ndate. Cells carry Context and Exact/Symbolic/Samples/CertifiedBounds/ExploredRange/\\\\nUnresolved tags. Path failure has an enum: EconomicDefault, Unsupported,\\\\nNumericalFailure, SolverUnknown, Cancelled. Default retains the legal obligations\\\\nand usable state; an unsupported required treatment stops affected descendants.\\\\nUnaffected outputs may survive through the dependency graph. No unweighted\\\\nfamily has a mean. Weighted runs preserve successful, unresolved and default\\\\nmass; missing outcomes block unconditional means/quantiles. Conditional-on-success\\\\nresults require an explicit separate request and show their denominator.\\\\n\\\\nFinite joint measures attach to disjoint economic hypotheses, not alternative\\\\nlabels. Overlapping views cannot be summed; reparameterisations require a\\\\npushforward measure, with Jacobian where densities are used. Priors and\\\\nlikelihoods list information blocks so totals/components do not duplicate\\\\nevidence. Exact finite inference is the reference optional method. Continuous\\\\ninference requires a declared density/parameterisation, numerical validity,\\\\nmultiple-chain/seed and downstream checks; no sampler default is selected here.\\\\n\\\\n## Identity, replay, migration and storage\\\\n\\\\nCanonical bytes are UTF-8 JSON, NFC strings, sorted ASCII keys, separators `,`/`:`\\\\nwithout whitespace, no floats, NaN, duplicate keys or negative zero. All numeric\\\\nvalues are reduced rational records. Arrays preserve order except schema fields\\\\ndeclared sets: dependencies, source IDs and constraint conjunctions sort by ID.\\\\nNo general algebraic equivalence rewriting is implied. Evidence identity hashes\\\\nraw documents, locators, extraction/review versions and context. Model identity\\\\nhashes normalised IR, assumptions, rule/calculator locks and resolution contract,\\\\nexcluding source byte offsets/formatting. Run identity additionally hashes\\\\nevidence view, scenarios, horizon, outputs, numeric/calendars, stream scheme and\\\\nenvironment profile. Every digest is SHA-256 with a domain/version prefix.\\\\n\\\\nEvent ID hashes run-independent economic owner, schedule version, date, phase,\\\\noperation and occurrence ordinal. Idempotency keys pair run ID and event ID;\\\\nsame payload returns the committed result, changed payload yields conflict.\\\\nIndependent events may reorder only if their read/write sets are disjoint or\\\\nthe package proves commutation, including cash/funding constraints. Otherwise\\\\nexplicit dependencies decide order or expose ambiguity. Atomic commit includes\\\\neconomic state, journals, measurements and explanation edges.\\\\n\\\\nThe reference random primitive hashes the canonical tuple (stream-v1, seed,\\\\ncoupling-group, entity, contract/cohort, economic-date, shock-kind, draw-index),\\\\ntakes the first unsigned 64 bits in big-endian order, and maps to the open-unit\\\\nrational (integer+1/2)/2^64. Branch enumeration order is absent. Coupling groups\\\\ndeclare shared uniforms; marginal transforms and correlation construction are\\\\nversioned. This is a deterministic reference primitive, not a claim of validated\\\\nMonte Carlo quality. Research runs must name an assessed counter-based generator\\\\nand preserve the same keying contract. Gaussian/transcendental transforms require\\\\na numerical environment and comparison tolerance; rational examples are exact.\\\\n\\\\nSQLite owns immutable source/readings/review rows and transactional execution\\\\nmetadata; content-addressed files own raw bytes and frozen JSON; DuckDB reads\\\\nversioned Parquet exports for analytics. No independent mutable copy owns truth.\\\\nForeign keys must resolve before commit. Schema migration is original payload +\\\\nnew payload + mapping + before/after IDs. Representation-only migration needs\\\\nconformance equivalence on the supported node set; changed semantics creates a\\\\nnew model. A major version is never relabelled as compatible merely because its\\\\nJSON parses. Restart requires exact locked identities and the last committed\\\\nstate; changed inputs require a new run.\\\\n\\\\n## APIs and adapter boundaries\\\\n\\\\nAll methods accept immutable referenced records and return either the typed\\\\nsuccess record or Diagnostic(code, message, source_ids, entity/period, dependency\\\\npath, retryable, capability). No method modifies its inputs. A request_id makes\\\\nmutating import/review operations idempotent. The normative operations are:\\\\n\\\\n| Operation | Required arguments | Success |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| ingest | bytes/hash, filing_id, availability, extractor_lock, request_id | SourceDocument, source units, proposed readings, coverage obligations |\\\\n| review | reading_ids, action, evidence, reviewer, reason, prior_view, request_id | ReviewDecision, new EvidenceView, invalidated descendants |\\\\n| compile | source/typed-IR, schema_version, package_lock, evidence_view | validated IR, unresolved simulation inputs, diagnostic list |\\\\n| reconstruct | IR, ModelScope, view, solver_lock, budgets | HistoryFamily and cell coverage, witnesses/conflicts/unknowns |\\\\n| simulate | family/conditions, initial_state, scenarios, horizon, InformationPolicy, packages, numeric and stream settings, outputs, budgets | RunResult with committed state/journals and branch manifest |\\\\n| report | committed run/date/period, mapping, view, queries | contextual joint cells and explanation references |\\\\n| bound | formula, query expression, domain, quantisation mode, solver/budget | certified bound/attainment or explicit Unknown/Unbounded |\\\\n| explain | output_id, frozen run_id | typed dependency graph, no latest-source substitution |\\\\n| replay | run_id, checkpoint_id, lock/environment | equal exact outputs or explicit numerical comparison report |\\\\n\\\\nContract methods are schedule(terms,start,end,calendar), observe(terms,date,info),\\\\npayoff(terms,event,state,market), transition(state,event). Behaviour is\\\\ndecide(state,information,policy) -> actions. Measurement is measure(state,event,\\\\ninformation,method) -> value/basis/error/method annotations. Accounting is\\\\nrecognise(event,state,measurement,rule) -> postings+proposed state patch.\\\\nReporting is map(state,journals,period,perimeter,policy) -> contextual cells.\\\\nEvery adapter advertises exact supported operations and input dimensions.\\\\n\\\\nArelle is selected for tagged filing proposals: read QName, contextID, entity,\\\\nperiod, dimensions, unitID, scale/decimals, nil flag and raw locator. Preserve\\\\nduplicate facts; validations are diagnostics, not a chosen truth. Docling\\\\nprovides layout/table proposals with page bounds and conversion status; a table\\\\ncell without a verified header/context is unresolved. Z3 receives named rational\\\\nlinear assertions and finite choices, returns status/witness/core; validate\\\\nwitnesses exactly and preserve unknown reasons. ACTUS receives locked contract\\\\nterms, calendars and dated risk factors; returns events/payoffs, never automatic\\\\naccounting entries. QuantLib receives explicit evaluation date, curves, fixings,\\\\ncalendar/day-count, instrument and measure; returns approximate valuations and\\\\nnumerical metadata, never historical probabilities. These are adapter designs\\\\ngrounded in archived interfaces. Only Z3 is exercised by the reference checks.\\\\n\\\\nBeancount is an optional concrete-journal export/check comparator; unsupported\\\\nsymbolic families stay in AccDSL. Catala is a rule-language comparator. Stan,\\\\nPyro/PyMC are possible later inference adapters, not required core dependencies.\\\\nLicences and inspected source hashes are in tools.json; deployment linking and\\\\nredistribution must be checked for the selected version. Python constructors\\\\nand the text frontend must emit the same IR and receive identical diagnostics.\\\\nUsability and maintenance comparisons remain empirical questions.\\\\n\\\\n### Concrete adapter exchanges\\\\n\\\\nThe following are expected exchanges at the AccDSL boundary, not captured\\\\noutputs of unrun libraries. Upstream wire formats must be translated by a\\\\nversion-pinned adapter before these records are accepted.\\\\n\\\\n* The acquired Apple interim fact `f-112` has QName\\\\n  `us-gaap:CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue`, literal `30,299`, scale 6,\\\\n  decimals -6, USD unit, context `c-17`, CIK `0000320193` and instant\\\\n  `2024-12-28`. Its nominal value becomes rational USD `30299000000/1`;\\\\n  the original display remains `30,299` in millions. The source locator is\\\\n  `html:f-112` in the frozen interim document; dimensions are empty. Accuracy\\\\n  metadata is retained separately from that nominal value. An uncertainty\\\\n  interval additionally needs the declared rounding convention; scale alone\\\\n  does not create an exact economic amount. Reapplying scale to an Arelle\\\\n  value already transformed by inline-XBRL is an error. A nil fact returns\\\\n  missingness, never zero. Two copies with conflicting values remain two\\\\n  readings, not an averaged amount. The source fields are in the Apple\\\\n  manifest; the inspected Arelle interface snapshot hash is recorded in\\\\n  `research/tools.json`. No Arelle integration was run.\\\\n* A normalized borrower interest event has contract `loan-1`, USD principal\\\\n  100, annual simple rate `1/20`, year fraction 1, payment date `2026-12-31`,\\\\n  payoff `-5/1` from the borrower's perspective, no fees and no unpaid prior\\\\n  accrual. A supported accrue-and-pay operation consumes this economic event\\\\n  and proposes debit interest expense 5 / credit cash 5, subject to available\\\\n  cash and book/context checks. A rate-reset event changes the contract's\\\\n  future rate and emits no posting under its declared non-recognition rule.\\\\n  The adapter must state whose payoff sign is returned and cannot infer\\\\n  liability carrying value or an accounting election from a schedule alone.\\\\n  This is an ACTUS-oriented boundary example; an actual ACTUS service request\\\\n  and returned event must be tested against a selected service version later.\\\\n* A normalized valuation request supplies evaluation date `2025-12-31`, one\\\\n  USD cash flow of 110 at `2026-12-31`, a declared one-year fraction, annual\\\\n  effective yield `1/10`, no options/default and discount factor `10/11`.\\\\n  Its exact reference present value is USD 100. A numerical QuantLib result\\\\n  must retain date, curve/engine/calendar locks, units, measurement purpose,\\\\n  status and justified error/tolerance against this reference. It is a\\\\n  valuation of the stated cash flow, not a historical weight or an automatic\\\\n  journal amount. Changing the evaluation date creates a distinct request;\\\\n  stale process-global settings must not contaminate the next branch.\\\\n\\\\nThese examples specify success meanings and the principal rejection cases.\\\\nPinned integration, exceptional-event coverage and empirical cost remain\\\\nseparate acceptance work.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_23\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '420,501p' scripts/core_semantics.py; cat docs/design/fixtures/demo-debt-package.json\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_23\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '420,501p' scripts/core_semantics.py; cat docs/design/fixtures/demo-debt-package.json\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"                    self.assumption(fields[name], c['id'])\\\\n        for s in d['states']:\\\\n            self.ref(s['book'], {'books'}); iso_date(s['date'], s['id'])\\\\n            seen = set(); total = Fraction(0)\\\\n            for b in s['balances']:\\\\n                a = self.ref(b['account'], {'accounts'})\\\\n                require(a['book'] == s['book'], 'StateBook', s['id'], 'Balance belongs to another book')\\\\n                require(a['id'] not in seen, 'DuplicateBalance', s['id'], a['id']); seen.add(a['id'])\\\\n                total += rational(b['signed_amount'], s['id'])\\\\n            require(total == 0, 'UnbalancedState', s['id'], 'Signed opening balances must sum to zero')\\\\n            require(seen == {a['id'] for a in d['accounts'] if a['book'] == s['book']}, 'IncompleteState', s['id'], 'This fixture requires explicit zero balances too')\\\\n            self.refs(s['contracts'], {'contracts'}); self.refs(s['dependencies'])\\\\n            require(not s['measurements'], 'UnsupportedState', s['id'], 'Measurement state not validated in this profile')\\\\n            require(all(self.nodes[c]['book'] == s['book'] for c in s['contracts']),\\\\n                    'StateBook', s['id'], 'Active contract belongs to another book')\\\\n            opening = package_data['registry']['after-2025-close']\\\\n            require(s['book'] == opening['book'] and s['date'] == opening['date'] and\\\\n                    set(s['contracts']) == set(opening['contracts']) and\\\\n                    {b['account']: rational(b['signed_amount'], s['id']) for b in s['balances']} ==\\\\n                    {a: Fraction(v) for a, v in opening['signed_balances'].items()},\\\\n                    'OpeningStateMismatch', s['id'], 'Balanced state differs from the frozen authored opening')\\\\n        for s in d['scenarios']:\\\\n            require(s['kind'] == 'ExogenousStress' and s['probability_model'] is None and s['observed_event'] is None and s['structural_model'] is None and not s['replaced_equations'], 'UnsupportedScenario', s['id'], 'Exogenous debt stress only')\\\\n            require(len(s['drivers']) == 1 and s['drivers'][0]['name'] == 'market_rate', 'ScenarioDrivers', s['id'], 'Expected market_rate')\\\\n            require(self.expression(s['drivers'][0]['expression'])[0] == 'Driver<Rate<annual_simple>>', 'TypeMismatch', s['id'], 'Rate driver required')\\\\n            self.assumption(s['drivers'][0]['expression'], s['id'])\\\\n            low, _ = self.bounds(s['drivers'][0]['expression'])\\\\n            require(low is not None and low >= 0, 'ContractDomain', s['id'], 'DemoDebt rejects a negative reset rate')\\\\n        for scope in d['modelScopes']:\\\\n            self.refs(scope['templates'], {'ContractType'}); self.refs(scope['calendars'], {'Calendar'})\\\\n            require(not scope['choices'] and not scope['obligations'], 'UnsupportedScope', scope['id'], 'Additional structural choices/obligations need a fuller checker')\\\\n            require(len(scope['slot_limits']) == 1, 'SlotLimit', scope['id'], 'One concrete debt slot limit required')\\\\n            for slot in scope['slot_limits']:\\\\n                require(self.expression(slot['expression'])[0] == 'Int', 'SlotLimitType', scope['id'], 'Slot limit is an integer, not an implicit Real cast')\\\\n                low, high = self.bounds(slot['expression'])\\\\n                require(low == high and low is not None and low >= 0 and slot['name'] == 'debt_contracts' and len(d['contracts']) <= low, 'SlotLimit', scope['id'], 'Concrete nonnegative capacity required')\\\\n        for f in d['historyFamilies']:\\\\n            for key, kind in [('scope', 'modelScopes'), ('evidence_view', 'evidenceViews'), ('opening_state', 'states')]:\\\\n                self.ref(f[key], {kind})\\\\n            for key, kind in [('symbols', 'symbols'), ('constraints', 'constraints'), ('alternatives', 'alternatives')]:\\\\n                self.refs(f[key], {kind})\\\\n            self.refs(f['witnesses'], {'Witness'}); self.refs(f['solver_results'], {'ReferenceResult'})\\\\n            view = self.nodes[f['evidence_view']]\\\\n            require(all(o['id'] in view['observations'] for o in d['observations']) and\\\\n                    all(s['admission'] in view['decisions'] for s in d['symbols']),\\\\n                    'ViewMembership', f['id'], 'All evidence used by this bounded family must be selected')\\\\n            require(set(f['symbols']) == {s['id'] for s in d['symbols']} and\\\\n                    set(f['alternatives']) == {a['id'] for a in d['alternatives'] if a['parent'] == f['id']},\\\\n                    'FamilyMembership', f['id'], 'Family omits an authored symbol or conditional alternative')\\\\n            require(not f['choices'], 'UnsupportedChoice', f['id'], 'Finite structural cells not implemented here')\\\\n            require(f['coverage'] != 'ExactWithinScope' or f['unresolved_cells'] == 0, 'FalseCoverage', f['id'], 'Exact coverage cannot contain unknown cells')\\\\n            require(f['coverage'] != 'ExactWithinScope' or (f['completed_cells'] > 0 and f['solver_results']),\\\\n                    'FalseCoverage', f['id'], 'Exact label needs completed cells and result references; this is not proof verification')\\\\n            require(f['feasibility'] != 'Feasible' or bool(f['witnesses']), 'MissingWitness', f['id'], 'Feasible label requires a witness reference')\\\\n        for r in d['reportMappings']:\\\\n            b = self.ref(r['book'], {'books'})\\\\n            require(r['basis'] == b['basis'], 'PackageBasis', r['id'], 'Report and book bases differ')\\\\n            self.ref(r['closing_policy'], {'Operation'}); self.ref(r['cash_flow_policy'], {'CashFlowPolicy'})\\\\n            self.refs(r['required_operations'], {'Operation'})\\\\n            require(r['closing_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/close' and r['cash_flow_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/interest_operating'\\\\n                    and r['required_operations'] == ['DemoDebt@1/accrue_and_pay'], 'ReportPolicy', r['id'],\\\\n                    'Wrong policy binding for the frozen report template')\\\\n            require(len(r['rows']) == 1 and r['rows'][0]['name'] == 'package_mapping', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'One frozen template binding required')\\\\n            for row in r['rows']:\\\\n                require(self.expression(row['expression'])[0] == 'SourceRef', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'This profile binds a frozen report template')\\\\n                e = self.nodes[row['expression']]\\\\n                require(e['op'] == 'literal' and e['text'] == 'DemoDebt.statements.v1', 'ReportMappingType', r['id'], 'Expected the statement mapping export')\\\\n        for m in d['models']:\\\\n            self.refs(m['declarations']); self.refs(m['package_lock'], {'packages'}); self.ref(m['scope'], {'modelScopes'})\\\\n            require(m['language_version'] == 'Core0.1', 'UnsupportedLanguage', m['id'], 'Core0.1 only')\\\\n            required = {r['id'] for section in ['entities', 'books', 'accounts', 'observations', 'symbols',\\\\n                        'contracts', 'alternatives', 'scenarios', 'reportMappings', 'states'] for r in d[section]}\\\\n            require(required <= set(m['declarations']) and set(m['package_lock']) == {p['id'] for p in d['packages']},\\\\n                    'ModelMembership', m['id'], 'Model omits an authored declaration or package lock')\\\\n        return {'status': 'passed', 'profile': 'authored-debt-example',\\\\n                'internal_records': len(self.nodes), 'external_exports': len(self.external),\\\\n                'coverage_claims_verified': False,\\\\n                'limits': 'Bounded static admission only; no general compiler, runtime, accounting certification or proof of historical coverage.'}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef validate(document, registry, schema, root):\\\\n    return Validator(document, registry, schema, root).validate()\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DemoDebt@1\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"illustrative executable-method specification; no standard compliance\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"registry\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"synthetic-note-7\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"document\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"synthetic disclosure NS.debt variant Acme\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"locator\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"debt and interest paragraph\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"literal\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Debt 100; interest 5; fixed/floating split not disclosed\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"entity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Acme\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"perimeter\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Acme-only\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"basis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DemoDebt@1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"concept\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"debt_principal\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"currency\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"USD\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"instant\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2025-12-31\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"precision\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Exact\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"amount\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"n\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"d\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"\\\\n      },\\\\n      \\\\\\\"accepted_reading\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"demo-review-1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    \\\\\\\"after-2025-close\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"book\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Local\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"date\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2025-12-31\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"signed_balances\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Cash\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"95\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Debt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"-100\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Retained\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"InterestExpense\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\"\\\\n      },\\\\n      \\\\\\\"contracts\\\\\\\": [\\\\n        \\\\\\\"loans\\\\\\\"\\\\n      ],\\\\n      \\\\\\\"unpaid_interest\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    \\\\\\\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"balance_sheet\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"cash\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Cash\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"debt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"-Debt\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"equity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"-Retained-current_temporary_total\\\\\\\"\\\\n      },\\\\n      \\\\\\\"income\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"interest expense movements excluding closing\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"comprehensive_income\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"profit; OCI zero\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"cash_flow\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"interest cash settlement operating\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"equity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"opening equity + profit; no dividends\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"closing\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"debit Retained / credit InterestExpense for expense balance; omit current profit from equity after closing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"symbol_admission\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"alpha\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"HistoricalFact\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"domain\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"[0,1]\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"synthetic-note-7\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Composition undisclosed\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"probability\\\\\\\": null\\\\n    }\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"currency\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"USD\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"scale\\\\\\\": 2,\\\\n      \\\\\\\"posting_rounding\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"half_even\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"DebtMix\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"fields\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"principal\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Money<book.currency>, >=0\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"fixed_fraction\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Real [0,1]\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"fixed_rate\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Rate<annual_simple> >=0\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"initial_floating_rate\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Rate<annual_simple> >=0\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    \\\\\\\"additional_terms\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"maturity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2027-12-31\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"fees\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"currency\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"USD\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"pay_date\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-12-31\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"accrual_period\\\\\\\": [\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2026-01-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2027-01-01\\\\\\\"\\\\n      ],\\\\n      \\\\\\\"year_fraction\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"default_rule\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"halt settlement with unpaid obligation; no hidden credit facility\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    \\\\\\\"state\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"principal\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"fixed_principal\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"floating_principal\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"current_floating_rate\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"unpaid_interest\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"initialization\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"F=alpha*principal; V=(1-alpha)*principal; current_floating_rate=initial_floating_rate; unpaid_interest=0; status=performing\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"operations\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"reset\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"market\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"precondition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"date=2026-01-01; driver available\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"payload\\\\\\\": [\\\\n          \\\\\\\"market_rate\\\\\\\"\\\\n        ],\\\\n        \\\\\\\"effect\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"current_floating_rate=market_rate\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"postings\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none; explicit non-recognition operation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      },\\\\n      {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"accrue_and_pay\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"settlement\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"precondition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"principal>=0 and cash>=rounded_interest\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"payload\\\\\\\": [\\\\n          \\\\\\\"F\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"V\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"fixed_rate\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"current_floating_rate\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"year_fraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n        ],\\\\n        \\\\\\\"amount\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"roundMoney((F*fixed_rate+V*current_floating_rate)*year_fraction,2,half_even)\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"postings\\\\\\\": [\\\\n          \\\\\\\"Dr InterestExpense amount\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"Cr Cash amount\\\\\\\"\\\\n        ],\\\\n        \\\\\\\"effect\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"interest obligation accrued and settled atomically\\\\\\\"\\\\n      },\\\\n      {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"close\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"closing\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"precondition\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"all required period operations committed\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"payload\\\\\\\": [\\\\n          \\\\\\\"InterestExpense balance\\\\\\\"\\\\n        ],\\\\n        \\\\\\\"postings\\\\\\\": [\\\\n          \\\\\\\"Dr Retained expense\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"Cr InterestExpense expense\\\\\\\"\\\\n        ],\\\\n        \\\\\\\"effect\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"temporary account zero\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    ]\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"request\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"BorrowingExample@1\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"evidence_view\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"synthetic-2025-exact\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"initial_state\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"after-2025-close\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"horizon\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"2026-01-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"2027-01-01\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"conditions\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"allFixed\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"allFloating\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"scenarios\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"rateShock\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"mode\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"conditional\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"weight_model\\\\\\\": null,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"reports\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"balance_sheet\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"income\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"comprehensive_income\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"cash_flow\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"equity\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"journals\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ]\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"expected\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"allFixed\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"interest\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"cash\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"90\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"debt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"profit\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"-5\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"equity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"-10\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    \\\\\\\"allFloating\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"interest\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"7\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"cash\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"88\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"debt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"profit\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"-7\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"equity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"-12\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    \\\\\\\"parent\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"interest\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"7-2*alpha\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"bounds\\\\\\\": [\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"7\\\\\\\"\\\\n      ],\\\\n      \\\\\\\"measure\\\\\\\": null\\\\n    }\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_24\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '73,98p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '60,79p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '119,138p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '1,45p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; sed -n '95,145p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; cat data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/result-review.json data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/result-review.json\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_24\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '73,98p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '60,79p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '119,138p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '1,45p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; sed -n '95,145p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md; cat data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/result-review.json data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/result-review.json\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"### G2. The normative language and IR contracts remain incomplete\\\\n\\\\nEvidence: [language scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:6),\\\\n[core records](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:84),\\\\nand [plugin interfaces](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/09-implementation.tex:117).\\\\n\\\\nThe grammar covers declaration forms and Appendix A supplies selected record\\\\nsketches. There is no complete serialised expression/domain model, model-scope\\\\nrecord, contract/economic-state schema, narrative-assertion schema, probability\\\\nmodel, run configuration or payload definition for every result variant.\\\\nMethods such as schedule, transition and measure are named without complete\\\\nargument/result types. The representation names semantic hashes, capabilities\\\\nand extension points without specifying canonical encoding, their full\\\\nvalidation rules or required built-in function semantics.\\\\n\\\\nThe running program relies on DemoDebt, DebtMix, an external evidence registry,\\\\nan opening state and reporting templates that are not fully defined in the\\\\ndocument. It therefore cannot itself serve as a complete language conformance\\\\nfixture.\\\\n\\\\nRequired repair: publish the complete Core 0 schema and reference package,\\\\nprecise typing/context rules and function contracts, serialisation rules and\\\\nmatched source-to-IR-to-result fixtures. Implementers need reproducible outcomes\\\\nfor valid and invalid programs, not just agreement on names of operations.\\\\n\\\\n### G3. Ordinary disclosure uncertainty can leave the promised solver fragment\\\\n### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\\\\n\\\\nRequirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\\\\nEvidence: [concept relationships](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:54)\\\\nand [contextual aggregation](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:69).\\\\n\\\\nEquivalent, component, broader, reclassified and measurement-transformed\\\\nconcepts are named, and partitions are required. Their records, applicability\\\\nconditions and allowed compositions are not fully defined. There is no worked\\\\ncase showing company extensions changing over time, gross/net distinctions,\\\\nor two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\\\\n\\\\nRequired evidence: a mapping registry and application rules, with cases where\\\\nsimilar labels mean different measurements and different labels mean the same\\\\nquantity. Define what proves a partition disjoint/exhaustive, how unallocated\\\\nresiduals are represented and how perimeter/context changes affect mappings.\\\\nThe representation need not impose one universal chart of accounts, but it\\\\nmust specify how comparability is established or left unresolved.\\\\n\\\\n### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\\\\n### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\\\\n\\\\nRequirements: MC04, MC08, MC10, MC12, MC24. Refines G1, G2 and G6.\\\\nEvidence: [interpretation distinction](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:67)\\\\nand [alternative records](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:183).\\\\n\\\\nAn unknown fixed-rate share, two readings of a note, a permitted accounting\\\\nelection, a measurement estimate and a future management decision are different\\\\nuncertainties. The text recognises this, but generic symbols/choices and\\\\nassumption provenance do not fully specify how each kind is validated,\\\\nupdated or propagated. An unsupported treatment must not be accepted as an\\\\nequally legitimate interpretation merely because it produces balanced entries.\\\\n\\\\nRequired evidence: define these distinctions in the model and review contracts,\\\\nincluding links between dependent uncertainties. Show an admissible alternative,\\\\nan evidence-refuted alternative and an unsupported accounting treatment.\\\\nPreserve a possibly erroneous source assertion as evidence without silently\\\\nendorsing its treatment. This requires no new fraud-detection product.\\\\n\\\\n### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\\\\n# Active checkpoint\\\\n\\\\nUpdated: 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong), after multi-year source-corpus\\\\nacceptance following the expanded-audit repair. The user directed us to do all\\\\nfeasible internal work before costly professional review. MC35 preserves that work order.\\\\nThe wider mission remains active; human review is not the next automatic step.\\\\n\\\\n## Accepted source corpus and next execution\\\\n\\\\nThe user's corpus-first work unit is complete at the source-acquisition layer:\\\\n**192 of 192 target reports, 2018–2025, across nine issuers and three evidenced\\\\naccounting families. All nine have eight consecutive complete years.**\\\\n`target-panel-v2.json` is active and is now the collector's explicit default.\\\\nHenkel replaces Unilever and Munich Re replaces Allianz under the reviewed\\\\nsource-access repair; frozen v1 coverage and all original files remain under\\\\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/snapshots/`.\\\\n\\\\nResume from the [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\\\\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/index.html`, `coverage.json` and\\\\n`integrity-manifest.json`. QA 6 revalidated all 244 retained original versions;\\\\nthe independent hash/provenance/grid/PDF checks pass, and 20 regression tests\\\\npass. The old 12-, 157- and 159-report counts are historical. There are 738\\\\nattempt/revalidation records, not 738 benchmark observations.\\\\n\\\\nThe collector checkpoints each attempt and supports `--revalidate-retained`,\\\\n`--resolved-only`, sequential `--index-plan` capture and bounded host failures.\\\\nOfficial HSBC and Midea archives, SAIC year pages, Ping An's published report\\\\nfeed, SEC submissions and issuer-hosted US filing feeds have been resolved.\\\\nDirect SEC archive downloads returned 403; issuer-hosted copies are used with\\\\nthe regulator identity and filing dates retained. Run one acquisition writer\\\\nat a time. The optional `--http-client curl` bounds total request time;\\\\n`--source-host` can select a resolved alternate without retrying known failures.\\\\nPing An's last ASBE slot was filled by an A-share report attachment on a public\\\\nmirror; the distinct IFRS copy remains excluded from that slot. Do not reset\\\\nthe ledger, initialise Git or promote source checks into accounting evidence.\\\\n\\\\nThe next internal work is task-specific literal/context/span annotation and\\\\nCore 0 semantic/compiler implementation using the preserved source set and\\\\nexisting fixtures. `benchmark-protocol-v1.json` and\\\\n`annotation-record.schema.json` define the proposed tasks and exchange format;\\\\nissuer-family roles are provisional, with no model score or gold labels.\\\\nResolve incorporated documents, revisions and publication timing before\\\\nhistorical forecasting. Publication dates are unverified for 136 of 192\\\\naccepted reports; 56 have filing-date metadata. No paid review is triggered.\\\\n\\\\n(5 positive, 71 schema-valid negative, 2 JSON-boundary); the new accounting\\\\ndossiers pass 17 exact/journal checks. These are bounded author evidence. The revised PDF has no serious TeX\\\\nwarnings and received contact-sheet plus selected full-page inspection.\\\\nThe verifier requires an author-review file and matching current-PDF render\\\\nmanifest and tracks the external grammar input. The library contains 32\\\\nverified paper PDFs. There are 179 individual title/metadata decisions across\\\\n194 occurrences and 72 forward queries; missing decisions stop generation.\\\\n\\\\nFixtures, grammar, schema and contracts are in `docs/design/fixtures` and\\\\n`docs/design/spec`. The complete demo IR is author-entered, not generated by a\\\\ncompiler. The new `core_semantics.py` validates the authored monetary debt\\\\nprofile and its 17 frozen exports; unsupported sections/operations are rejected.\\\\nIt does not prove family coverage or execute a general model. Checks evaluate\\\\nselected IR expressions and reference financial operations; they do not certify\\\\na production engine.\\\\n\\\\nSelected rule support comes from official AASB texts incorporating IAS 2,\\\\nIAS 32 and IFRS 17. Mack's chain-ladder technical method, proofs and aggregate\\\\nerror discussion were inspected. Sources and limits are recorded in\\\\n`docs/design/research/standards-support.json` and\\\\n`docs/design/cases/apple/manifest.json`.\\\\n\\\\n## Remaining work and next justified steps\\\\n\\\\n1. Extend the checked debt-profile registry/reference/type validation and implement source-to-IR lowering\\\\n   against the positive/negative cases. Schema parsing is not complete compiler\\\\n   conformance. Preserve assumptions, context, joint symbols and branch failures.\\\\n2. Build the bounded Northstar path and transactional replay; execute small\\\\n   version-pinned Arelle/ACTUS/QuantLib/Docling/ledger exchanges as selected.\\\\n   Only Z3 has been exercised in this repair.\\\\n3. Expand and independently annotate the real corpus. Apple's 121 annual pages\\\\n   and 23 total notes are inventoried, but full semantics and incorporated\\\\n   external documents are incomplete.\\\\n4. Obtain full ASC authority and official/current ASBE verification. Extend\\\\n   bank credit/prudential, insurance measurement/transition and richer hybrids\\\\n   with primary support and complete actual fact patterns. Existing bank capital\\\\n   assumptions are illustrative, not Basel rules. Dossiers retain source-version\\\\n   limits and calculations; source acquisition remains internal work.\\\\n5. After relevant internal tasks are complete, identify any consequential\\\\n   residual questions for independent implementability/accounting review. Use\\\\n   the unsent brief with narrow questions and a user-approved scope/cost only\\\\n   if later commissioned. Ordinary comprehension feedback is separate and need\\\\n   not come from a professional firm. Acceptance stays provisional while\\\\n   internal work continues. Forecast calibration, stochastic inference and\\\\n   performance comparisons need separate evidence plans; none was run here.\\\\n\\\\nG1–G18 are mapped in the result note; the wider audit is not fully closed.\\\\nA bounded complete synthetic case must not narrow the mission. No deployment,\\\\nexternal messaging, Git initialization or production claims were part of this\\\\nwork. No subagents were used.\\\\n\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"verdict\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"PASS\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"review_kind\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deterministic_fixed_operation_output_validation\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"checks_sha256\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"18c55c02e5e8dc27b49fc1e8432e2be4054b09a2a869b5014d2b278f7632310d\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Internal fixed-operation acceptance only; no independent model/accounting verdict.\\\\\\\"\\\\n}\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"verdict\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"PASS\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"review_kind\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"deterministic_fixed_operation_output_validation\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"checks_sha256\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"af0cb563dcaa33f3a024051d403069b805f2460130898c89d41b80581a21724e\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Internal fixed-operation acceptance only; no independent model/accounting verdict.\\\\\\\"\\\\n}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_25\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"reasoning\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"**Determining environment setup**\\\\n\\\\nI need to figure out the runtime working directory and ensure that permissions are set for read-only access without needing to install any packages. It’s important for me to obtain the exact plan for the environment version using Python introspection to check the existing environment or virtual environment. I want to ensure everything is correctly set up without any unnecessary installations. Let's gather all the necessary information to move forward!\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_26\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,110p' scripts/check_core_contract.py; sed -n '1,120p' data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/baseline.json; sed -n '1,100p' data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/source-work-register.json; rg -n 'P03|core-0|release|semantic|schema|fixture|p03' scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json data/financial-report-benchmark/integrity-manifest.json; rg --files tests\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_26\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,110p' scripts/check_core_contract.py; sed -n '1,120p' data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/baseline.json; sed -n '1,100p' data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/source-work-register.json; rg -n 'P03|core-0|release|semantic|schema|fixture|p03' scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json data/financial-report-benchmark/integrity-manifest.json; rg --files tests\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Bounded structural/semantic design oracles, with explicit coverage limits.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\\\nfrom fractions import Fraction as Q\\\\nimport hashlib\\\\nimport json\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nimport unicodedata\\\\nimport jsonschema\\\\nfrom lark import Lark, UnexpectedInput\\\\n\\\\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];D=ROOT/'docs/design';checks=[]\\\\ndef ck(name,ok,detail):\\\\n    checks.append(dict(name=name,passed=bool(ok),detail=detail))\\\\n    if not ok:raise AssertionError(name)\\\\ndef canonical(value):\\\\n    def normal(x):\\\\n        if isinstance(x,float):raise ValueError('FloatForbidden')\\\\n        if isinstance(x,str):return unicodedata.normalize('NFC',x)\\\\n        if isinstance(x,list):return [normal(i) for i in x]\\\\n        if isinstance(x,dict):return {k:normal(v) for k,v in sorted(x.items())}\\\\n        return x\\\\n    return json.dumps(normal(value),sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':'),ensure_ascii=False).encode()\\\\ndef digest(domain,value):return hashlib.sha256(domain.encode()+b'\\\\\\\\0'+canonical(value)).hexdigest()\\\\ndef uniform(seed,group,entity,contract,date,kind,index):\\\\n    key=['stream-v1',seed,group,entity,contract,date,kind,index]\\\\n    v=int.from_bytes(hashlib.sha256(canonical(key)).digest()[:8],'big')\\\\n    return Q(2*v+1,2**65)\\\\ndef main():\\\\n    source=(D/'fixtures/borrowing.acc').read_text();grammar=(D/'spec/core-0.lark').read_text()\\\\n    parser=Lark(grammar,parser='lalr',maybe_placeholders=False)\\\\n    a=parser.parse(source);b=parser.parse('// comment\\\\\\\\n'+source.replace(';',';\\\\\\\\n'))\\\\n    ck('grammar_format_invariance',a==b,'Same syntax tree after comments/whitespace')\\\\n    ck('declaration_closure',len(list(a.find_data('opening')))==1 and len(list(a.find_data('account')))==4,'Complete source has opening state and retained earnings account')\\\\n    try:parser.parse(source+'let bad = 1 + ;');raise AssertionError('Expected parse failure')\\\\n    except UnexpectedInput:ck('malformed_expression_rejected',True,'Incomplete binary expression rejected')\\\\n    package=json.loads((D/'fixtures/demo-debt-package.json').read_text())\\\\n    ck('opening_dependency_resolved',sum(Q(x) for x in package['registry']['after-2025-close']['signed_balances'].values())==0,'Cash 95, credit debt 100, debit retained loss 5')\\\\n    schema=json.loads((D/'spec/core-ir.schema.json').read_text());jsonschema.Draft202012Validator.check_schema(schema)\\\\n    fixture=json.loads((D/'fixtures/core-ir-structure.json').read_text());jsonschema.validate(fixture,schema)\\\\n    ck('closed_schema_fixture',True,'Structural validation only; full semantic compiler unimplemented')\\\\n    demo=json.loads((D/'fixtures/core-ir-demo.json').read_text());jsonschema.validate(demo,schema)\\\\n    ck('full_demo_ir_schema',True,'Author-entered expected lowering with source, context, review, state, contracts, alternatives, scenario and reporting package')\\\\n    expressions={e['id']:e for e in demo['expressions']};observations={o['id']:o for o in demo['observations']}\\\\n    def eval_expr(id,alpha):\\\\n        e=expressions[id]\\\\n        if e['op']=='literal':\\\\n            return Q(int(e['rational']['n']),int(e['rational']['d'])) if e['rational'] else e['text']\\\\n        if e['op']=='ref':return alpha if e['target']=='alpha' else observations[e['target']]\\\\n        if e['op']=='call':\\\\n            v=eval_expr(e['args'][0],alpha)\\\\n            if e['target']=='builtin:constant@1':return v\\\\n            if e['target']=='builtin:value@1':\\\\n                q=v['domain']['lower'];return Q(int(q['n']),int(q['d']))\\\\n        if e['op']=='eq':return eval_expr(e['args'][0],alpha)==eval_expr(e['args'][1],alpha)\\\\n        raise ValueError('UnsupportedReferenceExpression')\\\\n    fields={f['name']:f['expression'] for f in demo['contracts'][0]['fields']}\\\\n    for name,alpha,condition in [('allFixed',Q(1),'is.fixed'),('allFloating',Q(0),'is.floating')]:\\\\n        principal=eval_expr(fields['principal'],alpha);fixed=eval_expr(fields['fixed_rate'],alpha)\\\\n        floating=eval_expr(demo['scenarios'][0]['drivers'][0]['expression'],alpha)\\\\n        interest=principal*(alpha*fixed+(1-alpha)*floating)\\\\n        opening={x['account']:Q(int(x['signed_amount']['n']),int(x['signed_amount']['d'])) for x in demo['states'][0]['balances']}\\\\n        expected=package['expected'][name]\\\\n        ck('demo_ir_to_result_'+name,eval_expr(condition,alpha) and interest==Q(expected['interest']) and opening['Cash']-interest==Q(expected['cash']) and -opening['Retained']-interest==Q(expected['equity']),\\\\n           'Reference evaluator consumes authored IR; general source-to-IR compiler still pending')\\\\n    bad=deepcopy(fixture);bad['expressions'][0]['hidden_assumption']=True\\\\n    try:jsonschema.validate(bad,schema);raise AssertionError('Expected unknown field error')\\\\n    except jsonschema.ValidationError:ck('unknown_ir_field_rejected',True,'Closed record detects undeclared data')\\\\n    # A literal parsed from the real source agrees with a typed-library value.\\\\n    obs=list(a.find_data('observation'))[0];number=list(obs.find_data('number'))[0]\\\\n    parsed=Q(str(number.children[0]));typed=Q(100)\\\\n    ck('literal_frontend_equivalence',parsed==typed and fixture['expressions'][0]['rational']==dict(n=str(typed.numerator),d=str(typed.denominator)),'Limited literal lowering, not whole-program compiler conformance')\\\\n    x={'model':'M','amount':{'n':'5','d':'1'},'label':'caf\\\\\\\\u00e9'}\\\\n    y={'label':'cafe\\\\\\\\u0301','amount':{'d':'1','n':'5'},'model':'M'}\\\\n    ck('canonical_key_unicode',digest('model-v1',x)==digest('model-v1',y),'Dictionary order and Unicode composition do not change semantic digest')\\\\n    changed=deepcopy(x);changed['amount']['n']='7'\\\\n    ck('changed_model_identity',digest('model-v1',x)!=digest('model-v1',changed),'Rate/value change creates a different model')\\\\n    ck('identity_domains_separate',digest('evidence-v1',x)!=digest('model-v1',x),'Evidence and model hashes are not interchangeable')\\\\n    try:canonical({'amount':0.1});raise AssertionError('Expected float rejection')\\\\n    except ValueError:ck('canonical_float_rejected',True,'No accidental binary float identity')\\\\n    branches=['fixed','floating'];draws={b:uniform('seed1','shared','Acme','debt1','2026-01-01','rate',0) for b in branches}\\\\n    reversed_draws={b:uniform('seed1','shared','Acme','debt1','2026-01-01','rate',0) for b in reversed(branches)}\\\\n    ck('stable_branch_streams',draws==reversed_draws and draws['fixed']==draws['floating'],'Ordering absent; common coupling explicit')\\\\n    ck('measurement_outer_stream_separation',uniform('seed1','shared','Acme','loan1','2026-01-01','inner-default',0)!=uniform('seed1','shared','Acme','loan1','2026-01-01','outer-default',0),'No reuse of realised outer default in allowance draw')\\\\n    ck('uniform_open_interval',all(0<u<1 for u in draws.values()),'Reference primitive produces neither endpoint')\\\\n    # Dependency closure after a review correction.\\\\n    graph={'reading':['mapping'],'mapping':['constraint'],'constraint':['family'],'family':['run'],'run':['report'],'unrelated':[]}\\\\n    pending=['reading'];affected=set()\\\\n    while pending:\\\\n        k=pending.pop()\\\\n        for child in graph.get(k,[]):\\\\n            if child not in affected:affected.add(child);pending.append(child)\\\\n    ck('review_invalidation',affected=={'mapping','constraint','family','run','report'},'Transitive descendants stale; unrelated state reusable')\\\\n    # Information capability uses role/date rather than exposing the entire path.\\\\n    records=[dict(id='current-pd',date='2026-01-01',kind='forecast'),dict(id='future-default',date='2026-06-01',kind='realised')]\\\\n    visible=[r['id'] for r in records if r['date']<='2026-01-01']\\\\n    ck('no_future_realisation',visible==['current-pd'],'Measurement can use current PD, not future realised default')\\\\n    partitions={'geography':{'domestic':Q(180),'overseas':Q(80)},'channel':{'wholesale':Q(200),'retail':Q(60)}}\\\\n    ck('overlapping_axes',all(sum(v.values())==260 for v in partitions.values()) and sum(sum(v.values()) for v in partitions.values())==520,'Adding both axes double-counts the same population; require one partition')\\\\n    # Genuine joint counterexample: extrema of cash/equity cannot be selected independently.\\\\n    import z3\\\\n    alpha=z3.Real('alpha_joint');s=z3.Solver();s.add(alpha>=0,alpha<=1,z3.RealVal('93.6')+z3.RealVal('1.6')*alpha==z3.RealVal('93.6'),z3.RealVal('146.6')+z3.RealVal('1.6')*alpha==z3.RealVal('148.2'))\\\\n    ck('incompatible_marginal_extrema',s.check()==z3.unsat,'Lowest cash and highest equity do not describe one history')\\\\n    apple=json.loads((D/'cases/apple/manifest.json').read_text())\\\\n    ck('real_source_note_inventory',len([n for n in apple['notes'] if n['source']=='annual'])==13 and len([n for n in apple['notes'] if n['source']=='interim'])==10,'Note headings reconciled to annual/interim indices')\\\\n    for row in apple['statements']:\\\\n        ck('apple_balance_'+row['date'],Q(row['assets'])==Q(row['liabilities'])+Q(row['equity']),row['source'])\\\\n    d=apple['debt_measurements'];ck('apple_debt_measurements',Q(d['principal'])+Q(d['discount_cost_adjustment'])+Q(d['hedge_carrying_adjustment'])==Q(d['carrying']),'Note 9 principal differs from carrying and fair value')\\\\n    scenario=apple['marginal_stress'];i=Q(scenario['exposure_assumption'])*Q(scenario['rate_increment'])*Q(scenario['year_fraction']);last=apple['statements'][-1];expected=scenario['expected']\\\\n    ck('apple_marginal_forecast',i==Q(expected['interest']) and Q(last['cash'])-i==Q(expected['cash']) and Q(last['assets'])-i==Q(expected['assets']) and Q(last['equity'])-i==Q(expected['equity']),'Conditional extra interest 72.875 million, not estimated actual sensitivity')\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"verified_reports\\\\\\\": 192,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"reference_suites\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"script\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"check_design_examples.py\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"checks\\\\\\\": 12,\\\\n      \\\\\\\"report\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/example-checks.json\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Manuscript illustration arithmetic passes; no product implementation, accounting compliance or forecast validity is established.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"script\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"check_repair_conformance.py\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"checks\\\\\\\": 49,\\\\n      \\\\\\\"report\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/repair-conformance.json\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Design reference arithmetic, rational-linear solver, temporal selection and event oracle; no product implementation or accounting certification\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"script\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"check_core_contract.py\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"checks\\\\\\\": 31,\\\\n      \\\\\\\"report\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/core-contract-checks.json\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Reference grammar, selected schema/literal semantics, identities, information/dependency/financial counterexamples; no full compiler or adapter integration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"script\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"check_semantic_preparation.py\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"checks\\\\\\\": 78,\\\\n      \\\\\\\"report\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/semantic-preparation-checks.json\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Authored debt profile only; structural admission is checked separately before every semantic rejection.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"script\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"check_accounting_dossiers.py\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"checks\\\\\\\": 17,\\\\n      \\\\\\\"report\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P00/accounting-dossier-checks.json\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Exact arithmetic and signed journal reconciliation under stated dossier assumptions; no source applicability or professional assurance verdict.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"corpus_regression_tests\\\\\\\": 20,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"source_acceptance_only\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"mission_complete\\\\\\\": false,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"residuals\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    \\\\\\\"All G1–G18 retain work; bounded reference checks do not establish accounting or forecast validity.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"schema_version\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"accdsl.source_work_register.v1\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"passed\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"record_count\\\\\\\": 192,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"input_hashes\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"data/financial-report-benchmark/coverage.json\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"5fcc211923b82c96fa2a8a768a6eb98df007e922fe12100df070d2f8e925e182\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"data/financial-report-benchmark/source-evidence.json\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"d5bc57c93903805e92411cd693ab662e171396886ad04becb053aba20888d7b3\\\\\\\"\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"records\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"document_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"apple-2018-annual\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"issuer_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"apple\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"period_year